helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148664				0	uz	\<variable id=\"chart_main\"\>\<link href=\"text/schart/main0000.xhp\" name=\"Charts in $[officename]\"\>Using Charts in %PRODUCTNAME\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154685	2			0	uz	\<variable id=\"chart\"\>$[officename] lets you present data graphically in a chart, so that you can visually compare data series and view trends in the data. You can insert charts into spreadsheets, text documents, drawings, and presentations. \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153143				0	uz	Chart Data				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	par_id5181432				0	uz	Charts can be based on the following data:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	par_id7787102				0	uz	Spreadsheet values from Calc cell ranges				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	par_id7929929				0	uz	Cell values from a Writer table				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	par_id4727011				0	uz	Values that you enter in the Chart Data Table dialog (you can create these charts in Writer, Draw, or Impress, and you can copy and paste them also to Calc)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	hd_id5345011				0	uz	To insert a chart				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	hd_id5631580				0	uz	To edit a chart				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	par_id7911008				0	uz	Click a chart to edit the chart object properties:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	par_id9844660				0	uz	size and position on the current page				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	par_id8039796				0	uz	alignment, text wrap, outer borders, and more				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	par_id7986693				0	uz	Double-click a chart to enter the chart edit mode:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	par_id2350840				0	uz	chart data values (for charts with own data)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	par_id3776055				0	uz	chart type, axes, titles, walls, grid, and more				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	par_id8442335				0	uz	Double-click a chart element in chart edit mode:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	par_id4194769				0	uz	double-click an axis to edit the scale, type, color, and more				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	par_id6574907				0	uz	with a data series selected, double-click a single data point to edit the properties of this data point (for example, a single bar in a bar chart)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	par_id7528916				0	uz	double-click any other chart element, or click the element and open the Format menu, to edit the properties				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	par_id8420667				0	uz	Click outside the chart to leave the current edit mode.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0000.xhp	0	help	par_id4923856				0	uz	To print a chart in high quality, you can export the chart to a PDF file and print that file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0503.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	$[officename] Chart Features				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0503.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150543				0	uz	\<link href=\"text/schart/main0503.xhp\" name=\"$[officename] Chart Features\"\>$[officename] Chart Features\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0503.xhp	0	help	par_id3150868				0	uz	Charts allow you to present data so that it is easy to visualize.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0503.xhp	0	help	par_id3146974				0	uz	You can create a chart from source data in a Calc spreadsheet or a Writer table. When the chart is embedded in the same document as the data, it stays linked to the data, so that the chart automatically updates when you change the source data.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0503.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153143				0	uz	Chart Types				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0503.xhp	0	help	par_id3151112				0	uz	Choose from a variety of 3D charts and 2D charts, such as bar charts, line charts, stock charts. You can change chart types with a few clicks of the mouse.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0503.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149665				0	uz	Individual Formatting				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\main0503.xhp	0	help	par_id3156441				0	uz	You can customize individual chart elements, such as axes, data labels, and legends, by right-clicking them in the chart, or with toolbar icons and menu commands.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
