helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3149684				0	uz	Inserts a \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000005.xhp#dde\" name=\"DDE\"\>DDE\</link\> link into the document, that you can update as often as you want through the assigned name.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3159196				0	uz	Formulani qoʻyish				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3151322				0	uz	Formula natijasi yoki oʻrnatilgan raqamni oʻrnatadi.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3149494				0	uz	Input field				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3154829				0	uz	Oʻzgaruvchi uchun yangi qiymat yoki foydalanuvchi maydonini kiritadi.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3149098				0	uz	The value of a variable in an Input field is only valid from where the field is inserted and onwards. To change the value of the variable later in the document, insert another Input field of the same name, but with a different value. However, the value of a User Field is changed globally.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3151255				0	uz	The variables are displayed in the \<emph\>Selection\</emph\> field. When you click the \<emph\>Insert\</emph\> button, the dialog\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090100.xhp\" name=\"Input Field\"\>\<emph\>Input Field\</emph\>\</link\> appears, where you can enter the new value or additional text as a remark.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3149034				0	uz	Raqamlash oraligʻi				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3152772				0	uz	Jadvallar, grafik obʼektlar yoki matn freymlari uchun avtomatik raqamlashni kiritadi.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3147073				0	uz	Sahifa oʻzgaruvchisini oʻrnatish				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3154389				0	uz	Inserts a reference point in the document, after which the page count restarts. Select "on" to enable the reference point, and "off" to disable it. You can also enter an offset to start the page count at a different number.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3156267				0	uz	Sahifa oʻzgaruvchisini koʻrsatish				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3150588				0	uz	Displays the number of pages from the "Set page variable" reference point to this field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3145779				0	uz	Foydalanuvchi maydoni				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3151377				0	uz	Inserts a custom global variable. You can use the User Field to define a variable for a condition statement. When you change a User Field, all instances of the variable in the document are updated.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id0903200802243892				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click the format that you want to apply to the selected field, or click "Additional formats" to define a custom format.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3148886	25			0	uz	For user-defined fields, click the format that you want to apply in the \<emph\>Format \</emph\>list, or click "Additional formats" to define a custom format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id0903200802243880				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Type the name of the user-defined field that you want to create.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id0903200802243951				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the contents that you want to add to a user-defined field.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3155860				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_LISTBOX_TP_FLD_VAR_LB_VARFORMAT\"\>In the \<emph\>Format\</emph\> list, define if the value is inserted as text or a number.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	hd_id3888363				0	uz	Selection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id7453535				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:TP_FLD_DOK:LB_DOKSELECTION\"\>Lists the available fields for the field type selected in the \<emph\>Type \</emph\>list. To insert a field, click the field, and then click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3326822				0	uz	To quickly insert a field from the list, hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> and double-click the field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3150696	36			0	uz	In an HTML document, two additional fields are available for the "Set variable" field type: HTML_ON and HTML_OFF. The text that you type in the \<emph\>Value \</emph\>box is converted to an opening HTML \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000002.xhp#tags\" name=\"tag\"\>tag\</link\> (<Value>) or to a closing HTML (</Value>) tag when the file is saved as an HTML document, depending on the option that you select.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3149555				0	uz	If you double-click an entry while holding the Ctrl key or select the desired variable and press the spacebar, it is immediately inserted into your document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155969				0	uz	Formula				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3155982				0	uz	Ushbu parametr "Formula kiritish" maydoni turi tanlanganda aktiv boʻladi.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149229				0	uz	Koʻrinmaydigan				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3156233				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_CHECKBOX_TP_FLD_VAR_CB_VARINVISIBLE\"\>Hides the field contents in the document.\</ahelp\> The field is inserted as a thin gray mark in the document. This option is only available for the "Set Variable" and "User Field" field types.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146326				0	uz	Bobni raqamlash				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3146340				0	uz	Sets the options for resetting chapter numbers.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147456				0	uz	Level				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3149836				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_LISTBOX_TP_FLD_VAR_LB_VARCHAPTERLEVEL\"\>Choose the heading or chapter level at which to restart numbering in the document.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147594				0	uz	Separator				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3148846				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_EDIT_TP_FLD_VAR_ED_VARSEPARATOR\"\>Type the character that you want to use as a separator between the heading or chapter levels.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147057				0	uz	Apply				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3155562				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FLDVAR_APPLY\"\>Adds the user-defined field to the \<emph\>Selection\</emph\> list.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151080				0	uz	Delete				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3154769				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FLDVAR_DELETE\"\>Removes the user-defined field from the selection list. You can only remove fields that are not used in the current document.\</ahelp\> To remove a field that is used in the current document from the list, first delete all instances of the field in the document, and then remove it from the list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3150169				0	uz	Delete				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04130100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Resizing and Moving Frames, Objects With the Keyboard				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04130100.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154506				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>moving;objects and frames\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>objects;moving and resizing with keyboard\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>resizing;objects and frames, by keyboard\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04130100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154506				0	uz	Resizing and Moving Frames, Objects With the Keyboard				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04130100.xhp	0	help	par_id3145248				0	uz	Tanlangan freym yoki obʼektlarni klaviatura yordamida hajmini oʻzgartirishingiz va koʻchirishingiz mumkin.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04130100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148771				0	uz	To move a selected frame or object, press an arrow key. To move by one pixel, hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>, and then press an arrow key.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04130100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150762				0	uz	To resize a selected frame or object, first press Ctrl+Tab. Now one of the handles blinks to show that it is selected. To select another handle, press Ctrl+Tab again. Press an arrow key to resize the object by one grid unit. To resize by one pixel, hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>, and then press an arrow key.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Cross-references				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153641				0	uz	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090002.xhp\" name=\"Cross-references\"\>Cross-references\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3155142				0	uz	\<variable id=\"reftext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>This is where you insert the references or referenced fields into the current document. References are referenced fields within the same document or within sub-documents of a master document.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3159197				0	uz	The advantage of entering a cross-reference as a field is that you do not have to adjust the references manually every time you change the document. Just update the fields with F9 and the references in the document are updated too.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	hd_id4333628				0	uz	Type				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id4516129				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Lists the available field types. To add a field to your document, click a field type, click a field in the Selection list, and then click Insert.\</ahelp\> The following fields are available:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3151380				0	uz	Type				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3150700				0	uz	Meaning				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3155862				0	uz	Bogʻlamani oʻrnatish				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3147422				0	uz	Set target for a referenced field. Under \<emph\>Name\</emph\>, enter a name for the reference. When inserting the reference, the name will then appear as an identification in the list box \<emph\>Selection\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3149556				0	uz	In an HTML document, reference fields entered this way will be ignored. For the target in HTML documents, you have to \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04040000.xhp\" name=\"insert a bookmark\"\>insert a bookmark\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3150548				0	uz	Bogʻlama kiritish				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3147746				0	uz	Inserting a reference to another position in the document. The corresponding text position has to be defined with "Set Reference" first. Otherwise, inserting a reference by choosing a field name under \<emph\>Selection\</emph\> is not possible.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3146344				0	uz	In master documents, you can also reference from one sub-document to another. Note that the reference name will not appear in the selection field and has to be entered "by hand".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3149847				0	uz	In an HTML document, reference fields entered this way will be ignored. For referenced fields in HTML documents, you have to \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020400.xhp\" name=\"insert a hyperlink\"\>insert a hyperlink\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id2408825				0	uz	Headings				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id9988402				0	uz	The Selection box shows a list of all headings in the order of their appearance in the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id6401257				0	uz	Numbered Paragraphs				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id5841242				0	uz	The Selection box shows a list of all numbered headings and numbered paragraphs in the order of their appearance in the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id306711				0	uz	Bookmarks				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3150907				0	uz	After inserting a bookmark in the document with \<emph\>Insert - Bookmark\</emph\>, the bookmarks entry on the \<emph\>References\</emph\> tab becomes usable. Bookmarks are used to mark certain text passages in a document. In a text document, you can use the bookmarks, for example, to jump from one passage in the document to another.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3155080				0	uz	In an HTML document, these bookmarks become anchors <A name>, which determine the target of hyperlinks for example.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id0818200811011072				0	uz	Footnotes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id0818200811011049				0	uz	If your documents contains a footnote, you can select the Footnotes entry. A reference to a footnote returns the footnote number.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id6794030				0	uz	(Inserted objects with captions)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id7096774				0	uz	You can set references to objects that have captions applied. For example, insert a picture, right-click the picture, choose Caption. Now the object shows up as a numbered "Illustration" in the list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3154772				0	uz	References are fields. To remove a reference, delete the field. If you set a longer text as a reference and you do not want to reenter it after deleting the reference, select the text and copy it to the clipboard. You can then reinsert it as "unformatted text" at the same position using the command \<emph\>Edit - Paste special\</emph\>. The text remains intact while the reference is deleted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	hd_id5824152				0	uz	Selection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id7374187				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:TP_FLD_DOK:LB_DOKSELECTION\"\>Lists the available fields for the field type selected in the \<emph\>Type \</emph\>list. To insert a field, click the field, select a format in the "Insert reference to" list, and then click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id7729728				0	uz	To quickly insert a field from the list, hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> and double-click the field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id2171086				0	uz	In the \<emph\>Insert reference to\</emph\> list, click the format that you want to use.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154333				0	uz	Insert reference to				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3148786				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:TP_FLD_REF:LB_REFFORMAT\"\>Select the format that you want to use for the selected reference field.\</ahelp\> The following formats are available:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id7576525				0	uz	Format				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id641193				0	uz	Meaning				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3150039				0	uz	Page				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3153134				0	uz	Inserts the number of the page containing the reference target.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3150681				0	uz	Reference				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3154040				0	uz	Inserts the complete reference target text. For footnotes the footnote number is inserted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3149972				0	uz	Yuqori/Past				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3149619				0	uz	Inserts "above" or "below", depending on the location of the reference target relative to the position of the reference field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3148705				0	uz	As Page Style				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3148728				0	uz	Inserts the number of the page containing the reference target using the format specified in the page style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id5699942				0	uz	Number				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id6420484				0	uz	Inserts the number of the heading or numbered paragraph, including superior levels depending on the context. See note below this table for more information.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id6986602				0	uz	Number (no context)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id616779				0	uz	Inserts only the number of the heading or numbered paragraph.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id791039				0	uz	Number (full context)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id1953489				0	uz	Inserts the number of the heading or numbered paragraph, including all superior levels.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3154635				0	uz	Chapter				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3149646				0	uz	Inserts the number of the chapter containing the reference target.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3155553				0	uz	Category and Number				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3155356				0	uz	Inserts the category (caption type) and the number of the reference target. This option is only available when the reference target is an object with a caption.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3154224				0	uz	Sarlavha matni				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3145105				0	uz	Inserts the caption label of the reference target. This option is only available when the reference target is an object with a caption.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3149587				0	uz	Numbering				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3146883				0	uz	Inserts the caption number of the reference target. This option is only available when the reference target is an object with a caption.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id757469				0	uz	The "Number" format inserts the number of the heading or numbered paragraph. The superior levels are included depending on the context, as necessary. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id5189062				0	uz	For example, when you are in a chapter 1, subchapter 2, subpart 5, this may be numbered as 1.2.5. When you insert here a reference to text in the previous subpart "1.2.4" and you apply the "Number" format, then the reference will be shown as "4". If in this example the numbering is set to show more sublevels, the same reference will be shown as "2.4" or "1.2.4", depending on the setting. If you use the "Number (full context)" format, you will always see "1.2.4", no matter how the numbered paragraph is formatted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156242				0	uz	Name				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3156259				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:EDIT:TP_FLD_REF:ED_REFNAME\"\>Type the name of the user-defined field that you want to create.\</ahelp\> To set a target, click "Set Reference" in the \<emph\>Type\</emph\> list, type a name in this box, and then click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>. To reference the new target, click the target name in the \<emph\>Selection\</emph\> list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3156032	17			0	uz	In a master document, targets that are in different sub-documents are not displayed in the\<emph\> Selection\</emph\> list. If you want to insert a reference to the target, you must type the path and the name in the \<emph\>Name \</emph\>box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id0903200802250745				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the contents that you want to add to a user-defined fields.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3159216				0	uz	If you select text in the document, and then insert a reference, the selected text becomes the contents of the field that you insert.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id6501968				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Edit the value.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
