helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	hd_id6618243				0	uz	\<variable id=\"table_cellmerge\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/table_cellmerge.xhp\" name=\"Merging and Splitting Cells\"\>Merging and Splitting Cells\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id1211890				0	uz	You can select adjacent cells, then merge them into a single cell. Conversely, you can take a large cell and divide it into individual cells.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id5708792				0	uz	Select the adjacent cells.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id6301461				0	uz	Choose \<emph\>Table - Merge Cells\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id3415936				0	uz	Place the cursor in the cell to be split.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id4044312				0	uz	Choose \<emph\>Table - Split Cells\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id634174				0	uz	A dialog allows you to split the cell into two or more cells, horizontally or vertically.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Using Captions 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147691				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>inserting; captions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>captions; inserting and editing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing;captions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>objects; captioning\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; labeling\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>frames; labeling\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>charts; labeling\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text frames; labeling\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>draw objects; inserting captions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>legends, see also captions\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150537				0	uz	\<variable id=\"captions\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/captions.xhp\" name=\"Using Captions\"\>Using Captions\</link\> \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_id3153156				0	uz	In text documents, you can add continuously numbered captions to graphics, tables, frames, and drawing objects.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_id3153172				0	uz	You can edit the text and the number ranges for different types of captions.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_id3153186				0	uz	When you add a caption to a picture or to an object, the object and the caption text are placed together in a new frame. When you add a caption to a table, the caption text is inserted as a paragraph next to the table. When you add a caption to a frame, the caption text is added to the text inside the frame, either before or after the existing text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_idN10713				0	uz	To move both the object and the caption, drag the frame that contains these items. To update the caption numbering after you move the frame, press F9.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_id3155567				0	uz	Select the item that you want to add a caption to.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_id3155586				0	uz	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Caption\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_id3147254				0	uz	You can edit caption text directly in the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_id3147271				0	uz	A caption is formatted with the paragraph style that matches the name of the caption \<emph\>Category\</emph\>. For example, if you insert a "Table" caption, the "Table" paragraph style is applied to the caption text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Numbering and Numbering Styles				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155174				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>numbering; manually/by styles\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>manual numbering in text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>paragraph styles;numbering\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155174	30			0	uz	\<variable id=\"using_numbering\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/using_numbering.xhp\" name=\"Numbering and Numbering Styles\"\>Numbering and Numbering Styles\</link\> \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3149818				0	uz	You can apply numbering to a paragraph manually or with a paragraph style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3153405				0	uz	You cannot apply manual numbering to paragraphs that are listed under "Special Styles" in the Styles and Formatting window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_idN10711				0	uz	When you press Enter in a numbered or bulleted list, \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> automatically numbers the next paragraph. To remove the numbering or bullet from the new paragraph, press Enter again.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_idN1072B				0	uz	To change the hierarchical level of a bullet in a list, click in front of the paragraph, then press the Tab key.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_idN1072F				0	uz	To change the bullets or numbering format for the current paragraph only, select a character or word in the paragraph, choose Bullets and Numbering, and then click a new format. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_idN10733				0	uz	To change the bullet or numbering format for all paragraphs in the list, ensure that the cursor is in the list, choose Bullets and Numbering, and then click a new format. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_idN10737				0	uz	To apply the same bullet or numbering format to all paragraphs in the list, select all paragraphs, choose Bullets and Numbering, and then click a format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_idN1073A				0	uz	You can also use the commands on the \<link href=\"text/swriter/main0206.xhp\" name=\"Numbering Object Bar\"\>Bullets and Numbering\</link\> toolbar to edit a numbered or bulleted list. To change the numbering or bullet format, click the \<emph\>Bullets and Numbering\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153123				0	uz	To apply numbering with a Paragraph Style				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3153137				0	uz	Paragraph Styles give you greater control over numbering that you apply in a document. When you change the numbering format of the style, all paragraphs using the style are automatically updated.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3149599				0	uz	Right-click the paragraph style that you want to apply numbering to, and then choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3149874				0	uz	In the \<emph\>Numbering Styles\</emph\> box, select the type of numbering that you want to use.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3145113				0	uz	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3149589				0	uz	Apply the style to the paragraphs that you want to add numbering to.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
