helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Protecting Content in %PRODUCTNAME Writer				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150620				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>indexes;unprotecting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables of contents;unprotecting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables;protecting/unprotecting cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sections;protecting/unprotecting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>unprotecting tables of contents and indexes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>protecting;tables and sections\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells;protecting/unprotecting\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id6007263				0	uz	\<variable id=\"protection\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/protection.xhp\" name=\"Protecting Content in %PRODUCTNAME Writer\"\>Protecting Content in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Writer\</item\>\</link\> \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id1924802				0	uz	The following is an overview of the different ways of protecting contents in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer from being modified, deleted or viewed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150114				0	uz	Protecting Sections in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3150592				0	uz	Any section of a \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer text document can be protected against changes with a password.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id4545426				0	uz	This protection is not intended to be a secure protection. It is just a switch to protect the section against accidental changes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3166413				0	uz	Turning on protection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3144764				0	uz	Select the text. Choose \<emph\>Insert - Section - Section\</emph\>, then under \<emph\>Write protection\</emph\> mark the \<emph\>Protect\</emph\> and \<emph\>With password\</emph\> check boxes. (If the section already exists: \<emph\>Format - Sections\</emph\>.) Enter and confirm a password of at least 5 characters.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3147497				0	uz	Turning off protection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3147173				0	uz	Choose \<emph\>Format - Sections - Section\</emph\> and under \<emph\>Write protection\</emph\> clear the \<emph\>Protect\</emph\> check box. Enter the correct password.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146081				0	uz	Protecting Cells in a \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer Table				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3154480				0	uz	You can protect the contents of individual cells of a \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer text table from changes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id363170				0	uz	This protection is not intended to be a secure protection. It is just a switch to protect the cells against accidental changes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3154360				0	uz	Turning on protection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3145643				0	uz	Place the cursor in a cell or select cells. Right-click to open the context menu, then choose \<emph\>Cell - Protect\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3150042				0	uz	Turning off protection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3151189				0	uz	Select the table in the Navigator, open the context menu and select \<emph\>Table - Unprotect\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3147322				0	uz	Use Shift+Ctrl+T to remove protection for the entire current table or all selected tables.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149259				0	uz	Automatic Protection of Indexes and Tables				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3153966				0	uz	Tables of contents and indexes created automatically in a \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer text are automatically protected against accidental changes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id814539				0	uz	This protection is not intended to be a secure protection. It is just a switch to protect the contents against accidental changes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3145767				0	uz	Turning on protection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3153786				0	uz	Place the cursor in the index/table of contents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3159088				0	uz	From the context menu choose \<emph\>Edit Index/Table\</emph\>. On the Index/Table tab page, mark \<emph\>Protected against manual changes\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3154118				0	uz	Turning off protection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3152968				0	uz	From the context menu choose \<emph\>Edit Index/Table\</emph\>. On the Index/Table tab page, unmark \<emph\>Protected against manual changes\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3152774				0	uz	In the Navigator, select the index, then open the context menu in the Navigator and select \<emph\>Index - Read-only\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B8C				0	uz	 \<embedvar href=\"text/shared/guide/digital_signatures.xhp#digital_signatures\"/\> 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id7858516				0	uz	\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/protection.xhp\"\>Protecting Other Contents\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_repeat_multiple_headers.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Repeating a Table Header on a New Page				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_repeat_multiple_headers.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155870				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>tables; heading repetition after page breaks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>repeating; table headings after page breaks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>headings; repeating in tables\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_repeat_multiple_headers.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153406				0	uz	\<variable id=\"table_repeat_multiple_headers\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/table_repeat_multiple_headers.xhp\" name=\"Repeating a Table Header on a New Page\"\>Repeating a Table Heading on a New Page\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_repeat_multiple_headers.xhp	0	help	par_id3149636				0	uz	You can repeat a table heading on each new page that the table spans.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_repeat_multiple_headers.xhp	0	help	par_id3145098				0	uz	Choose \<emph\>Table - Insert - Table\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_repeat_multiple_headers.xhp	0	help	par_id3153376				0	uz	Select the number of rows and columns for the table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_repeat_multiple_headers.xhp	0	help	par_id3153393				0	uz	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_line.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Formatting Headers or Footers				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_line.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154866				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>inserting; lines under headers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>lines; under headers/above footers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>headers;formatting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>footers;formatting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>shadows;headers/footers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>borders;for headers/footers\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154866				0	uz	\<variable id=\"header_with_line\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/header_with_line.xhp\" name=\"Formatting Headers or Footers\"\>Formatting Headers or Footers\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3154243				0	uz	You can apply direct formatting to the text in a header or footer. You can also adjust the spacing of the text relative to the header or footer frame or apply a border to the header or footer.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3147109				0	uz	Oraliq parametrlarini kiriting.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Changing Page Orientation (Landscape or Portrait)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	bm_id9683828				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>page styles;orientation/scope\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>page formats; changing individual pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting; changing individual pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>portrait and landscape\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>landscape and portrait\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>printing;portrait/landscape format\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>orientation of pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>paper orientation\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pages;orientation\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sideways orientation of pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>scope of page styles\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN106FF				0	uz	\<variable id=\"pageorientation\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/pageorientation.xhp\"\>Changing Page Orientation\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id6418042				0	uz	All page properties for Writer text documents, like for example the page orientation, are defined by page styles. By default, a new text document uses the \<emph\>Default\</emph\> page style for all pages. If you open an existing text document, different page styles may have been applied to the different pages. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id8324533				0	uz	It is important to know that changes that you apply to a page property will only affect the pages that use the current page style. The current page style is listed in the Status Bar at the lower window border.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id7524033				0	uz	To change the page orientation for all pages				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id6307260				0	uz	If your text document consists only of pages with the same page style, you can change the page properties directly:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id5256508				0	uz	Choose \<emph\>Format - Page\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id9681997				0	uz	Click the \<emph\>Page\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id7069002				0	uz	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	hd_id4202398				0	uz	To change the page orientation only for some pages				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN1071D				0	uz	$[officename] uses page styles to specify the orientation of the pages in a document. Page styles define more page properties, as for example header and footer or page margins. You can either change the \<emph\>Default\</emph\> page style for the current document, or you can define own page styles and apply those page styles to any parts of your text. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id1449324				0	uz	At the end of this help page, we'll discuss the scope of page styles in detail. If you are unsure about the page style concept, please read the section at the end of this page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id1480758				0	uz	Unlike character styles or paragraph styles, the page styles don't know a hierarchy. You can create a new page style based on the properties of an existing page style, but when you later change the source style, the new page style does not automatically inherit the changes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id2962126				0	uz	To change the page orientation for all pages that share the same page style, you first need a page style, then apply that style:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN10727				0	uz	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN10741				0	uz	Click the \<emph\>Page Styles\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN10749				0	uz	Right-click a page style and choose \<emph\>New\</emph\>. The new page style initially gets all properties of the selected page style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN10751				0	uz	On the \<emph\>Organizer\</emph\> tab page, type a name for the page style in the \<emph\>Name\</emph\> box, for example "My Landscape".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN1075D				0	uz	In the \<emph\>Next Style\</emph\> box, select the page style that you want to apply to the next page that follows a page with the new style. See the section about the scope of page styles at the end of this help page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN10775				0	uz	Click the \<emph\>Page\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN108AE				0	uz	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id1658375				0	uz	Now you have defined a proper page style with the name "My Landscape". To apply the new style, double-click the "My Landscape" page style in the \<emph\>Styles and Formatting\</emph\> window. All pages in the current scope of page styles will be changed. If you defined the "next style" to be a different style, only the first page of the current scope of page styles will be changed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	hd_id6082949				0	uz	The scope of page styles				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id2858668				0	uz	You should be aware of the scope of page styles in %PRODUCTNAME. Which pages of your text document get affected by editing a page style?				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3278603				0	uz	One page long styles				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id5169225				0	uz	A page style can be defined to span one page only. The \<emph\>First Page\</emph\> style is an example. You set this property by defining another page style to be the "next style", on the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Page - Organizer\</item\> tab page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id6670125				0	uz	A one page long style starts from the lower border of the current page style range up to the next page break. The next page break appears automatically when the text flows to the next page, which is sometimes called a "soft page break". Alternatively, you can insert a manual page break.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id2118594				0	uz	To insert a manual page break at the cursor position, press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl+Enter\</item\> or choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Manual Break\</item\> and just click OK.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	hd_id166020				0	uz	Manually defined range of a page style				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id6386913				0	uz	The \<emph\>Default\</emph\> page style does not set a different "next style" on the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Page - Organizer\</item\> tab page. Instead, the "next style" is set also to be \<emph\>Default\</emph\>. All page styles that are followed by the same page style can span multiple pages. The lower and upper borders of the page style range are defined by "page breaks with style". All the pages between any two "page breaks with style" use the same page style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id6062196				0	uz	You can insert a "page break with style" directly at the cursor position. Alternatively, you can apply the "page break with style" property to a paragraph or to a paragraph style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id6054261				0	uz	Perform any one of the following commands:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id1811578				0	uz	To insert a "page break with style" at the cursor position, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Manual Break\</item\>, select a \<emph\>Style\</emph\> name from the listbox, and click OK.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id9935911				0	uz	To apply the "page break with style" property to the current paragraph, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Paragraph - Text Flow\</item\>. In the Breaks area, activate \<emph\>Enable\</emph\> and \<emph\>With Page Style\</emph\>. Select a page style name from the listbox.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id4753868				0	uz	To apply the "page break with style" property to the current paragraph style, right-click the current paragraph. Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit Paragraph Style\</item\> from the context menu. Click the \<emph\>Text Flow\</emph\> tab. In the Breaks area, activate \<emph\>Enable\</emph\> and \<emph\>With Page Style\</emph\>. Select a page style name from the listbox.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id4744407				0	uz	To apply the "page break with style" property to an arbitrary paragraph style, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</item\>. Click the \<emph\>Paragraph Styles\</emph\> icon. Right-click the name of the paragraph style you want to modify and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>. Click the \<emph\>Text Flow\</emph\> tab. In the Breaks area, activate \<emph\>Enable\</emph\> and \<emph\>With Page Style\</emph\>. Select a page style name from the listbox.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	About Headers and Footers				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155863				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>headers;about\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>footers;about\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>HTML documents; headers and footers\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155863				0	uz	\<variable id=\"header_footer\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/header_footer.xhp\" name=\"About Headers and Footers\"\>About Headers and Footers\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3154255				0	uz	Headers and footers are areas in the top and the bottom page margins, where you can add text or graphics. Headers and footers are added to the current page style. Any page that uses the same style automatically receives the header or footer that you add. You can insert \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090000.xhp\" name=\"Fields\"\>Fields\</link\>, such as page numbers and chapter headings, in headers and footers in a text document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3150511				0	uz	The page style for the current page is displayed in the \<emph\>Status Bar\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3155896				0	uz	To add a header to a page, choose \<emph\>Insert - Header\</emph\>, and then select the page style for the current page from the submenu.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3147119				0	uz	To add a footer to a page, choose \<emph\>Insert - Footer\</emph\>, and then select the page style for the current page from the submenu.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3146876				0	uz	To use different headers or footers in your document, you must add them to different \<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/header_pagestyles.xhp\" name=\"Page Styles\"\>Page Styles\</link\>, and then apply the styles to the pages where you want the headers or footer to appear.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150704				0	uz	Headers and Footers in HTML Documents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3150717	34			0	uz	Some of the header and footer options are also available for HTML documents. Headers and footers are not supported by HTML and instead are exported with special tags, so that they can be viewed in a browser. Headers and footers are only exported in HTML documents if they are enabled in Web Layout mode. When you reopen the document in $[officename], the headers and footers are displayed correctly, including any fields that you inserted. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3153174				0	uz	\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/header_pagestyles.xhp\" name=\"Page Styles\"\>Page Styles\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Fine-Tuning the Word Completion for Text Documents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148882				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>settings;word completion\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>word completion;settings\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text documents;word completion settings\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>weekdays; automatically completing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>months; automatically completing\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	hd_id4745017				0	uz	\<variable id=\"word_completion_adjust\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/word_completion_adjust.xhp\"\>Fine-Tuning the Word Completion for Text Documents\</link\> \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_id4814294				0	uz	If you like it that $[officename] automatically completes the words that you frequently use, you can make further adjustments to refine that behaviour. If you want, you can also save the current list of collected words so that it can be used in the next session. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_id2593462				0	uz	To fine-tune the word completion choose \<emph\>Tools - AutoCorrect - Word Completion\</emph\> and select any of the following options: 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN107C6				0	uz	 Inserting an additional space character 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B03				0	uz	 Select \<emph\>Append space\</emph\>. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B0E				0	uz	 The space character is appended after you type the first character of the next word after the auto-completed word. The space character is suppressed if the next character is a delimiter, such as a full stop or a new line character. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B20				0	uz	 Choose the key to accept the suggested word using the \<emph\>Accept with\</emph\> list box. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B36				0	uz	 Use the \<emph\>Min. word length\</emph\> box to set the minimum number of characters a word must have to be collected into the list. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN107D8				0	uz	 Selecting the scope of collected words 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B53				0	uz	 Now the list is also valid for other documents that you open. When you close the last %PRODUCTNAME document, the word list is deleted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B56				0	uz	 If you do not select the checkbox, the list is only valid as long as the current document is open. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_id2634968				0	uz	If you want the word list to exist longer than the current %PRODUCTNAME session, save it as a document, as described in the following section.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B94				0	uz	 If the automatic spellcheck option is enabled, only the words that are recognized by the spellcheck are collected. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10BA1				0	uz	 Use the word list to always start with a defined set of technical terms for the word completion feature. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10BA7				0	uz	 Open the text document that contains the terms that you want to use for word completion. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10BAB				0	uz	 The word completion feature collects the words. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN107ED				0	uz	 Select all or some of the words in the list. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F4				0	uz	 Use \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+C to copy all selected words into the clipboard. Paste the clipboard into a new document and save it to get a reference list of collected words. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10BC6				0	uz	 Later you can open the reference list and automatically collect the words, so that the word completion feature starts with a defined set of words. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10809				0	uz	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/06040600.xhp\"\>Word Completion \</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_id5458845				0	uz	\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/word_completion.xhp\"\>Using Word Completion\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Templates and Styles				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153396				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>formatting styles; styles and templates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>styles; styles and templates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>organizing; templates (guide)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>templates; organizing (guide)\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153396				0	uz	\<variable id=\"templates_styles\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/templates_styles.xhp\" name=\"Templates and Styles\"\>Templates and Styles\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3149635				0	uz	A template is a document that contains specific formatting styles, graphics, tables, objects, and other information. A template is used as the basis for creating other documents. For example, you can define paragraph and character styles in a document, save the document as a template, and then use the template to create a new document with the same styles.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3149957				0	uz	Unless you specify otherwise, every new $[officename] text document is based on the default template.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3149974				0	uz	$[officename] has a number of \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05130000.xhp\" name=\"predefined templates\"\>predefined templates\</link\> that you can use to create different types or text documents, such as business letters.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149613				0	uz	Viewing and Organizing Styles in Templates				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B0				0	uz	Use the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01110100.xhp\" name=\"Template Management\"\>Template Management\</link\> dialog to copy styles from one document to another.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3153377				0	uz	To copy a style, drag it to another template or document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyphen_prevent.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Preventing Hyphenation of Specific Words				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyphen_prevent.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149695				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>hyphenation;preventing for specific words\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>words;wrapping/not wrapping in text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>switching off;hyphenation for specific words\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyphen_prevent.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149695				0	uz	\<variable id=\"hyphen_prevent\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/hyphen_prevent.xhp\" name=\"Preventing Hyphenation of Specific Words\"\>Preventing Hyphenation of Specific Words\</link\> \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyphen_prevent.xhp	0	help	par_id5640125				0	uz	If your text is \<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/using_hyphen.xhp\"\>automatically hyphenated\</link\> and certain hyphenated words look ugly, or if you want specific words never to be hyphenated you can switch off hyphenation for those words:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyphen_prevent.xhp	0	help	par_id3153658	41			0	uz	Select a dictionary in the \<emph\>User-defined dictionary \</emph\>list, and then click \<emph\>Edit\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyphen_prevent.xhp	0	help	par_id3147125				0	uz	If the list is empty, click \<emph\>New\</emph\> to create a dictionary.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyphen_prevent.xhp	0	help	par_id3150218	42			0	uz	In the\<emph\> Word\</emph\> box, type the word you want to exclude from hyphenation, followed by an equal sign (=), for example, "pretentious=".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyphen_prevent.xhp	0	help	par_id3150247				0	uz	Click \<emph\>New\</emph\>, and then click \<emph\>Close\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyphen_prevent.xhp	0	help	par_id3147036	29			0	uz	To quickly exclude a word from hyphenation, select the word, choose \<emph\>Format - Character\</emph\>, click the \<emph\>Font \</emph\>tab, and select "None" in the \<emph\>Language \</emph\>box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
