helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3149842				0	uz	A text frame is a container for text and graphics that you can place anywhere on a page. You can also use a frame to apply a column layout to text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3149961				0	uz	Select the text that you want to include in the frame.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3149602				0	uz	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Frame\</emph\>, and click OK.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3149578				0	uz	To edit the contents of a text frame, click in the frame, and make the changes that you want.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3156239				0	uz	To edit a frame, select the frame, right-click, and then choose a formatting option. You can also right-click the selected frame, and choose \<emph\>Frame\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3156261				0	uz	To resize a text frame, click an edge of frame, and drag one of the edges or corners of the frame. Hold down Shift while you drag to maintain the proportion of the frame.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153386				0	uz	Hiding Text From Printing				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3154262				0	uz	Any Writer text frame can be set to a mode which allows viewing the text on screen, but hides the text from printing.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3154858				0	uz	Select the text frame (you see the eight handles).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3155875				0	uz	Choose \<emph\>Format - Frame/Object - Options\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3155899				0	uz	In the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> area, unmark the \<emph\>Print\</emph\> check box and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3149986				0	uz	You can link Writer text frames so that their contents automatically flow from one frame to another.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3153025				0	uz	Click the edge of a frame that you want to link. Selection handles appear on the edges of the frame.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3150930				0	uz	Click the frame that you want to link to.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3150947				0	uz	You can only link frames if:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3150969				0	uz	The target frame is empty.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3154365				0	uz	The target frame is not linked to another frame.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3154383				0	uz	The source and the target frames are in the same section. For example, you cannot link a header frame to a footer frame.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3145559				0	uz	The source frame does not have a next link.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3145577				0	uz	The target or the source frame are not contained in each other.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3151083				0	uz	When you select a linked frame, a line is displayed that connects the linked frames.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id5853144				0	uz	The Autosize feature is available only for the last frame in a chain of linked frames.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
