helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3150534				0	uz	In $[officename] Writer, you can store text - also containing graphics, tables, and fields - as AutoText, so that you can quickly insert the text later on. If you want, you can also store formatted text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155539				0	uz	Avto-matn yozuvini qoʻyish				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3155560				0	uz	Select the text, text with graphics, table, or field that you want to save as an AutoText entry. A graphic can only be stored if it is anchored as a character and is preceded and followed by at least one text character.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3147761				0	uz	Avto-matn saqlanishi kerak boʻlgan turkumni tanlang.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3147779				0	uz	Type a name that is longer than four characters. This allows you to use the \<emph\>Display remainder of name as suggestion while typing\</emph\> AutoText option. If you want, you can modify the proposed shortcut.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3147807	60			0	uz	Click the \<emph\>AutoText\</emph\> button, and then choose \<emph\>New\</emph\>. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
