helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149695				0	uz	\<variable id=\"indices_edit\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/indices_edit.xhp\" name=\"Updating, Editing and Deleting Indexes and Tables of Contents\"\>Updating, Editing and Deleting Indexes and Tables of Contents\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3155856				0	uz	Kursorni indeks yoki mundarijaga olib boring.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3154248				0	uz	Sichqoncha oʻng tugmasini bosing va menyudan tahrirlash parametrini tanlang.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3155872				0	uz	You can also make changes directly to an index or table of contents. Right-click in the index or table of contents, choose \<emph\>Edit Index/Table\</emph\>, click \<emph\>Index/Table\</emph\> tab, and then clear the \<emph\>Protected from manual changes\</emph\> check box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Outline Numbering				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147682				0	uz	\<variable id=\"chapter_numbering\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/chapter_numbering.xhp\" name=\"Outline Numbering\"\>Outline Numbering\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3155605				0	uz	You can modify the heading hierarchy or assign a level in the hierarchy to a custom paragraph style. You can also add chapter and section numbering to heading paragraph styles. By default, the "Heading 1" paragraph style is at the top of the outline hierarchy.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155626				0	uz	To add automatic numbering to a heading style:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_idN107CE				0	uz	To remove automatic outline numbering from a heading paragraph:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_idN107D5				0	uz	Click at the beginning of the text in the heading paragraph, after the number.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_idN107D9				0	uz	Press the \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Backspace\</item\> key to delete the number.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155552				0	uz	To use a custom paragraph style as a heading:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3147758				0	uz	Select the custom style in the \<emph\>Paragraph Style\</emph\> box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3147808				0	uz	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Using Wildcards in Text Searches				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150099				0	uz	\<variable id=\"search_regexp\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/search_regexp.xhp\"\>Using Wildcards in Text Searches\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3155182				0	uz	You can use wildcards when you find and replace text in a document. For example, "s.n" finds "sun" and "son".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3149843				0	uz	In the \<emph\>Search for \</emph\>box, type the search term and the wildcard(s) that you want to use in your search.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153401				0	uz	Regular Expression Examples				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3149641				0	uz	The wildcard for a single character is a period (.).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3153136				0	uz	The wildcard for zero or more occurrences of the previous character is an asterisk. For example: "123*" finds "12" "123", and "1233".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3149609				0	uz	The wildcard combination to search for zero or more occurrences of any character is a period and asterisk (.*).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3149854				0	uz	The wildcard for the end of a paragraph is a dollar sign ($). The wildcard character combination for the start of a paragraph is a caret and a period (^.).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3149875				0	uz	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/02100001.xhp\" name=\"List of Wildcards\"\>List of Wildcards\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cells.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Adding or Deleting a Row or Column to a Table Using the Keyboard				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cells.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156377				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>rows; inserting/deleting in tables by keyboard\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>columns; inserting/deleting in tables by keyboard\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; editing by keyboard\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>keyboard;adding or deleting rows/columns\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>splitting cells;by keyboard\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>merging;cells, by keyboard\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>deleting;rows/columns, by keyboard\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;rows/columns, by keyboard\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cells.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156377				0	uz	\<variable id=\"table_cells\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/table_cells.xhp\" name=\"Adding or Deleting a Row or Column to a Table Using the Keyboard\"\>Adding or Deleting a Row or Column to a Table Using the Keyboard\</link\> \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3149487				0	uz	You can add or delete rows or columns in table as well as split or merge table cells using the keyboard.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3155906				0	uz	To insert a new row in a table, place the cursor in a table cell, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Insert, and then press the up or down arrow key. You can also move the cursor to the last cell in the table, and then press Tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3147412				0	uz	To insert a new column, place the cursor in a table cell, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Insert, and then press the left or right arrow key.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3156096				0	uz	To split a table cell instead of adding a column, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Insert, and then hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> while you press the left or right arrow key.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3153408				0	uz	To delete a row, place the cursor in a table cell, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Delete, and then press the up or down arrow key.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3149626				0	uz	To delete a column, place the cursor in a table cell, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Delete, and then press the left or the right arrow key.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3149612				0	uz	To merge a table into an adjacent cell, place the cursor in the cell, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Delete, hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>, and then press the left or the right arrow key.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
