helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Defining Borders for Objects 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146957				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>objects; defining borders\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>borders; for objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>frames; around objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>charts;borders\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pictures;borders\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>OLE objects;borders\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defining;object borders\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146957				0	uz	\<variable id=\"border_object\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/border_object.xhp\" name=\"Defining Borders for Objects\"\>Defining Borders for Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3146797				0	uz	In Writer, you can define borders around OLE objects, plug-ins, diagrams/charts, graphics and frames. The name of the menu to be used depends on the object selected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145673				0	uz	Setting a Predefined Border Style				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3155388				0	uz	Select the object for which you want to define a border.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3149578	4			0	uz	Click the \<emph\>Borders\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>OLE-Object\</emph\> toolbar or \<emph\>Frame\</emph\> toolbar to open the \<emph\>Borders\</emph\> window. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3159176				0	uz	Click one of the predefined border styles. This replaces the current border style of the object with the selected style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152474				0	uz	Setting a Customized Border Style				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3153896				0	uz	Oʻzgartirilishi kerak boʻlgan jadval kataklarini tanlang.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3148797				0	uz	In the \<emph\>User-defined\</emph\> area select the edge(s) that you want to appear in a common layout. Click on an edge in the preview to toggle the selection of an edge.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3152933				0	uz	Select a line style and color for the selected border style in the \<emph\>Line\</emph\> area. These settings apply to all border lines that are included in the selected border style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3125865				0	uz	Repeat the last two steps for every border edge.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3150447				0	uz	Select the distance between the border lines and the page contents in the \<emph\>Spacing to Contents\</emph\> area.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3154908				0	uz	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to apply the changes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
