helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Creating a Table of Contents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147104				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>tables of contents; creating and updating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>updating; tables of contents\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147104				0	uz	\<variable id=\"indices_toc\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/indices_toc.xhp\" name=\"Creating a Table of Contents\"\>Creating a Table of Contents\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	par_id3150942				0	uz	The best way to generate a table of contents is to apply the predefined heading paragraph styles, such as "Heading 1", to the paragraphs that you want to include in your table of contents. After you apply these styles, you can then create a table of contents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	hd_id5876949				0	uz	Updating a Table of Contents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	par_id3150510				0	uz	Click in your document where you want to create the table of contents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	par_id3150528				0	uz	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Indexes and Tables - Indexes and Tables\</emph\>, and then click the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04120211.xhp\" name=\"Index/Table\"\>\<emph\>Index/Table\</emph\>\</link\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	par_id3153746				0	uz	Select "Table of Contents" in the \<emph\>Type\</emph\> box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	par_id3146856				0	uz	Select any options that you want.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	par_id3146872				0	uz	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153148				0	uz	Updating a Table of Contents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	par_id3153161				0	uz	Do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	par_id3153183				0	uz	Right-click in the table of contents and choose \<emph\>Update Index/Table\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	par_id3147066				0	uz	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Update - All Indexes and Tables\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\form_letters_main.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Creating a Form Letter				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\form_letters_main.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159257				0	uz	\<variable id=\"form_letters\"\>\<variable id=\"form_letters_main\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/form_letters_main.xhp\" name=\"Creating a Form Letter\"\>Creating a Form Letter\</link\>\</variable\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\form_letters_main.xhp	0	help	par_id3150502				0	uz	To create a form letter, you need a text document that contains fields for address data, and an address database. Then you combine or merge the address data and the text document to either print the letters or send them by e-mail.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\form_letters_main.xhp	0	help	par_id0805200801132382				0	uz	If the document is in HTML format, any embedded or linked images will not be sent with the e-mail.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\form_letters_main.xhp	0	help	par_idN10653				0	uz	The \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/mailmerge00.xhp\"\>Mail Merge Wizard\</link\> helps you to create form letters.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\form_letters_main.xhp	0	help	par_idN10664				0	uz	To create a form letter				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\form_letters_main.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066B				0	uz	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Mail Merge Wizard\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\form_letters_main.xhp	0	help	par_idN10672				0	uz	You see the Mail Merge Wizard dialog. The following is an example of one of many possible ways to navigate the wizard's pages:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\form_letters_main.xhp	0	help	par_idN10676				0	uz	Select \<emph\>Start from a template\</emph\>, and click the \<emph\>Browse\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\form_letters_main.xhp	0	help	par_idN10685				0	uz	Select \<item type=\"literal\"\>Business Correspondence\</item\> in the left list, and then \<item type=\"literal\"\>Modern letter\</item\> in the right list. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to close the Templates dialog, and click \<emph\>Next\</emph\> in the wizard.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\form_letters_main.xhp	0	help	par_id2669759				0	uz	Select \<emph\>Letter\</emph\> and click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\form_letters_main.xhp	0	help	par_idN106BD				0	uz	On the next step of the wizard, click the \<emph\>Select Address List\</emph\> button to check that you are using the correct address list. Select an address block type, match the data fields if necessary, and click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\form_letters_main.xhp	0	help	par_idN106C5				0	uz	Next follows the \<emph\>Create a salutation\</emph\> step. Deselect the \<emph\>Insert personalized salutation\</emph\> box. Under \<emph\>General salutation\</emph\>, select the salutation that you want on top of all letters.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\form_letters_main.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D5				0	uz	Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\> and finally \<emph\>Finish\</emph\> to create the mail merge.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\send2html.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Saving Text Documents in HTML Format				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\send2html.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145087				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>text documents; publishing in HTML\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>HTML documents; creating from text documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>homepage creation\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>saving;in HTML format\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\send2html.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145087				0	uz	\<variable id=\"send2html\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/send2html.xhp\" name=\"Saving Text Documents in HTML Format\"\>Saving Text Documents in HTML Format\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\send2html.xhp	0	help	par_id3149825				0	uz	You can save a $[officename] Writer document in HTML format, so that you can view it in a web browser. If you want, you can associate a page break with a specific heading paragraph style to generate a separate HTML page each time the style appears in the document. $[officename] Writer automatically creates a page containing hyperlinks to each of these pages.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\send2html.xhp	0	help	par_id3155922				0	uz	When you save a text document in HTML format, any graphics in the document are saved in JPEG format. The name of the HTML document is added as a prefix to the name of the graphic file. The JPEG images are saved in the same folder as the HTML document and are referenced with <IMG> tags in the HTML code.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\send2html.xhp	0	help	par_id3155868				0	uz	Apply one of the default $[officename] heading paragraph styles, for example, "Heading 1", to the paragraphs where you want to generate a new HTML page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\send2html.xhp	0	help	par_id3156100				0	uz	Choose \<emph\>File - Send - Create HTML Document\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\send2html.xhp	0	help	par_id3149281				0	uz	In the \<emph\>Style \</emph\>box, select the paragraph style that you want to use for chapter titles, for example, "Heading 1".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\send2html.xhp	0	help	par_id3153407				0	uz	Enter a path and a name for the HTML document, and then click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\load_styles.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Using Styles From Another Document or Template				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\load_styles.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145086				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>formatting styles; importing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>styles; importing from other files\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>importing;styles from other files\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>loading;styles from other files\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\load_styles.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145086				0	uz	\<variable id=\"load_styles\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/load_styles.xhp\" name=\"Using Styles From Another Document or Template\"\>Using Styles From Another Document or Template\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\load_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3154491				0	uz	You can import styles from another document or template into the current document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\load_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3155910				0	uz	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\> to open the \<emph\>Styles and Formatting\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\load_styles.xhp	0	help	par_idN10703				0	uz	Click the arrow next to the \<emph\>New Style from Selection\</emph\> icon to open the submenu.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\load_styles.xhp	0	help	par_idN1070B				0	uz	Choose \<emph\>Load styles\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\load_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3149632				0	uz	Use the check boxes at the bottom of the dialog to select the style types that you want to import. To replace styles in the current document that have the same name as the ones you are importing, select \<emph\>Overwrite\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\load_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3145098				0	uz	Do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Using Shortcut Keys ($[officename] Writer Accessibility)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151169				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>keyboard; accessibility $[officename] Writer\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>accessibility; $[officename] Writer\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151169				0	uz	\<variable id=\"keyboard\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/keyboard.xhp\" name=\"Using Shortcut Keys ($[officename] Writer Accessibility)\"\>Using Shortcut Keys ($[officename] Writer Accessibility)\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149685				0	uz	Press the keys \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+<underlined character> to open a menu. In an open menu, press the underlined character to run a command. For example, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+I to open the \<emph\>Insert\</emph\> menu, and then T to insert a table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155186				0	uz	To open a context menu, press Shift+F10. To close a context menu, press Escape.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_idN106AA				0	uz	Choose \<emph\>View - Toolbars - Insert\</emph\> to open the \<emph\>Insert\</emph\> toolbar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149630				0	uz	Press the right arrow key until the \<emph\>Section\</emph\> icon is selected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145100				0	uz	Press the down arrow key, and then press the right arrow key to set the width of the section that you want to insert.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3156237				0	uz	Press Enter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3156253				0	uz	Press F6 to place the cursor inside the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154849				0	uz	Press the right arrow key until the \<emph\>Table\</emph\> icon is selected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155872				0	uz	Press the down arrow key, and then use the arrow keys to select the number of columns and rows to include in the table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155892				0	uz	Press Enter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_idN1072C				0	uz	Press F6 to place the cursor inside the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Master Documents and Subdocuments				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145246				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>master documents;properties\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>subdocuments;properties\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>central documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>subsidiary documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>documents; master documents and subdocuments\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>styles;master documents\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145246				0	uz	\<variable id=\"globaldoc\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/globaldoc.xhp\"\>Master Documents and Subdocuments\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc.xhp	0	help	par_id3149806				0	uz	A master document lets you manage large documents, such as a book with many chapters. The master document can be seen as a container for individual \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer files. The individual files are called subdocuments.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc.xhp	0	help	hd_id6537369				0	uz	Characteristics of Master Documents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc.xhp	0	help	par_id3150096				0	uz	When you print a master document, the contents of all subdocuments, indexes, and any text that you entered are printed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc.xhp	0	help	par_id3153400				0	uz	You can create a table of contents and index in the master document for all of the subdocuments.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc.xhp	0	help	par_id3155854				0	uz	Styles that are used in subdocuments, such as new paragraph styles, are automatically imported into the master document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc.xhp	0	help	par_id9033783				0	uz	When viewing the master document, styles that are already present in the master document take precedence over styles with the same name that are imported from subdocuments. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc.xhp	0	help	par_id3419598				0	uz	Subdocuments never get changed by changes made to the master document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc.xhp	0	help	par_id3155180				0	uz	When you add a document to a master document or create a new subdocument, a link is created in the master document. You cannot edit the content of a subdocument directly in the master document, but you can use the Navigator to open any subdocument for edit.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc.xhp	0	help	hd_id7904904				0	uz	Example of using styles				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc.xhp	0	help	par_id5817743				0	uz	A master document master.odm consists of some text and links to the subdocuments sub1.odt and sub2.odt. In each subdocument a new paragraph style with the same name Style1 is defined and used, and the subdocuments are saved.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc.xhp	0	help	par_id9169591				0	uz	When you save the master document, the styles from the subdocuments are imported into the master document. First, the new style Style1 from the sub1.odt is imported. Next, the new styles from sub2.odt will be imported, but as Style1 now already is present in the master document, this style from sub2.odt will not be imported. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc.xhp	0	help	par_id1590014				0	uz	In the master document you now see the new style Style1 from the first subdocument. All Style1 paragraphs in the master document will be shown using the Style1 attributes from the first subdocument. However, the second subdocument by itself will not be changed. You see the Style1 paragraphs from the second subdocument with different attributes, depending whether you open the sub2.odt document by itself or as part of the master document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc.xhp	0	help	par_id5878780				0	uz	To avoid confusion, use the same document template for the master document and its subdocuments. This happens automatically when you create the master document and its subdocuments from an existing document with headings, using the command \<emph\>File - Send - Create Master Document\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc.xhp	0	help	par_id3154382				0	uz	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/02110000.xhp\" name=\"Navigator in master mode\"\>Navigator in master mode\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
