helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Defining Different Headers and Footers				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155920				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>headers;defining for left and right pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>footers;defining for left and right pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>page styles; changing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defining; headers/footers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>mirrored page layout\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155920				0	uz	\<variable id=\"header_pagestyles\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/header_pagestyles.xhp\" name=\"Defining Different Headers and Footers\"\>Defining Different Headers and Footers\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3154263				0	uz	You can use different headers and footers on different pages in your document, so long as the pages use different page styles. $[officename] provides several predefined page styles, such as \<emph\>First page\</emph\>, \<emph\>Left page\</emph\> and \<emph\>Right page\</emph\>, or you can create a custom page style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150224				0	uz	For example, you can use page styles to define different headers for even and odd pages in a document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150929				0	uz	Yangi matn hujjati oching.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150946				0	uz	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Page Styles\</emph\> icon in the Styles and Formatting window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150510				0	uz	Right-click "Right Page" in the list of page styles and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3146889				0	uz	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150714				0	uz	In the \<emph\>Styles and Formatting\</emph\> window, right-click "Left Page" in the list of page styles and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3147086				0	uz	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3145263				0	uz	Uslubni joriy sahifaga qoʻllash uchun sahifa uslublari roʻyxatidan "Oʻngdagi sahifa"ni ikki marta bosing.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3145284	43			0	uz	Enter text or graphics in the header for the Left Page style. After the next page is added to your document, enter text or graphics in the header for the Right Page style. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Hyphenation				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149695				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>hyphenation;manual/automatic\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>separation, see hyphenation\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>automatic hyphenation in text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>manual hyphenation in text\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149695				0	uz	\<variable id=\"using_hyphen\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/using_hyphen.xhp\" name=\"Hyphenation\"\>Hyphenation\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3155918	31			0	uz	By default, $[officename] moves words that do not fit on a line to the next line. If you want, you can use automatic or manual hyphenation to avoid this behavior: 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155864				0	uz	Automatic hyphenation				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3147414				0	uz	Automatic hyphenation inserts hyphens where they are needed in a paragraph. This option is only available for paragraph styles and individual paragraphs.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149832				0	uz	To automatically hyphenate text in a paragraph:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3148850				0	uz	Right-click in a paragraph, and choose \<emph\>Paragraph\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3156104				0	uz	Click the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05030200.xhp\" name=\"Text Flow\"\>\<emph\>Text Flow\</emph\>\</link\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3153121				0	uz	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149629				0	uz	To automatically hyphenate text in multiple paragraphs:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3149644				0	uz	If you want to automatically hyphenate more than one paragraph, use a paragraph style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3149956				0	uz	For example, enable the automatic hyphenation option for the "Default" paragraph style, and then apply the style to the paragraphs that you want to hyphenate.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3149611				0	uz	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Paragraph Styles\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3149867				0	uz	Right-click the paragraph style that you want to hyphenate, and then choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3149582				0	uz	In the \<emph\>Hyphenation\</emph\> area, select the \<emph\>Automatically\</emph\> check box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3156250				0	uz	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3145400				0	uz	Apply the style to the paragraphs that you want to hyphenate.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145417				0	uz	Manual Hyphenation				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3154400				0	uz	You can insert a hyphen where you want on a line, or let $[officename] search for the words to hyphenate, and then offer a suggested hyphenation.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3153363				0	uz	To quickly insert a hyphen, click in the word where you want to add the hyphen, and then press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Hyphen(-).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3154244				0	uz	If you insert a manual hyphen in a word, the word is only hyphenated at the manual hyphen. No additional automatic hyphenation is applied for this word. A word with a manual hyphen will be hyphenated without regard to the settings on the \<emph\>Text Flow\</emph\> tab page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154847				0	uz	To manually hyphenate text in a selection:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3154869				0	uz	Select the text that you want to hyphenate.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3155886				0	uz	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Language - Hyphenation\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3154361				0	uz	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05030200.xhp\" name=\"Text Flow\"\>Text Flow\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
