helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155622				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>smart tags\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>AutoCorrect function; smart tags\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>options;smart tags\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>disabling;smart tags\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>installing;smart tags\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	hd_id3563951				0	uz	\<variable id=\"smarttags\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/smarttags.xhp\"\>Using Smart Tags\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	par_id368358				0	uz	Smart Tags provide additional information and functionality to specified words in a Writer document. The available features can be different for different Smart Tags extensions.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	hd_id9298379				0	uz	Installing Smart Tags				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	par_id1827448				0	uz	Smart Tags can be supplied as \<link href=\"text/shared/01/packagemanager.xhp\"\>extensions\</link\> to %PRODUCTNAME Writer. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	par_id2508621				0	uz	To install a Smart Tag, do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	par_id3856013				0	uz	Save the *.oxt extension file to your harddrive, then double-click the *.oxt file in your file manager. Alternatively, in %PRODUCTNAME choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Extension Manager\</item\> to open the Extension Manager, click Add and browse to the file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	par_id7814264				0	uz	Click a Smart Tag *.oxt file link on a web page and open the link with the default application. This requires a properly configured Web browser.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	hd_id8142338				0	uz	Smart Tags menu				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	par_id192266				0	uz	When you point to a Smart Tag, a tip help informs you to Ctrl-click to open the Smart Tags menu. If you don't use a mouse, position the cursor inside the marked text and open the context menu by Shift+F10.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	par_id1998962				0	uz	In the Smart Tags menu you see the available actions that are defined for this Smart Tag. Choose an option from the menu. The \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Smart Tags Options\</item\> command opens the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/06040700.xhp\"\>Smart Tags\</link\> page of Tools - Autocorrect Options.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	hd_id2376476				0	uz	To enable and disable Smart Tags				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	par_id349131				0	uz	When you have installed at least one Smart Tags extension, you see the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/06040700.xhp\"\>Smart Tags\</link\> page in \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Autocorrect Options\</item\>. Use this dialog to enable or disable Smart Tags and to manage the installed tags.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	par_id1216467				0	uz	Text that is recognized as a Smart Tag is not checked by the automatic spellcheck.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
