helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\printer_tray.xhp	0	help	par_id3155858				0	uz	Use page styles to specify different paper sources for different pages in your document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\printer_tray.xhp	0	help	par_id3149841				0	uz	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\printer_tray.xhp	0	help	par_id3155066				0	uz	Right-click the page style in the list that you want to specify the paper source for, and then choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\printer_tray.xhp	0	help	par_id3153140				0	uz	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\printer_tray.xhp	0	help	par_id3149649				0	uz	Repeat steps 1-5 for each page style that you want to specify the paper for.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\printer_tray.xhp	0	help	par_id3149616				0	uz	Apply the page style to the pages that you want.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
