helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153880				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:LISTBOX:RID_SVXPAGE_INET_SEARCH:LB_SEARCH\"\>Displays the available search engines.\</ahelp\> Select a search engine to display its configuration in the adjacent text and option boxes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150276				0	uz	Name				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155449	12			0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:EDIT:RID_SVXPAGE_INET_SEARCH:ED_SEARCH_NAME\"\>Displays the name of the selected search engine.\</ahelp\> This is the name that will be shown in the sub-menu of the \<emph\>Search\</emph\> icon on the Hyperlink bar. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151245				0	uz	Type				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154758				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SVXPAGE_INET_SEARCH:RB_EXACT\"\>Sets the advanced search preferences (and, or, exact) as well as the way the results are defined and displayed.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148663				0	uz	The links \<emph\>And, Or\</emph\> and \<emph\>Exactly\</emph\> are available.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150358				0	uz	Prefix				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154138				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:EDIT:RID_SVXPAGE_INET_SEARCH:ED_URL\"\>This text box displays the URL and the first part of the query command for a search machine. A URL can also be typed directly.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153193				0	uz	Suffix				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153970				0	uz	The search terms are passed between the prefix and the suffix.\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:EDIT:RID_SVXPAGE_INET_SEARCH:ED_POSTFIX\"\>The suffix provides the command sequence, sent at the end of a search.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147086				0	uz	Separator				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150870				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:EDIT:RID_SVXPAGE_INET_SEARCH:ED_SEPARATOR\"\>If you type more than one word while running a search, these words will be separated by the character specified here.\</ahelp\> Most search engines require the "+" character.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149560				0	uz	To determine which prefixes, separators and suffixes to use when defining a new search engine:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3159255				0	uz	Activate the search engine and perform a search with at least two words.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147434				0	uz	Copy the URL from your browser's \<emph\>URL\</emph\> field and paste it into a blank document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148647				0	uz	Change the conditions for the search in the search engine, if it offers you the choice.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147317				0	uz	Again, copy the contents of the \<emph\>URL\</emph\> field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147213				0	uz	Compare the URLs with the sample URLs in the fields of this dialog and make a note of the prefixes, suffixes and separators used.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147348				0	uz	Case match				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154918				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:LISTBOX:RID_SVXPAGE_INET_SEARCH:ED_CASE\"\>Determines the case match for running a search.\</ahelp\> The list contains the following entries: \<emph\>None\</emph\>, \<emph\>Upper\</emph\> and \<emph\>Lower\</emph\>. The search terms entered are converted according to your selection.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149262				0	uz	Search engines handle queries differently according to the way they are constructed. For example, some are case sensitive and some are not. Because of this, it is best to select \<emph\>None\</emph\> as the case match option.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156283				0	uz	New				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149413				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:PUSHBUTTON:RID_SVXPAGE_INET_SEARCH:PB_NEW\"\>Use this button to include a new search engine.\</ahelp\>\<emph\>New\</emph\> deletes all important entries of the entry mask such as "Name" and "Suffix". Enter the new search engine together with all of the necessary details. As soon as you accept your entries with \<emph\>Add\</emph\>, the new search engine will appear in the search engine list under \<emph\>Search in\</emph\>. Close the dialog with the \<emph\>OK\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
