helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3153527				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_OPTIONS_LINGU\"\>Specifies the properties of the spellcheck, thesaurus and hyphenation.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149096				0	uz	Available Language Modules				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3154749				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_CLB_LINGU_MODULES\"\>Contains the installed language modules.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3153663	35			0	uz	A language module can contain one, two or three submodules: Spellcheck, hyphenation and thesaurus. Each sub-module can be available in one or more languages. If you click in front of the name of the module, you activate all the available sub-modules simultaneously. If you remove a set mark, you deactivate all the available sub-modules simultaneously. If you wish to activate or deactivate individual sub-modules, click the\<emph\> Edit button \</emph\>to open the \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010401.xhp\" name=\"Edit Modules\"\>\<emph\>Edit Modules\</emph\>\</link\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3294778				0	uz	The configuration allows for two different directories: one folder where the user has write permissions, and one without write permissions. The user can only edit and delete the user dictionaries that are located in the writable path. Other dictionaries can be read only.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154307				0	uz	Edit				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3145673	37			0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_PUSHBUTTON_RID_SFXPAGE_LINGU_PB_LINGU_MODULES_EDIT\"\>To edit a language module, select it and click \<emph\>Edit\</emph\>.\</ahelp\> The \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010401.xhp\" name=\"Edit Modules\"\>\<emph\>Edit \</emph\>\<emph\>Modules\</emph\>\</link\> dialog appears.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153348				0	uz	User-defined dictionaries				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3155419				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_CLB_EDIT_MODULES_DICS\"\>Lists the available user dictionaries.\</ahelp\> Mark the user dictionaries that you want to use for spellcheck and hyphenation.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144511				0	uz	New				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3146794				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_PUSHBUTTON_RID_SFXPAGE_LINGU_PB_LINGU_DICS_NEW_DIC\"\>Opens the \<emph\>New Dictionary\</emph\> dialog, in which you can name a new user-defined dictionary or dictionary of exceptions and specify the language.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151054				0	uz	New Dictionary				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3153360				0	uz	In the \<emph\>Dictionary\</emph\> section you can name a new user-defined dictionary or dictionary of exceptions and specify the language.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150398				0	uz	Name				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3153192				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:EDIT:RID_SFXDLG_NEWDICT:ED_DICTNAME\"\>Specifies the name of the new custom dictionary.\</ahelp\> The file extension "*.DIC" is automatically appended.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150767				0	uz	Language				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3148920				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:LISTBOX:RID_SFXDLG_NEWDICT:LB_DICTLANG\"\>By selecting a certain language you can limit the use of the custom dictionary.\</ahelp\> By selecting \<emph\>All\</emph\> the custom dictionary is used independently of the current language.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153106				0	uz	Exceptions (-)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3149561				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:CHECKBOX:RID_SFXDLG_NEWDICT:BTN_EXCEPT\"\>Specifies whether you wish to avoid certain words in your documents.\</ahelp\> In this way, you can create a custom dictionary of all the words to be avoided. If this exception dictionary is activated, during spellchecking you receive a corresponding note about any words which should be avoided.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145785				0	uz	Edit				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3152576				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_PUSHBUTTON_RID_SFXPAGE_LINGU_PB_LINGU_DICS_EDIT_DIC\"\>Opens the \<emph\>Edit custom dictionary\</emph\> dialog, in which you can add to your custom dictionary or edit existing entries.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3147436	75			0	uz	In the \<emph\>Edit custom dictionary \</emph\>dialog you have the option to enter new terms or edit existing entries. If you edit an exception dictionary, the dialog has the added facility of defining an exception for a word. During the spellcheck this exception is then listed as a suggestion.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3145750	76			0	uz	When a dictionary is edited, a check is made on the status of the file. If the file is write-protected, it cannot be changed. The buttons \<emph\>New\</emph\> and \<emph\>Delete\</emph\> are then deactivated. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150116				0	uz	Book				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3147394				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:LISTBOX:RID_SFXDLG_EDITDICT:LB_ALLDICTS\"\>Specifies the book to be edited.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3154730	79			0	uz	\<variable id=\"ignore\"\>The \<emph\>IgnoreAllList (All) \</emph\>includes all words that have been marked with \<emph\>Ignore\</emph\> during spellcheck. This list is valid only for the current spellcheck. \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3154757				0	uz	The \<emph\>IgnoreAllList\</emph\> entry cannot be selected and cannot be deleted. Only the words included as content can be deleted. This happens automatically each time that $[officename] is closed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149018				0	uz	Language				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3154255				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:LISTBOX:RID_SFXDLG_EDITDICT:LB_DICTLANG\"\>Assigns a new language to the current custom dictionary.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151189				0	uz	Word				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3151252				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:EDIT:RID_SFXDLG_EDITDICT:ED_WORD\"\>You can type a new word for inclusion in the dictionary. In the list below you will see the contents of the current custom dictionary.\</ahelp\> If you select a word from this list it is displayed in the text field. If you type a word with a trailing = character, such as "AutoComplete=", the word is never automatically hyphenated and no hyphenation is suggested. Typing "Auto=Complete" results in the word being hyphenated, or a hyphenation suggested, where you insert the = sign.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155175				0	uz	Suggestion				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3147323				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:EDIT:RID_SFXDLG_EDITDICT:ED_REPLACE\"\>This input field is only available if you are editing an exception dictionary. The field shows the alternative suggestion for the current word in the "Word" text box.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147361				0	uz	New				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3163808	89			0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:PUSHBUTTON:RID_SFXDLG_EDITDICT:PB_NEW_REPLACE\"\>Adds the word in the \<emph\>Word \</emph\>text field to your current custom dictionary. The word in the \<emph\>Suggestion \</emph\>field is also added when working with exception dictionaries.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3145790				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Removes the marked word from the current custom dictionary.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3151277				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Deletes the selected dictionary after a confirmation, provided it is not write-protected.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149032				0	uz	Options				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3145259				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_CLB_LINGU_OPTIONS\"\>Defines the options for the spellcheck and hyphenation.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149965				0	uz	Edit				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3153231				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_PUSHBUTTON_RID_SFXPAGE_LINGU_PB_LINGU_OPTIONS_EDIT\"\>If you want to change a value, select the entry and then click \<emph\>Edit\</emph\>.\</ahelp\> You will see a dialog for entering a new value.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150983				0	uz	Check uppercase words				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3152582				0	uz	Specifies that capitalization is checked during spellcheck.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150826				0	uz	Check words with numbers.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3150208				0	uz	Specifies that words that contain numbers as well as letters are to be checked.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147509				0	uz	Check capitalization				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3154200				0	uz	Checks for the correct use of capitals at the start of words during spellcheck.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166424				0	uz	Check special regions				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3150345				0	uz	Specifies that special regions, such as drawing text, are checked during spellcheck.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166429				0	uz	Check spelling as you type				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3155531				0	uz	\<variable id=\"automatisch\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:SpellOnline\"\>Automatically checks spelling as you type, and underlines errors.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3156291				0	uz	Typing errors are highlighted in the document with a red underline. If you place the cursor over a word marked in this way, you can open the context menu to obtain a list of corrections. Select a correction to replace the word. If you make the same mistake again while editing the document, it will be marked as an error again.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3153815				0	uz	To place the word pair in the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/06040200.xhp\" name=\"AutoCorrect replacement table\"\>AutoCorrect replacement table\</link\>, open the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/06040500.xhp\" name=\"AutoCorrect context menu\"\>AutoCorrect context menu\</link\> and choose \<emph\>AutoCorrect\</emph\>. Make your selection from the submenu. The word is replaced and at the same time the word pair is placed in the replacement table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150111	53			0	uz	Minimal number of characters for hyphenation 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3150316				0	uz	Specifies the minimum number of characters required for automatic hyphenation to be applied. \<ahelp hid=\"HID_LNGDLG_NUM_PREBREAK\" visibility=\"hidden\"\> Type the minimum number of characters that must come before or after the hyphen.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148823				0	uz	Characters before line break				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3156029				0	uz	Sets the minimum number of characters of the word to be hyphenated that must remain at the end of the line.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154956				0	uz	Characters after line break				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3149439				0	uz	Specifies the minimum number of characters of a hyphenated word required at the next line.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156337				0	uz	Hyphenate without inquiry				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3151130				0	uz	Specifies that you will never be asked for a manual hyphenation. If the field is not marked, when a word is not recognized you will be presented with a dialog for entering hyphens.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155900				0	uz	Hyphenate special regions				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3155098				0	uz	Specifies that hyphenation will also be carried out in footnotes, headers and footers.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Proxy				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147577				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>settings; proxies\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>proxy settings\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156414				0	uz	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01020100.xhp\" name=\"Proxy\"\>Proxy\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3145090				0	uz	\<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000002.xhp#proxy\" name=\"Proxy servers\"\>Proxy servers\</link\> for accessing the Internet can be set up manually as needed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147577				0	uz	Settings				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153748				0	uz	Defines the settings for the \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000002.xhp#proxy\" name=\"proxy server\"\>proxy server\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151110				0	uz	Proxy server				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147275				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:LISTBOX:RID_SVXPAGE_INET_PROXY:LB_PROXYMODE\"\>Specifies the type of proxy definition.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147574				0	uz	None				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148685				0	uz	Accesses the Internet without a proxy server. Allows you to set up a connection directly on your computer to an Internet provider that does not use a proxy.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150984				0	uz	Manual				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3156155				0	uz	Lets you enter the proxy server manually. Specify the proxy servers in accordance with your Internet service. Ask your system administrator for the proxies and ports to enter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148943				0	uz	Type server names without the protocol prefix. For example, type www.sun.com, not http://www.sun.com.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_idN10684				0	uz	System				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_idN10688				0	uz	On Windows or UNIX systems using GNOME or KDE, this option tells %PRODUCTNAME to use the system settings. You must restart %PRODUCTNAME to initiate this setting.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148948				0	uz	HTTP proxy				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154923				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:EDIT:RID_SVXPAGE_INET_PROXY:ED_HTTP_PROXY\"\>Type the name of the proxy server for \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000002.xhp#http\" name=\"HTTP\"\>HTTP\</link\>.\</ahelp\> Type the port in the right-hand field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id9971922				0	uz	HTTPS proxy				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id5319071				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Type the name of the proxy server for HTTPS. Type the port in the right-hand field.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150543				0	uz	FTP proxy				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154138				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_EDIT_RID_SVXPAGE_INET_PROXY_ED_FTP_PROXY\"\>Type the name of the proxy server for \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000002.xhp#ftp\" name=\"FTP\"\>FTP\</link\>.\</ahelp\> Type the port in the right-hand field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3125863				0	uz	No proxy for				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3151178				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:EDIT:RID_SVXPAGE_INET_PROXY:ED_NOPROXYFOR\"\>Specifies the names of the servers that do not require any proxy servers, separated by semicolons.\</ahelp\> These are servers addressed in your local network, and servers used for video and audio streaming, for example.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3145171				0	uz	You can also use placeholders for the names of hosts and domains. For example, type *.sun.com to address all the hosts in the sun.com domain without proxy.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149808				0	uz	Port				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153666				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:EDIT:RID_SVXPAGE_INET_PROXY:ED_SOCKS_PORT\"\>Type the port for the corresponding proxy server.\</ahelp\> The maximum value of a port number is fixed at 65535.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	View				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060100.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147242				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>cells; showing grid lines (Calc)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>borders; cells on screen (Calc)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>grids; displaying lines (Calc)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>colors; grid lines and cells (Calc)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>page breaks; displaying (Calc)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>guides; showing (Calc)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>handles; showing simple/large handles (Calc)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>displaying; zero values (Calc)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>zero values; displaying (Calc)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>displaying; notes (Calc)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>notes; displaying (Calc)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables in spreadsheets; value highlighting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; formatting without effect (Calc)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; coloring (Calc)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>anchors; displaying (Calc)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>colors;restriction (Calc)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text overflow in spreadsheet cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>references; displaying in color (Calc)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>objects; displaying in spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pictures; displaying in Calc\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>charts; displaying (Calc)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>draw objects; displaying (Calc)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>row headers; displaying (Calc)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>column headers; displaying (Calc)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>scrollbars; displaying (Calc)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheet tabs; displaying\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tabs; displaying sheet tabs\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>outlines;outline symbols\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150445				0	uz	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01060100.xhp\" name=\"View\"\>View\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153988				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SCPAGE_CONTENT\"\>Defines which elements of the \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc main window are displayed. You can also show or hide highlighting of values in tables.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
