helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010601.xhp	0	help	par_idN10566				0	uz	You can use this dialog to edit, to add, or to delete entries from the translation dictionary. The file path name for the translation dictionary is user/wordbook/commonterms.ctd. You cannot delete the default entries in this file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010601.xhp	0	help	par_idN10569				0	uz	Traditional Chinese to Simplified Chinese				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010601.xhp	0	help	par_idN1056D				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Translates traditional Chinese to simplified Chinese.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010601.xhp	0	help	par_idN10570				0	uz	Simplified Chinese to Traditional Chinese				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010601.xhp	0	help	par_idN10574				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Translates simplified Chinese to traditional Chinese.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010601.xhp	0	help	par_idN10577				0	uz	Reverse Mapping				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010601.xhp	0	help	par_idN1057B				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Automatically adds the reverse mapping direction to the list for each modification that you enter.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010601.xhp	0	help	par_idN1057E				0	uz	Term				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010601.xhp	0	help	par_idN10582				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Enter the text that you want to replace with the Mapping term.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010601.xhp	0	help	par_idN10585				0	uz	Mapping				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010601.xhp	0	help	par_idN10589				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Enter the text that you want to replace the Term with.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010601.xhp	0	help	par_idN1058C				0	uz	Property				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010601.xhp	0	help	par_idN10590				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Defines the class of the selected term.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010601.xhp	0	help	par_idN10593				0	uz	Add				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010601.xhp	0	help	par_idN10597				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Adds the term to the translation dictionary. If the term is already in the dictionary, the new term receives precedence.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010601.xhp	0	help	par_idN1059A				0	uz	Modify				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010601.xhp	0	help	par_idN1059E				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Saves the modified entry to the database file.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010601.xhp	0	help	par_idN105A1				0	uz	Delete				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010601.xhp	0	help	par_idN105A5				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Removes the selected user-defined entry from the dictionary.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Number Format Codes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153514				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>format codes; numbers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>conditions; in number formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>number formats; codes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>currency formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formats;of currencies/date/time\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>numbers; date, time and currency formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Euro; currency formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>date formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>times, formats\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153514				0	uz	\<variable id=\"zahlenformatcodes\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020301.xhp\" name=\"Number Format Codes\"\>Number Format Codes\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3150467				0	uz	Number format codes can consist of up to three sections separated by a semicolon (;).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3150146				0	uz	In a number format code with two sections, the first section applies to positive values and zero, and the second section applies to negative values.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3158442				0	uz	In a number format code with three sections, the first section applies to positive values, the second section to negative values, and the third section to the value zero.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3155069				0	uz	You can also assign conditions to the three sections, so that the format is only applied if a condition is met.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151262				0	uz	Decimal Places and Significant Digits				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3153624	3			0	uz	Use zero (0) or the number sign (#) as placeholders in your number format code to represent numbers. The (#) only displays significant digits, while the (0) displays zeroes if there are fewer digits in the number than in the number format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3153323				0	uz	Use question marks (?) to represent the number of digits to include in the numerator and the denominator of a fraction. Fractions that do not fit the pattern that you define are displayed as floating point numbers.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3148440				0	uz	If a number contains more digits to the right of the decimal delimiter than there are placeholders in the format, the number is rounded accordingly. If a number contains more digits to the left of the decimal delimiter than there are placeholders in the format, the entire number is displayed. Use the following list as a guide for using placeholders when you create a number format code:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3150902				0	uz	Placeholders				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3157896				0	uz	Explanation				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3152801				0	uz	#				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3145090				0	uz	Does not display extra zeros.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088				0	uz	0 (Zero)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3150774				0	uz	Displays extra zeros if the number has less places than zeros in the format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_idN1087E				0	uz	Examples				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3149182				0	uz	Number Format				2002-02-02 02:02:02
