helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06050600.xhp	0	help	par_id3158397				0	uz	Sets the indent, spacing, and alignment options for the numbered or bulleted list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06050600.xhp	0	help	par_id5004119				0	uz	The Position tab page looks different for documents using the new position and spacing attributes introduced with OpenOffice.org 3.0, or documents using the old attributes from versions before 3.0. The new version of this tab page shows the controls "Numbering followed by", "Numbering alignment", "Aligned at", and "Indent at". The old version of this tab page that can be seen in an old numbered or bulleted list shows the controls "Indent", "Width of numbering", "Minimum space numbering <-> text", and "Numbering alignment".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06050600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149031				0	uz	Level				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06050600.xhp	0	help	par_id3155755				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:MULTILISTBOX:TP_NUM_POSITION:LB_LEVEL\"\>Select the level(s) that you want to modify.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06050600.xhp	0	help	hd_id6561784				0	uz	Numbering followed by				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06050600.xhp	0	help	par_id423291				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Select the element that will follow the numbering: a tab stop, a space, or nothing.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06050600.xhp	0	help	hd_id7809686				0	uz	at				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06050600.xhp	0	help	par_id8177434				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>If you select a tab stop to follow the numbering, you can enter a non-negative value as the tab stop position.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06050600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155583				0	uz	Numbering alignment				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06050600.xhp	0	help	par_id3153063				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:TP_NUM_POSITION:LB_ALIGN\"\>Set the alignment of the numbering symbols. Select "Left" to align the numbering symbol to start directly at the "Aligned at" position. Select "Right" to align the symbol to end directly before the "Aligned at" position. Select "Centered" to center the symbol around the "Aligned at" position.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06050600.xhp	0	help	par_id3147422				0	uz	The \<emph\>Numbering alignment\</emph\> option does not set the alignment of the paragraph.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
