helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id1857051				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Choose a command to delete the current note, or all notes from the same author as the current note, or all notes in the document.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id4271370				0	uz	When the cursor is inside a note, you can press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command+Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl+Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Page Down to jump to the next note, or press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command+Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl+Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Page Up to jump to the previous note.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id2116153				0	uz	When the cursor is inside the normal text, press the above mentioned keys to jump to the next or previous note anchor. You can also use the small Navigation window below the vertical scrollbar to jump from one note anchor to the next note anchor.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id5381328				0	uz	You can also open the Navigator to see a list of all notes. Right-click a note name in the Navigator to edit or delete the note.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id5664235				0	uz	Edit comment				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3166460				0	uz	When you attach a note to a cell, a callout appears where you can enter your text. A small square in the upper right corner of a cell marks the position of a note. To display the note permanently, right-click the cell, and choose \<emph\>Show Note\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id8336741				0	uz	To change the object properties of a note, for example the background color, choose \<emph\>Show Note\</emph\> as above, then right-click the note (do not double-click the text).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155390				0	uz	To edit a shown note, double-click the note text. To edit a note that is not shown permanently, click in the cell that contains the note, and then choose \<emph\>Insert - Note\</emph\>. To specify the formatting of the note text, right-click the note text in edit mode.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_idN107A1				0	uz	To change the position or size of a note, drag a border or corner of the note. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id9499496				0	uz	To delete a note, right-click the cell, then choose \<emph\>Delete Note\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id2036805				0	uz	You can also right-click a note name in the Navigator window to choose some editing commands.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153716				0	uz	To set the printing options for notes in your spreadsheet, choose \<emph\>Format - Page\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Sheet\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
