helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05030500.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155855				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>shadows; borders\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>borders; shadows\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>margins; shadows\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05030500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155855				0	uz	Shadow style				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05030500.xhp	0	help	par_id3146975				0	uz	You can also apply a shadow effect to borders. For the best results, only apply this effect when all four borders are visible.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05030500.xhp	0	help	par_id3157309				0	uz	Graphics or objects that are anchored to a frame in the document cannot exceed the size of the frame. If you apply a shadow to the borders of an object that fills an entire frame, the size of the object is reduced to display the shadows.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
