helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3154763				0	uz	"$$$empty$$$"				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3151012				0	uz	An empty string ("ListBox1=")				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148901				0	uz	Empty string is NULL				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3145357				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_EMPTY_IS_NULL\"\>Defines how an empty string input should be handled. If set to Yes, an input string of length zero will be treated as a value NULL. If set to No, any input will be treated as-is without any conversion.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id0820200812403467				0	uz	An empty string is a string of length zero (""). Normally, a value NULL is not the same as an empty string. In general, a term NULL is used to denote an undefined value, an unknown value, or "no value has been entered yet."				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id0820200812403455				0	uz	Database systems vary and they might handle a value NULL differently. Refer to documentations of the database that you are using.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	hd_id3161653				0	uz	Filter proposal				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3151221	89			0	uz	\<variable id=\"filtervorschlag\"\>\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_FILTERPROPOSAL\"\>While designing your form, you can set the "Filter proposal" property for each text box in the \<emph\>Data\</emph\> tab of the corresponding \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> dialog. In subsequent searches in the filter mode, you can select from all information contained in these fields.\</ahelp\> The field content can then be selected using the AutoComplete function. Note, however, that this function requires a greater amount of memory space and time, especially when used in large databases and should therefore be used sparingly. \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_idN10EE3				0	uz	Linked cell				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_idN10EE7				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_BOUND_CELL\"\>Specifies the reference to a linked cell on a spreadsheet. The live state or contents of the control are linked to the cell contents.\</ahelp\> The following tables list the controls and their corresponding link type:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
