helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01110000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153539				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>printing; directly\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01110000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153539				0	uz	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01110000.xhp\" name=\"Print File Directly\"\>Print File Directly\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01110000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154398				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:PrintDefault\"\>Click the \<emph\>Print File Directly\</emph\> icon to print the active document with the current default print settings.\</ahelp\> These can be found in the \<emph\>Printer Setup\</emph\> dialog, which you can call with the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01140000.xhp\" name=\"Printer Settings\"\>\<emph\>Printer Settings\</emph\>\</link\> menu command.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01110000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147275	3			0	uz	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>If you select text or a graphic and click the \<emph\>Print File Direct\</emph\> icon, you are prompted to print the selection or the document. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01110000.xhp	0	help	par_id9547105				0	uz	If the current document uses a printer that is not the default printer for your operating system, the \<emph\>Print File Direct \</emph\>icon opens the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01130000.xhp\"\>\<emph\>Print\</emph\>\</link\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01110000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10679				0	uz	If the current document uses a printer that is not the default printer that was specified in the \<link href=\"text/shared/guide/spadmin.xhp\"\>spadmin\</link\>, printer administration program, the \<emph\>Print File Direct \</emph\>icon opens the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01130000.xhp\"\>\<emph\>Print\</emph\>\</link\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Setting Indents, Margins, and Columns				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148668				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>margins; setting with the mouse\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>columns; setting with the mouse\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>paragraphs; indents, margins and columns\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148668				0	uz	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/13020000.xhp\" name=\"Setting Indents, Margins, and Columns\"\>Setting Indents, Margins, and Columns\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155364				0	uz	You can define the indents and margins for the current paragraph, or for all selected paragraphs, using the mouse.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152594				0	uz	If you split the page into columns, or the cursor is placed in a multiple-column text frame, you can change the column width and the column spacing by dragging them on the ruler with the mouse.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154398				0	uz	When an object, an image, or a draw object is selected, you will see the borders of the object in the ruler. You can change the borders by dragging them on the ruler with the mouse.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146130				0	uz	If the cursor is placed in a table cell, you can change the indents for the contents of the cell by dragging them with the mouse on the ruler. You can change the boundary lines of the table on the ruler or by dragging the actual boundary line.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156136				0	uz	\<image id=\"img_id3153750\" src=\"res/helpimg/linleft.png\" width=\"0.1665inch\" height=\"0.2291inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3153750\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150693				0	uz	These icons mark the left indent for the first line of the current paragraph (top triangle) and the left indent for the other lines of the paragraph (bottom triangle).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150774				0	uz	\<image id=\"img_id3145071\" src=\"res/helpimg/linright.png\" width=\"0.3646inch\" height=\"0.2602inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3145071\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3166460				0	uz	This icon on the right of the ruler marks the right indent of the current paragraph.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146949				0	uz	\<emph\>Task\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153087				0	uz	\<emph\>Procedure\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154143				0	uz	Set left indent				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154307				0	uz	Drag the bottom left mark to the right while pressing the mouse button				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155449				0	uz	Set left indent of first line				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145673				0	uz	Drag the top left mark to the right while pressing the mouse button				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156156				0	uz	Set right indent				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153761				0	uz	Drag the mark on the right to the left while pressing the mouse button				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154760				0	uz	In order to change the left indent starting with the second line of a paragraph, hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key, click the triangle on the bottom left, and drag it to the right.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148453				0	uz	Tabs that have been set are not changed when indenting a paragraph. If the set tabs end up outside the margins of the paragraph, they are no longer displayed, but they still exist.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Form Navigator				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	bm_id3143284				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>controls;arranging in forms\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>forms;Navigator\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Form Navigator\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>subforms; creating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>controls; hidden\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hidden controls in Form Navigator\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143284				0	uz	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170600.xhp\" name=\"Form Navigator\"\>Form Navigator\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	par_id3149760				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ShowFmExplorer\"\>Opens the \<emph\>Form Navigator\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Form Navigator\</emph\> displays all forms and subforms of the current document with their respective controls.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	par_id3147399				0	uz	When using several forms, the Form Navigator gives an overview of all forms, and also provides various functions for editing them.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	par_id3155552				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FORM_NAVIGATOR\"\>The \<emph\>Form Navigator\</emph\> contains a list of all created (logical) forms with the corresponding control fields.\</ahelp\> You can see whether a form contains control fields by the plus sign displayed before the entry. Click the plus sign to open the list of the form elements.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	par_id3146957				0	uz	You can change how the different controls are arranged by dragging and dropping them in the \<emph\>Form Navigator\</emph\>. Select one or more controls and drag them into another form. Alternatively use \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+X or the context menu command \<emph\>Cut\</emph\> to move a control to the clipboard and \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+V or the command \<emph\>Insert\</emph\> to insert the control into another position.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	par_id3155892				0	uz	To edit the name in the \<emph\>Form Navigator\</emph\>, click on the name and enter a new name, or use the command in the context menu.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	par_id3156347				0	uz	If you select a control in the \<emph\>Form Navigator\</emph\>, the corresponding element is selected in the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	par_id3153662				0	uz	If you call the context menu of a selected entry, the \<emph\>Form Navigator\</emph\> offers the following functions:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153252				0	uz	New				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	par_id3153561	8			0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_NEW\"\>Adds new elements to the form. The\<emph\> Add \</emph\>function can only be called if a form is selected in the \<emph\>Form Navigator\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149763				0	uz	Form				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	par_id3156117	10			0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_NEW_FORM\"\>Creates a new form in the document. \</ahelp\> To create a \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170203.xhp\" name=\"subform\"\>subform\</link\>, add the new form under the desired parent form.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155342				0	uz	Hidden Control				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	par_id3158430				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_NEW_HIDDEN\"\>Creates a hidden control in the selected form that is not displayed on the screen. A hidden control serves to include data that is transmitted together with the form.\</ahelp\> It contains additional information or clarifying text that you can specify when creating the form through the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170101.xhp\" name=\"Special Properties\"\>Special Properties\</link\> of the control. Select the entry of the hidden control in the \<emph\>Form Navigator\</emph\> and select the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> command.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	par_id3159147				0	uz	You can copy controls in the document through the clipboard (shortcut keys \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+C for copying and \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+V for inserting). You can copy hidden controls in the \<emph\>Form Navigator\</emph\> by using drag-and-drop while keeping the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key pressed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	par_id3145068				0	uz	Drag and drop to copy controls within the same document or between documents. Open another form document and drag the hidden control from the \<emph\>Form Navigator\</emph\> into the \<emph\>Form Navigator\</emph\> of the target document. Click a visible control directly in the document, rest the mouse for a moment so that a copy of the control is added to the drag-and-drop clipboard, then drag the copy into the other document. If you want a copy in the same document, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>while dragging.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152812				0	uz	Delete				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	par_id3154938				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_DELETE\"\>Deletes the selected entry.\</ahelp\> This allows you to delete individual form components as well as whole forms with one mouse click.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153799				0	uz	Tab order				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	par_id3156282				0	uz	When a form is selected, it opens the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170300.xhp\" name=\"Tab Order\"\>\<emph\>Tab Order\</emph\>\</link\> dialog, where the indices for focusing the control elements on the Tab key are defined.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150869				0	uz	Rename				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	par_id3145607				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_RENAME_OBJECT\"\>Renames the selected object.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153194				0	uz	Properties				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	par_id3149766				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ShowPropertyBrowser\"\>Starts the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> dialog for the selected entry.\</ahelp\> If a form is selected, the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170200.xhp\" name=\"Form Properties\"\>Form Properties\</link\> dialog opens. If a control is selected, the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170100.xhp\" name=\"Control Properties\"\>Control Properties\</link\> dialog opens.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Format Paintbrush				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN1056A				0	uz	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/paintbrush.xhp\"\>Format Paintbrush\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN1057A				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>First select some text or an object, then click this icon. Then click on or drag across other text or click an object to apply the same formatting.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN10617				0	uz	Click the \<emph\>Format Paintbrush\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3610034\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_formatpaintbrush.png\" width=\"0.423cm\" height=\"0.423cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3610034\"\>{ENTER ALTERNATE DESCRIPTION HERE}\</alt\>\</image\> on the \<emph\>Standard\</emph\> toolbar. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
