helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000210.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156324				0	uz	Fit page to print range				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000210.xhp	0	help	par_id3158405	7			0	uz	If you select the \<emph\>Fit page to print range \</emph\>option, the \<emph\>Warning Print Options\</emph\> dialog will not appear in subsequent print runs of this document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000210.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156553				0	uz	Print on multiple pages				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000210.xhp	0	help	par_id3154823				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"SD:RADIOBUTTON:DLG_PRINT_WARNINGS:RBT_POSTER\"\>Specifies whether to distribute the printout on multiple pages.\</ahelp\> The print range will be printed on multiple pages.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000210.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147010				0	uz	Trim				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000210.xhp	0	help	par_id3151111				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"SD:RADIOBUTTON:DLG_PRINT_WARNINGS:RBT_CUT\"\>Specifies that anything extending beyond the maximum print range will be cut off and not included in the printing.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_specialchar.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Inserting Special Characters				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_specialchar.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154927				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>characters; special\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting; special characters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>special characters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text; inserting special characters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>accents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>compose key to insert special characters\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_specialchar.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154927				0	uz	\<variable id=\"insert_specialchar\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/insert_specialchar.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Special Characters\"\>Inserting Special Characters\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_specialchar.xhp	0	help	par_id3147576				0	uz	This function allows you to insert special characters, such as check marks, boxes, and telephone symbols, into your text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_specialchar.xhp	0	help	par_id3155535				0	uz	To view a selection of all characters, choose \<emph\>Insert - Special Character\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_specialchar.xhp	0	help	par_id3147275				0	uz	In the large selection field click the desired character or several characters in succession. The characters are displayed at the bottom of the dialog. When you close the dialog with \<emph\>OK\</emph\>, all displayed characters in the selected font are inserted in the current document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_specialchar.xhp	0	help	par_id3153031				0	uz	In any text input field (such as the input fields in the \<emph\>Find & Replace\</emph\> dialog) you can press Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+S to open the \<emph\>Special Characters\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_specialchar.xhp	0	help	par_id3155630				0	uz	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>At present there are three ways of entering letters with accents directly from the keyboard. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_specialchar.xhp	0	help	par_id3154897				0	uz	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>\<emph\>Sun Solaris:\</emph\> Using a Sun keyboard. First press the Compose key to the right of the space bar, then enter the first and second modifiers. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_specialchar.xhp	0	help	par_id3145315				0	uz	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>\<emph\>Linux / NetBSD:\</emph\> Using the dead-keys. In an xterm window first press the (´) or (`) key. The character should not appear on the screen. Now press a letter, such as "e". The e is given an accent, é or è. If not, then check in the XF86Config file if a "nodeadkeys" XkbdVariant has been loaded there and replace it. You may also have set the environment variable SAL_NO_DEADKEYS, which deactivates the dead-keys. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_specialchar.xhp	0	help	par_id3148943				0	uz	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>\<emph\>All Unix systems:\</emph\> (Alt Graph) as additional compose key. The (Alt Graph) key can work in $[officename] like the Compose key, if you set the environment variable SAL_ALTGR_COMPOSE. The (Alt Graph) key must trigger a mode_switch, so, for example, xmodmap -e "keysym Alt_R = Mode_switch" must be set. First press (Alt Graph), then the first modifier, then the second modifier. The characters are combined as described on a Solaris system in the file /usr/openwin/include/X11/Suncompose.h. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_specialchar.xhp	0	help	par_id3149047				0	uz	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/04100000.xhp\" name=\"Special Characters\"\>Special Characters\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_specialchar.xhp	0	help	par_id3153896				0	uz	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/06040200.xhp\" name=\"AutoCorrect\"\>AutoCorrect\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Opening Documents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147834				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>opening; documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>documents; opening\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>files; opening\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>loading; documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets;creating/opening\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>presentations;creating/opening\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>FTP; opening documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>new documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>empty documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text documents;creating/opening\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>drawings; creating/opening\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>HTML documents; new\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formulas; new\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147834				0	uz	\<variable id=\"doc_open\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/doc_open.xhp\" name=\"Opening Documents\"\>Opening Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147653				0	uz	Opening an existing document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id3149398				0	uz	Do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_idN107A9				0	uz	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Open\</item\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_idN107AF				0	uz	Click the \<emph\>Open\</emph\> icon on the Standard toolbar				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_idN107B2				0	uz	Press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+O 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id3150275				0	uz	The \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01020000.xhp\" name=\"Open\"\>Open\</link\> dialog appears.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id3149164				0	uz	Select the file you want to open and click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149234				0	uz	Restrict Files to Display				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id3150985				0	uz	To restrict the display of files in the \<emph\>Open\</emph\> dialog to a certain type select the corresponding \<emph\>File type\</emph\> from the list. Select \<emph\>All Files (*.*)\</emph\> to display all files.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	hd_id4651326				0	uz	Cursor Position				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id5509201				0	uz	In general, all documents open with the cursor at the start of the document. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id3422650				0	uz	Press Shift+F5 to set the cursor to the last saved position.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148453				0	uz	Opening an Empty Document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id3147287				0	uz	Click the \<emph\>New\</emph\> icon on the Standard bar or choose \<emph\>File - New\</emph\>. This opens a document of the document type specified.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id3153092				0	uz	If you click the arrow next to the \<emph\>New\</emph\> icon, a submenu opens in which you can select another document type.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	hd_id0820200803501358				0	uz	System File Dialogs or %PRODUCTNAME Dialogs				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id0820200803501356				0	uz	On most operating systems, you can choose to use the system file dialogs or %PRODUCTNAME dialogs.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id0820200803501449				0	uz	The %PRODUCTNAME dialogs support file download and upload using secure https connections.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	hd_id0820200803501453				0	uz	Opening Files from a Web Server				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id3153126	9			0	uz	You can enter a URL in the \<emph\>File name\</emph\> box of the \<emph\>Open\</emph\> dialogs. The URL must start with file:/// or ftp:// or http://. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id0820200803501548				0	uz	If you use the %PRODUCTNAME dialog, you can use the https:// prefix for a secure connection, and you can save a document on the web server.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_idN107C4				0	uz	When you open a file by a URL from the Windows file dialog, Windows will open a local copy of the file, located in the Internet Explorer cache. The %PRODUCTNAME file dialog opens a local copy of the file in the system's temp folder.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id3148616				0	uz	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01020000.xhp\" name=\"File - Open\"\>File - Open\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Recording and Displaying Changes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150499				0	uz	\<variable id=\"redlining\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/redlining.xhp\" name=\"Recording and Displaying Changes\"\>Recording and Displaying Changes\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	par_id4013794				0	uz	The review function is available in %PRODUCTNAME for text documents and spreadsheet documents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	par_id3153681				0	uz	When several authors are working on the same text or spreadsheet, the review function records and displays who made the various changes. On the final edit of the document, it is then possible to look at each individual change and decide whether it should be accepted or rejected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	par_id3147008				0	uz	For example: You are an editor and are delivering your latest report. But before publication the report must be read by the senior editor and the proofreader, and both will add their changes. The senior editor writes "clarify" after one paragraph and crosses out another entirely. The proofreader corrects the spelling of your document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	par_id3150774				0	uz	The edited document comes back to you, and you can incorporate or ignore the suggestions of the two reviewers.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	par_id3146957				0	uz	Let's say you also e-mailed a copy of the report to a good friend and colleague who has done research on a similar topic in the past. You asked for a few suggestions, and the document is now returned by e-mail with your colleague's suggestions.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088				0	uz	As all your colleagues and the managers in your company work with $[officename], you can produce a final version of the document from the results you get back.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\email.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Sending Documents as E-mail				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\email.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153345				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>documents; sending as e-mail\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sending; documents as e-mail\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>e-mail attachments\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>files; sending as e-mail\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text documents;sending as e-mail\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; sending as e-mail\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>drawings; sending as e-mail\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>presentations; sending as e-mail\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>attachments in e-mails\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\email.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153345				0	uz	\<variable id=\"email\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/email.xhp\" name=\"Sending Documents as E-mail\"\>Sending Documents as E-mail\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\email.xhp	0	help	par_id3154897				0	uz	Working in $[officename], you can send the current document as an e-mail attachment.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\email.xhp	0	help	par_id3147335				0	uz	Choose \<emph\>File - Send - Document as E-mail\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\email.xhp	0	help	par_id3153127				0	uz	$[officename] opens your default e-mail program.\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\> If you want to send the current document with another e-mail program, you can select the program to use with \<emph\>Tools - Options - Internet - E-mail\</emph\>. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\email.xhp	0	help	par_id3150986				0	uz	In your e-mail program, enter the recipient, subject and any text you want to add, then send the e-mail.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\email.xhp	0	help	par_id3595385				0	uz	In case you want to send the e-mail to a recipient who only has software that cannot read the OpenDocument format, you can send the current document in an often used proprietary format.\<br/\>For a text document, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Send - Document as Microsoft Word\</item\>. For a spreadsheet, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Send - Document as Microsoft Excel\</item\>. And for a presentation, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Send - Document as Microsoft PowerPoint\</item\>. \<br/\>If you want to send the document as a read-only file, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Send - Document as PDF\</item\>.\<br/\>These commands do not change your current document. Only a temporary copy is created and sent.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\change_title.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Changing the Title of a Document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\change_title.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156324				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>titles; changing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing;document titles\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>documents; changing titles\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\change_title.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156324				0	uz	\<variable id=\"change_title\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/change_title.xhp\" name=\"Changing the Title of a Document\"\>Changing the Title of a Document\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\change_title.xhp	0	help	par_id3152801				0	uz	You can specify a title for your document. Some file manager utilities can display the titles next to the filenames of your documents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\change_title.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156136				0	uz	How to change the title of the current document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\change_title.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345				0	uz	Choose \<emph\>File - Properties\</emph\>. This opens the \<emph\>Properties of\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\change_title.xhp	0	help	par_id3156410				0	uz	Select the \<emph\>Description\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\change_title.xhp	0	help	par_id3147242				0	uz	Type the new title in the \<emph\>Title\</emph\> box and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\change_title.xhp	0	help	par_id3163802				0	uz	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01100000.xhp\" name=\"Properties of\"\>Properties of\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Working With %PRODUCTNAME XML Filters 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	bm_id7007583				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>saving;to XML\</bookmark_value\> \<bookmark_value\>loading;XML files\</bookmark_value\> \<bookmark_value\>importing;from XML\</bookmark_value\> \<bookmark_value\>exporting;to XML\</bookmark_value\> \<bookmark_value\>file filters;XML\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>XSLT filters, see also XML filters\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10923				0	uz	\<variable id=\"xsltfilter\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/xsltfilter.xhp\"\>About XML Filters\</link\> \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10927				0	uz	%PRODUCTNAME \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000021.xhp\"\>stores documents in XML format\</link\>. You can create customized filters that convert the native OpenDocument XML file format used by %PRODUCTNAME into another format. These filters can be integrated into %PRODUCTNAME seamlessly so that you can save or load these formats transparently.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN1093A				0	uz	To create an XML filter, you must have a good understanding of XML and XSLT concepts. These concepts are beyond the scope of this help.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN1093D				0	uz	An XML filter contains \<emph\>stylesheets\</emph\> that are written in the XSLT language. The stylesheets define the transformation from the OpenDocument file format to another XML format through export and import filters. There are three types of XML filters:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10947				0	uz	 \<emph\>Import Filters\</emph\> load external XML files and transform the format of the files into the OpenDocument XML file format. After you install an import filter, the name of the filter is added to the list of file types in the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01020000.xhp\"\>File Open dialog\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10960				0	uz	 \<emph\>Export Filters\</emph\> transform OpenDocument XML files and \<emph\>save\</emph\> the files to a different XML format. After you install an export filter, the name of the filter is added to the list of file types in the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01070001.xhp\"\>Export dialog\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10979				0	uz	 \<emph\>Import/Export Filters\</emph\> load and save OpenDocument XML files into a different XML \<emph\>format\</emph\>. After you install these filters, the names of the filters are added to the list of file types in the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01020000.xhp\"\>File Open dialog\</link\> and the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01070000.xhp\"\>File Save As dialog\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B39				0	uz	\<link href=\"http://www.w3.org/Style/XSL/\"\>World Wide Web Consortium Pages on Extensible \<emph\>Stylesheet\</emph\> Language (XSL)\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B4E				0	uz	\<link href=\"http://www.w3.org/XML/\"\>World Wide Web Consortium Pages on Extensible Markup Language (XML)\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10D97				0	uz	 \<embedvar href=\"text/shared/00/00000021.xhp#xmlformat\"/\> 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_id5569017				0	uz	\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/xsltfilter_distribute.xhp\"\>Distributing XML filters\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_id6426892				0	uz	\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/xsltfilter_create.xhp\"\>Creating and Testing XML filters\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
