helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1070A				0	uz	\<variable id=\"scripting\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/scripting.xhp\"\>Assigning Scripts in %PRODUCTNAME\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10728				0	uz	You can assign custom scripts (macros) to menu items, icons, dialog controls, and events in %PRODUCTNAME.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1072B				0	uz	%PRODUCTNAME internally supports the following scripting languages:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10731				0	uz	%PRODUCTNAME Basic				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10739				0	uz	JavaScript				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1073D				0	uz	BeanShell				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1091F				0	uz	In addition, developers can use high-level languages, for example Java programming language, to control %PRODUCTNAME externally. See the API project at OpenOffice.org.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10751				0	uz	To assign a script to a new menu entry				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10758				0	uz	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Customize\</emph\>, and click the \<emph\>Menus\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1093D				0	uz	Click \<emph\>Add\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10760				0	uz	In the \<emph\>Category\</emph\> list box, scroll down and open the "%PRODUCTNAME Macros" entry.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10768				0	uz	You see entries for "%PRODUCTNAME Macros" (scripts in the share directory of your %PRODUCTNAME installation), "My Macros" (scripts in the user directory), and the current document. Open any one of them to see the supported scripting languages.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1076C				0	uz	Open any scripting language entry to see the available scripts. Select a script.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10770				0	uz	A list of the script functions appears in the \<emph\>Functions\</emph\> list box. Select a function.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10783				0	uz	To assign a script to a key combination				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10787				0	uz	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Customize - Keyboard\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A59				0	uz	In the \<emph\>Category\</emph\> list box, scroll down and open the "%PRODUCTNAME Macros" entry.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A61				0	uz	You see entries for "%PRODUCTNAME Macros" (scripts in the share directory of your %PRODUCTNAME installation), "My Macros" (scripts in the user directory), and the current document. Open any one of them to see the supported scripting languages.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A65				0	uz	Open any scripting language entry to see the available scripts. Select any script.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A69				0	uz	A list of the script functions will appear in the \<emph\>Functions\</emph\> list box. Select any function.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A71				0	uz	Click the option button for %PRODUCTNAME or Writer (or whichever application is currently open). 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A74				0	uz	Selecting the option button sets the scope of the new key combination to be applicable in all of %PRODUCTNAME or only in documents of the current module.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A78				0	uz	Select a key combination from the \<emph\>Shortcut keys\</emph\> list box and click \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
