helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A9E				0	uz	In the \<emph\>Library\</emph\> list box, scroll down and open the "%PRODUCTNAME Macros" entry.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10AA6				0	uz	You see entries for "%PRODUCTNAME Macros" (scripts in the share directory of your %PRODUCTNAME installation), "My Macros" (scripts in the user directory), and the current document. Open any one of them to see the supported scripting languages.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10AAA				0	uz	Open any scripting language entry to see the available scripts. Select any script.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10AAE				0	uz	A list of the script functions will appear in the \<emph\>Assigned Macros\</emph\> list box. Select any function.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10AB6				0	uz	Select to save in %PRODUCTNAME or current document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10AB9				0	uz	This sets the scope of the new event assignment to be applicable in all of %PRODUCTNAME or only in documents of the current module.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10ABD				0	uz	Select an event from the list and click \<emph\>Assign\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10791				0	uz	To assign a script to an event for an embedded object				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10795				0	uz	Select the embedded object, for example a chart, in your document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10ADB				0	uz	Choose \<emph\>Format - Frame/Object - Macro\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10ADF				0	uz	In the \<emph\>Macros\</emph\> list box, open the %PRODUCTNAME Scripts entry.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10AE7				0	uz	You see entries for share (scripts in the share directory of your %PRODUCTNAME installation), user (scripts in the user directory), and the current document. Open any one of them to see the supported scripting languages.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10AEB				0	uz	Open any scripting language entry to see the available scripts. Select any script.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10AEF				0	uz	A list of the script functions will appear in the \<emph\>Existing macros in\</emph\> list box. Select any function.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10AF7				0	uz	Select an event from the list and click \<emph\>Assign\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10798				0	uz	To assign a script to a hyperlink				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1079C				0	uz	Position the cursor inside the hyperlink. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B15				0	uz	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Hyperlink\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B19				0	uz	Click the \<emph\>Events\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B21				0	uz	Select and assign as stated above.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
