helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN107A6				0	uz	To assign a script to a form control				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN107AA				0	uz	Insert a form control, for example a button: Open the Form Controls toolbar, click the \<emph\>Push Button\</emph\> icon, drag open a button on your document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B59				0	uz	With the form control selected, click \<emph\>Control\</emph\> on the Form Controls toolbar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B5D				0	uz	Click the \<emph\>Events\</emph\> tab of the Properties dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B61				0	uz	Click one of the \<emph\>...\</emph\> buttons to open a dialog where you can assign a script to the selected event.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN107AD				0	uz	To assign a script to a control in the %PRODUCTNAME Basic dialog				2002-02-02 02:02:02
