helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id2761314				0	uz	An easy method to import and export database tables uses Calc as a "helper application".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	hd_id3912778				0	uz	Exporting data from Base				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id3163853				0	uz	You copy a table from Base to a new Calc sheet, then you can save or export the data to any file format that Calc supports.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id121158				0	uz	Open the database file that contains the database table to be exported. Click Tables to view the tables, or click Queries to view the queries.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id4644306				0	uz	Choose \<emph\>File - New - Spreadsheet\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id1331217				0	uz	In the Base window, right-click the name of the table to export. Choose \<emph\>Copy\</emph\> from the context menu.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id3806878				0	uz	Click cell A1 in the new Calc window, then choose \<emph\>Edit - Paste\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id130619				0	uz	Now you can save or export the data to many file types.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	hd_id9999694				0	uz	Importing data to Base				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id8494521				0	uz	You can import text files, spreadsheet files, and your system address book in read-only mode only. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id9579760				0	uz	When you import from a text or spreadsheet file, the file must have a first row of header information. The second row of the file is the first valid data row. The format of every field in the second row determines the format for the entire column. Any format information from a spreadsheet file gets lost when importing to Base.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id325632				0	uz	For example, to ensure the first column has a text format, you must make sure that the first field of the first valid data row contains text. If a field in the first valid data row contains a number, the whole column is set to number format, and only numbers, no text, will be shown in that column. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id2216559				0	uz	Open a Base file of the database type that you want. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id7869502				0	uz	Either create a new Base file using the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/dabawiz00.xhp\"\>Database Wizard\</link\>, or open any existing Base file that is not read-only.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id9852900				0	uz	Open the Calc file that contains the data to be imported to Base. You can open a *.dbf dBASE file or many other file types. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id3791924				0	uz	Select the data to be copied to Base. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id6173894				0	uz	You can enter a range reference like A1:X500 in the Name Box if you don't want to scroll.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id533768				0	uz	If you copy a dBASE sheet, include the top row that contains the header data.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id5669423				0	uz	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Copy\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id3619495				0	uz	In the Base window, click \<emph\>Tables\</emph\> to view the tables.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id1175572				0	uz	In the Base window, choose \<emph\>Edit - Paste\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id4815820				0	uz	You see the Copy Table dialog. Most databases need a primary key, so you may want to check the \<emph\>Create primary key\</emph\> box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id2584002				0	uz	On Windows systems, you can also use drag-and-drop instead of Copy and Paste. Also, for registered databases, you can open the datasource browser (press F4) instead of opening the Base window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id5871761				0	uz	\<embedvar href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/main.xhp#base\"/\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
