helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Working with Queries				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	bm_id840784				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>databases;creating queries\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>filtering;data in databases\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>queries;defining (Base)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defining;queries (Base)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>wizards;database queries\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Query Wizard (Base)\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	par_idN105F9				0	uz	\<variable id=\"data_queries\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_queries.xhp\"\>Working with Queries\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	par_idN10617				0	uz	If you often want to access only a subset of your data that can be well defined by a filter condition, you can define a query. This is basically a name for the new view at the filtered data. You open the query and see the current data in the table layout that you defined.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	par_idN1061A				0	uz	Creating a New Query With the Query Wizard				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	par_idN1061E				0	uz	In %PRODUCTNAME you can create a new query using the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/querywizard00.xhp\"\>Query Wizard\</link\>:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	par_idN10632				0	uz	Open the database file where you want to create the new query.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	par_idN10636				0	uz	In the left pane of the database window, click the \<emph\>Queries\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	par_idN1063E				0	uz	Click \<emph\>Use Wizard to Create Query\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	par_idN10645				0	uz	Creating a New Query With the Design View				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	par_idN1064C				0	uz	Open the database file where you want to create the new query.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	par_idN10650				0	uz	In the left pane of the database window, click the \<emph\>Queries\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	par_idN10658				0	uz	Click \<emph\>Create Query in Design View\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	par_idN1065F				0	uz	You see the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/02010100.xhp\"\>Query Design window\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	par_idN1067B				0	uz	\<embedvar href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/main.xhp#base\"/\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
