helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3153915				0	uz	-display {display}				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3146786	46			0	uz	Sets the \<emph\>DISPLAY \</emph\>environment variable on UNIX based platforms to the value \<emph\>{display}\</emph\>. This parameter is only supported by the start script for the $[officename] software on UNIX based platforms.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3149595				0	uz	-headless				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3150530				0	uz	Starts in "headless mode" which allows using the application without user interface.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3156353				0	uz	This special mode can be used when the application is controlled by external clients via the \<link href=\"http://api.openoffice.org\" name=\"API\"\>API\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Registering an Address Book				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152823				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>data sources; registering address books\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>address books; registering\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>system address book registration\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>registering; address books\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154228				0	uz	\<variable id=\"data_addressbook\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_addressbook.xhp\" name=\"Registering an Address Book\"\>Registering an Address Book\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3154927				0	uz	In \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> you can register different data sources. The contents of the data fields are then available to you for use in various fields and controls. Your system address book is such a data source.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3149346				0	uz	\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> templates and wizards use fields for the contents of the address book. When activated, the general fields in the templates are automatically replaced with the fields from the data source of your address book.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3147399				0	uz	In order for the replacement to take place, you must tell \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> which address book you use. The wizard asking for this information appears automatically the first time you activate, for example, a business letter template. You can also call the wizard by following the steps listed below.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id5941648				0	uz	The address book data is read-only in %PRODUCTNAME Base. It is not possible to add, edit, or delete address data from within Base.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149096				0	uz	Address Data Source Wizard				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3147008				0	uz	To call the \<link href=\"text/shared/autopi/01170000.xhp\" name=\"Address Data Source\"\>Address Data Source\</link\> wizard, choose \<emph\>File - Wizards - Address Data Source\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149811				0	uz	Registering An Existing Address Book Manually				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3150771				0	uz	Choose \<emph\>File - Templates - Address Book Source\</emph\>. The \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01110101.xhp\" name=\"Templates: Address Book Assignment\"\>\<emph\>Templates: Address Book Assignment\</emph\>\</link\> dialog appears.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3148491				0	uz	In the \<emph\>Data source\</emph\> combo box, select the system address book or the data source you want to use as an address book.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3149669	11			0	uz	If you have not yet registered the system address book in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> as the data source, click the \<emph\>Configure\</emph\> button. This takes you to the \<emph\>Address Book Data Source Wizard\</emph\>, in which you can register your address book as a new data source in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3154365				0	uz	In the \<emph\>Table\</emph\> combo box, select the database table you want to use as the address book.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3147084				0	uz	Under \<emph\>Field assignment\</emph\>, match the fields for first name, company, department, and so on to the actual field names used in your address book.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_idN10784				0	uz	When finished, close the dialog with \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3149983				0	uz	Now your data source is registered in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> as the address book. If you now open a template from the \<emph\>Business Correspondence\</emph\> category, \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> can automatically insert the correct fields for a form letter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_save.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Saving Documents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_save.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147226				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>documents; saving\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>saving; documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>backups; documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>files; saving\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text documents; saving\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; saving\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>drawings; saving\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>presentations; saving\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>FTP; saving documents\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_save.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147226				0	uz	\<variable id=\"doc_save\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/doc_save.xhp\" name=\"Saving Documents\"\>Saving Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_save.xhp	0	help	par_id3156113				0	uz	Click the \<emph\>Save\</emph\> icon or press the shortcut keys \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+S.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_save.xhp	0	help	par_id3155450				0	uz	\<image id=\"img_id3152349\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_save.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3152349\"\>This icon is for tips on how to use the program more effectively.\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_save.xhp	0	help	par_id3148685				0	uz	The document is saved under its path and name on the current local data medium or network drive or on the Internet, overwriting any file of the same name.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_save.xhp	0	help	par_id3150984				0	uz	When you save a new file for the first time, the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01070000.xhp\" name=\"Save As\"\>Save As\</link\> dialog opens, in which you can enter a name, folder and drive or volume for the file. To open this dialog, choose \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_save.xhp	0	help	hd_id7146824				0	uz	Automatic extension to the file name				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_save.xhp	0	help	par_id9359111				0	uz	When saving a file, %PRODUCTNAME always appends an extension to the file name, except when the file name already has an extension that matches the file type. See the list of \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000021.xhp\"\>ODF extensions\</link\>. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_save.xhp	0	help	par_id6709494				0	uz	Some examples for the automatic extensions are listed in the following table:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_save.xhp	0	help	par_id9009674				0	uz	You enter this file name				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_save.xhp	0	help	par_id485549				0	uz	You select this file type				2002-02-02 02:02:02
