helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Working with Tables				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	bm_id1983703				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>tables in databases;creating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>databases;creating tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>table views of databases\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN105F9				0	uz	\<variable id=\"data_tables\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_tables.xhp\"\>Working with Tables\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10617				0	uz	Data is stored in tables. As an example, your system address book that you use for your e-mail addresses is a table of the address book database. Each address is a data record, presented as a row in that table. The data records consist of data fields, for example the first and the last name fields and the e-mail field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN1061A				0	uz	Creating a New Table With the Table Wizard				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN1061E				0	uz	In %PRODUCTNAME you can create a new table using the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/tablewizard00.xhp\"\>Table Wizard\</link\>:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10632				0	uz	Open the database file where you want to create the new table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10636				0	uz	In the left pane of the database window, click the \<emph\>Tables\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN1063E				0	uz	Click \<emph\>Use Wizard to Create Table\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10645				0	uz	Creating a New Table With the Design View				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN1064C				0	uz	Open the database file where you want to create the new table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10650				0	uz	In the left pane of the database window, click the \<emph\>Tables\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10658				0	uz	Click \<emph\>Create Table in Design View\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN1065F				0	uz	You see the \<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_tabledefine.xhp\"\>Table Design\</link\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10778				0	uz	Creating a New Table View				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN1077C				0	uz	Some database types support table views. A table view is a query that is stored with the database. For most database operations, a view can be used as you would use a table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10782				0	uz	Open the database file where you want to create the new table view.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10786				0	uz	In the left pane of the database window, click the \<emph\>Tables\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN1078E				0	uz	Click \<emph\>Create Table View\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10795				0	uz	You see the View Design window, which is almost the same as the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/02010100.xhp\"\>Query Design window\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
