helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Comparing Versions of a Document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154788				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>documents; comparing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>comparisons;document versions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>versions; comparing documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changes;comparing to original\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>review function; comparing documents\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154788				0	uz	\<variable id=\"redlining_doccompare\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/redlining_doccompare.xhp\" name=\"Comparing Versions of a Document\"\>Comparing Versions of a Document\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	par_id4186223				0	uz	The review function is available in %PRODUCTNAME for text documents and spreadsheet documents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	par_id3995178				0	uz	Imagine you have some co-authors or reviewers who collaborate with you writing your original document. One day you send out copies of your document to all reviewers. You ask them to edit the copy and send it back.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	par_id9948423				0	uz	Normally, the reviewers enable change tracking by \<emph\>Edit - Changes - Record\</emph\> and you can easily see the changes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	par_id3155421				0	uz	If one of the authors has made changes to a document without recording them, you can compare the changed document to your original document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	par_id3153087				0	uz	Open the reviewer's document and then choose \<emph\>Edit - Compare Document\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	par_id4208807				0	uz	You should always start with opening the newer document and compare it with the older document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	par_id3145315				0	uz	A file selection dialog appears. Select your older original document and confirm the dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	par_id3149762				0	uz	\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> combines both documents into the reviewer's document. All text passages that occur in the reviewer's document but not in the original are identified as having been inserted, and all text passages that got deleted by the reviewer are identified as deletions.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	par_id3145674				0	uz	You can now accept or reject the insertions and deletions. At the end you may save the reviewer's document as a new original with a new name.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\breaking_lines.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Inserting Line Breaks in Cells				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\breaking_lines.xhp	0	help	bm_id6305734				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>line breaks; in cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; line breaks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text flow; in cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text breaks in cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>wrapping text; in cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>words; wrapping in cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>automatic line breaks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>new lines in cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;line breaks in cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables;inserting line breaks\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\breaking_lines.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D5				0	uz	\<variable id=\"breaking_lines\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/breaking_lines.xhp\"\>Inserting Line Breaks in Cells\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\breaking_lines.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D9				0	uz	Inserting line breaks in $[officename] Calc spreadsheet cells				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\breaking_lines.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E0				0	uz	To insert a line break in a spreadsheet cell, press the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Enter keys. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\breaking_lines.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E3				0	uz	This will work only with the text edit cursor inside the cell, not at the input line. So first double-click the cell, then single-click at the text position where you want the line break.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\breaking_lines.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E6				0	uz	Formatting $[officename] Calc cells for automatic line wrapping				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\breaking_lines.xhp	0	help	par_idN106ED				0	uz	Select the cells for which you want an automatic line break.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\breaking_lines.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F1				0	uz	Choose \<emph\>Format - Cells - Alignment\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\breaking_lines.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F9				0	uz	Select \<emph\>Wrap text automatically\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\breaking_lines.xhp	0	help	par_idN10700				0	uz	Inserting line breaks in $[officename] Writer text document tables				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\breaking_lines.xhp	0	help	par_idN10707				0	uz	To insert a line break in a text document table cell, press the Enter key.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\breaking_lines.xhp	0	help	par_idN1070A				0	uz	An automatic line break will be performed while you type across the end of each cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\breaking_lines.xhp	0	help	par_idN10718				0	uz	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05340300.xhp\"\>Alignment\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
