helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_doctypes.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143267				0	uz	\<variable id=\"ms_doctypes\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/ms_doctypes.xhp\" name=\"Changing the Association of Microsoft Office Document Types\"\>Changing the Association of Microsoft Office Document Types\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_doctypes.xhp	0	help	par_id3152780				0	uz	To change the association of Microsoft Office file name extensions to open the files either in $[officename] or in Microsoft Office, using Microsoft Windows:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_doctypes.xhp	0	help	par_id0815200803314147				0	uz	In Windows Explorer, right-click a file of the type that you want to assign to another application.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_doctypes.xhp	0	help	par_id0815200803314268				0	uz	In the context menu, choose "Open with..."				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_doctypes.xhp	0	help	par_id0815200803314245				0	uz	In the list of applications, select the program that should open the current type of files. Make sure that "Always use this program" is selected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_doctypes.xhp	0	help	par_id0815200803314243				0	uz	If these steps do not apply to your brand of Microsoft Windows, search your Microsoft Windows Help for instructions how to change the file associations.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
