helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153910				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>hyperlinks; editing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>links; editing hyperlinks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing; hyperlinks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text attributes; hyperlinks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>buttons;editing hyperlink buttons\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>URL;changing hyperlink URLs\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153910				0	uz	\<variable id=\"hyperlink_edit\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/hyperlink_edit.xhp\" name=\"Editing Hyperlinks\"\>Editing Hyperlinks\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id4124881				0	uz	When you \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>-click a hyperlink in a Writer document, your web browser opens with the requested web address. If you don't use a mouse, position the cursor inside the hyperlink and open the context menu by Shift+F10, then choose Open Hyperlink.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145071				0	uz	Change the text of a hyperlink as follows				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3166410	12			0	uz	In Writer documents, you can click anywhere into a hyperlink and edit the visible text. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id2690511				0	uz	If you leave the hyperlink by positioning the cursor somewhere else, only the visible text will be changed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id1983092				0	uz	If you leave the hyperlink by entering a space character directly following the last character, the AutoCorrect - if enabled - will change the target URL to be the same as the visible text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id333262				0	uz	In all document types, you can open the Hyperlink dialog to edit a hyperlink. First set the cursor into the hyperlink or directly in front of the hyperlink, then click the Hyperlink icon on the Standard bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158432				0	uz	Change the URL of a hyperlink as follows				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3150503				0	uz	Option 1: As described above, open \<link href=\"text/shared/02/09070000.xhp\" name=\"Hyperlink Dialog\"\>Hyperlink Dialog\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3145119				0	uz	Option 2: Open \<link href=\"text/shared/main0209.xhp\" name=\"Hyperlink Bar\"\>Hyperlink Bar\</link\> (\<emph\>View - Toolbars - Hyperlink Bar\</emph\>). Click on the hyperlink, do not release the mouse button and drag the hyperlink to the Hyperlink Bar. Edit the URL on the Hyperlink Bar and press the Return key.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148686				0	uz	Change the attribute of all hyperlinks				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3148943				0	uz	Open the Styles and Formatting window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_idN10826				0	uz	Click the Character Styles icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_idN1082C				0	uz	Right-click the "Internet Link" or "Visited Internet Link" character style, and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_idN10834				0	uz	In the dialog, select the new attributes, and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147530				0	uz	Edit a hyperlink button				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3152361				0	uz	If the hyperlink is a button, click on the border to select it, or press the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key while clicking. Open the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> dialog through the context menu. You can edit the label text under "Caption," and modify the address in the "URL" field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Changing Default Templates				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154285				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>modifying, see changing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing, see also editing and replacing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>default templates; changing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defaults;documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>custom templates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>updating; templates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing;templates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>templates;editing and saving\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>saving;templates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>resetting;templates\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154285				0	uz	\<variable id=\"standard_template\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/standard_template.xhp\" name=\"Changing Default Templates\"\>Changing Default Templates\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3152811				0	uz	When you open a new document with \<emph\>File - New\</emph\>, a blank document appears based on a $[officename] template. You can edit, modify, or replace this template so that the new document contains your customized Styles or other contents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150792				0	uz	Modifying Default Templates				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3154365				0	uz	First, open either an existing $[officename] template and modify it, or open a new document and edit it as necessary to create the desired template.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3159152				0	uz	You can define a document template for each $[officename] module. The following describes how to proceed for text documents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3145748	8			0	uz	Save the document by choosing\<emph\> File\</emph\> -\<emph\> Templates - Save \</emph\>and saving the document in the \<emph\>My Templates\</emph\> category.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3154011				0	uz	Choose \<emph\>File - Templates - Organize\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3146901				0	uz	Choose \<emph\>Set As Default Template\</emph\>. The next time you open a new text document, the new document will be based on the new default template.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153947				0	uz	Resetting Default Templates				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3156276				0	uz	To reset the modified text template to the original default template:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3146792				0	uz	Choose \<emph\>File - Templates - Organize\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3153714				0	uz	Open the context menu and choose \<emph\>Reset default template\</emph\>. In the submenu, select the document type whose default setting you want to restore. Thereafter, when you open an empty text document, it will again correspond to the $[officename] default template for text documents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153764				0	uz	Using Custom Templates				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3150386	14			0	uz	There are several ways to make your work easier by using your own custom templates. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149109				0	uz	Templates in the Template Folder				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3155960				0	uz	You may need to update the view of the templates in the dialog before you can see a newly created template. In this case, choose \<emph\>File - Templates - Organize\</emph\> and in the submenu of the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> button, choose \<emph\>Update\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3147343				0	uz	To open the template for editing, choose \<emph\>File - Templates - Edit\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
