helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Copying Attributes With the Format Paintbrush				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN1053A				0	uz	\<variable id=\"formatpaintbrush\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/paintbrush.xhp\"\>Copying Formatting With the Format Paintbrush\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN10655				0	uz	You can use the Format Paintbrush tool to copy formatting from a text selection in Writer or from an object and apply the formatting to another text selection or object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106DD				0	uz	Select the text (in Writer) or object whose formatting you want to copy.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN10667				0	uz	On the \<emph\>Standard Bar\</emph\>, click the \<emph\>Format Paintbrush\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN10660				0	uz	The cursor changes to a paint bucket.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN10663				0	uz	If you want to apply the formatting to more than one selection, double-click the \<emph\>Format Paintbrush\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id209967\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_formatpaintbrush.png\" width=\"0.2228in\" height=\"0.2228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id209967\"\>{ENTER ALTERNATE DESCRIPTION HERE}\</alt\>\</image\>. After you apply all the formatting, click the icon again.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066E				0	uz	Select or click the text (in Writer) or object that you want to apply the formatting to.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN10716				0	uz	To exclude paragraph formatting, hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> when you click. To exclude character formatting, hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift when you click.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN10671				0	uz	The following table describes the formatting attributes that the \<emph\>Format Paintbrush\</emph\> can copy:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN10691				0	uz	Type of Selection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN10697				0	uz	Comment				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN1069E				0	uz	Nothing selected, but cursor is inside a text passage				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A4				0	uz	Copies the formatting of the current paragraph and the character formatting of the next character in the text flow direction.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106AB				0	uz	Text is selected				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B1				0	uz	Copies the formatting of the last selected character and of the paragraph that contains the character.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B8				0	uz	Frame is selected				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106BE				0	uz	Copies the frame attributes that are defined in Format - Frame dialog. The contents, size, position, linking, hyperlinks, and macros in the frame are not copied.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106C5				0	uz	Object is selected				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106CB				0	uz	Copies the object formatting that is defined in the Format - Graphics or Format - Drawing Object dialogs. The contents, size, position, hyperlinks, and macros in the object are not copied.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D2				0	uz	Form control is selected				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D8				0	uz	Not supported				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106DF				0	uz	Drawing object is selected				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E5				0	uz	Copies all formatting attributes. In Impress and Draw, the text contents of the object is also copied.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F2				0	uz	Not supported				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F9				0	uz	Writer table or cells are selected				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106FF				0	uz	Copies the formatting that is specified in Table, Text Flow, Borders, and Background tab pages in the Format - Table dialog. The paragraph and character formatting are also copied.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN10706				0	uz	Calc table or cells are selected				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN1070C				0	uz	Copies the formatting that is specified in the Format - Cells dialog as well as the formatting of the cell contents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
