helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3143267				0	uz	You can place a graphic from a document such as an HTML page in the Gallery by drag-and-drop.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3154823				0	uz	Display the Gallery theme to which you want to add the graphic.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3153748				0	uz	Position the mouse pointer above the graphic, without clicking.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3156346				0	uz	If the mouse pointer changes to a hand symbol, the graphic refers to a hyperlink. In this case, click the graphic while pressing the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key to select it without executing the respective link.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3149578				0	uz	If the mouse pointer does not change to a hand symbol, you can simply click the graphic to select it.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3145120				0	uz	Once the graphic is selected, release the mouse button. Click again on the graphic image, keeping the mouse button pressed for more than two seconds. The graphic image is copied to the internal memory.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3150772				0	uz	Without releasing the mouse button, drag the graphic into the Gallery.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
