helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155630				0	uz	The row headers contain the following context menu commands:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156330				0	uz	Cut				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3159157				0	uz	Cuts the selected row to the clipboard.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159177				0	uz	Copy				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148685				0	uz	Copies the selected row to the clipboard.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156327				0	uz	Paste				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152472				0	uz	Pastes the content of the clipboard.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144511				0	uz	Delete				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148550				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Delete\"\>Deletes the selected row.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147303				0	uz	Insert Rows				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149456				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_TABLEDESIGN_INSERTROWS\"\>Inserts an empty row above the current row, if the table has not been saved. Inserts an empty row at the end of the table if the table has been saved.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153524				0	uz	Primary Key				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150398				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_TABLEDESIGN_TABED_PRIMARYKEY\"\>If this command has a check mark, the data field in this line is a primary key.\</ahelp\> By clicking the command you activate/deactivate the status. The command is only visible if the data source supports primary keys.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153104				0	uz	Field properties				2002-02-02 02:02:02
