helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Report Navigator				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	bm_id5823847				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>formulas in reports;editing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>functions in reports;editing\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	hd_id1821955				0	uz	\<variable id=\"rep_navigator\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/rep_navigator.xhp\"\>Report Navigator\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id1150852				0	uz	You can open the Report Navigator window of the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/rep_main.xhp\"\>Report Builder\</link\> by choosing \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>View - Report Navigator\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id1111484				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>The Report Navigator reveals the structure of the report. You can use the Report Navigator to insert functions into the report.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id8314157				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Click an entry in the Report Navigator. The corresponding object or area is selected in the Report Builder view. Right-click an entry to open the context menu.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	hd_id2932828				0	uz	To enter functions to the report				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id5091708				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>In the context menu of the Report Navigator, you see the same commands as in the Report Builder view, plus additional commands to create new functions or to delete them.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id9449446				0	uz	Functions can be entered using a syntax as specified by the \<link href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/OpenFormula\"\>OpenFormula\</link\> proposal.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id4095583				0	uz	See \<link href=\"http://wiki.services.openoffice.org/wiki/Database\"\>Wiki page about Base\</link\> for some more help regarding the functions in a report.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	hd_id311593				0	uz	To calculate a sum for each client				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id3948789				0	uz	Open the Report Navigator.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id5391399				0	uz	Open the Groups entry and the group where you want to calculate the cost. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id6989654				0	uz	The group has a sub entry called functions. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id1803643				0	uz	Open the context menu (right click) on the functions entry, choose to create a new function, and select it. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id868251				0	uz	In the property browser you see the function. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id6247749				0	uz	Change the name to e.g. CostCalc and the formula to [CostCalc] + [enter your cost column name].				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id1565904				0	uz	In the initial value enter 0.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id1569261				0	uz	Now you can insert a text field and bind it to your [CostCalc] (appears in the data field list box).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id9256874				0	uz	Maybe you have to set the initial value to the value of the field like [field].				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id4601886				0	uz	If there are blank fields in the cost column, use the following formula to replace the blank fields' content with zero:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id1754509				0	uz	[SumCost] + IF(ISBLANK([field]);0;[field])				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id8122196				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the formula that defines the function. Use OpenFormula syntax.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id9909665				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the initial value for the evaluation of the formula. Often this is set to 0 or to 1.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id9141819				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>If Deep traversing is enabled, functions are evaluated considering all lower levels of hierarchy. This would be used for instance for line numbering. If Deep traversing is not enabled, only the first level of hierarchy is evaluated.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id6354869				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>If Pre evaluation is enabled, functions are evaluated only when the report is finished.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Create New Adabas Database				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159176				0	uz	\<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/30100000.xhp\" name=\"Create New Adabas Database\"\>Create New Adabas Database\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154515				0	uz	Creates a new \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/30000000.xhp\" name=\"Adabas database\"\>Adabas database\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156117				0	uz	Database name				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3158432				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_ADABAS_DBNAME\"\>Type the name of the database.\</ahelp\> The name is added to the \<emph\>Data source URL\</emph\> field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150256				0	uz	User settings				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155628				0	uz	Administrator				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145609				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_ADABAS_SYSUSR\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the name of the database administrator.\</ahelp\> The administrator name and password is assigned when you create an Adabas database. Apart from the administrator, two more users can access the Adabas database.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149045				0	uz	Control User				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149294				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_ADABAS_CONUSR\"\>Enter the name of a user that you want to give limited control to modify some parameters of the database. Normally, the default settings for the name and the password of the control user are not changed.\</ahelp\> The control user does not affect the three-user limitation.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153379				0	uz	Domain User				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153362				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_ADABAS_USR\"\>Enter the name of the domain user that is used by Adabas internally. Normally, the default settings for the name and password of the domain user are not changed.\</ahelp\> The domain user does not affect the three-user limit.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147084				0	uz	Password				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148674				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_ADABAS_DOMAINPWD\"\>Enter a password.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144433				0	uz	Database settings				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145607				0	uz	Drives containing parts of the Serverdb are called DEVSPACEs. To improve performance, store each DEVSPACE on separate drives.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146985				0	uz	The file path for a DEVSPACE, including its file name, cannot exceed 40 characters.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146148				0	uz	SYSDEVSPACE				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149064				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_ADABAS_SYSDEVSPACE\"\>Enter the path for the system DEVSPACE.\</ahelp\> The SYSDEVSPACE manages the configuration data for the database. The size of the SYSDEVSPACE depends on the size of the database.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147319				0	uz	TRANSACTIONLOG				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154190				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_ADABAS_TRANSACTIONLOG\"\>Enter the path for the transaction log file.\</ahelp\> This file records all modifications that are made to the database during a transaction, and overwrites them when the transaction is completed. The TRANSACTIONLOG is also used for the rollback of a transaction.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145748				0	uz	DATADEVSPACE				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152597				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_ADABAS_DATADEVSPACE\"\>Enter the path for the data DEVSPACE.\</ahelp\> This file stores user data, such as tables and indexes, as well as the SQL catalog (schema info). The data contained in one user table is evenly distributed across all DATADEVSPACEs. The combined size of all DATADEVSPACEs corresponds to the size of the database.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150103				0	uz	The maximum size for a DATADEVSPACE in the limited version Adabas database is 100MB.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147426				0	uz	If the DATADEVSPACE reaches full capacity during a database operation, Adabas shuts down, increases the capacity of the DATADEVSPACE (up to 100 MB), and restarts the database. Saved data is not lost.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153189				0	uz	...				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153091				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_ADABAS_PBDATADEVSPACE\"\>Locate the directory where you want to save the file, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150686				0	uz	Transaction file (MB)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147396				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_ADABAS_TRANSACTIONLOG_SIZE\"\>Enter the size of the transaction file in megabytes.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157977				0	uz	Database size (MB)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150115				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_ADABAS_DATADEVSPACE_SIZE\"\>Enter the size of the database in megabytes here. The maximum size is 100 MB.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155415				0	uz	Data buffer size (MB)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149378	31			0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_ADABAS_CACHE_SIZE\"\>Enter the size of the data cache in megabytes. \</ahelp\> The data buffer can be simultaneously accessed by all users and stores the most recently accessed pages from the DATADEVSPACEs.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Sorting and Grouping				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	hd_id3486434				0	uz	\<variable id=\"rep_sort\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/rep_sort.xhp\"\>Sorting and Grouping\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id3068636				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>In the Sorting and Grouping dialog of \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/rep_main.xhp\"\>Report Builder\</link\>, you can define the fields that should be sorted in your report, and the fields that should be kept together to form a group.\</ahelp\> If you group your report by a certain field, all records with the same value of that field will be kept together in one group.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id876186				0	uz	The Groups box shows the fields in an order from top to bottom. You can select any field, then click the Move Up or Move Down button to move this field up or down in the list. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id3939634				0	uz	The sorting and grouping will be applied in the order of the list from top to bottom.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id599688				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Lists the fields that will be used for sorting or grouping. The field at the top has the highest priority, the second field has the second priority, and so on.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id1371501				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click to open a list from which you can select a field.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id4661702				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Moves the selected field up in the list.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id7868892				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Moves the selected field down in the list.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id2188787				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select the sorting order.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id5833307				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select to show or hide the Group Header.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id7726676				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select to show or hide the Group Footer.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id3729361				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select to create a new group on each changed value, or on other properties.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id0409200922142041				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Moves the selected field up in the list.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id3405560				0	uz	By default a new group is created on every changed value of a record from the selected field. You can change this property depending on the type of field:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id3409527				0	uz	For fields of type Text, you can select Prefix Characters and enter a number n of characters in the text box below. The records which are identical in the first n characters will be grouped together.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id7112338				0	uz	For fields of type Date/Time, you can group the records by the same year, quarter, month, week, day, hour, or minute. You can additionally specify an interval for weeks and hours: 2 weeks groups data in biweekly groups, 12 hours groups data in half-day groups.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id2855616				0	uz	For fields of type AutoNumber, Currency, or Number, you specify an interval.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id7700430				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the group interval value that records are grouped by.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id1180455				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select the level of detail by which a group is kept together on the same page.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id2091433				0	uz	When you specify to keep together some records on the same page, you have three choices:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id5092318				0	uz	No - page boundaries are not taken into account.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id9312417				0	uz	Whole Group - prints the group header, detail section, and group footer on the same page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id9089022				0	uz	With First Detail - prints the group header on a page only if the first detail record also can be printed on the same page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
