helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30000000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151262				0	uz	\<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/30000000.xhp\" name=\"Adabas D Database\"\>Adabas D Database\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30000000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152997				0	uz	About Adabas				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151111				0	uz	The Adabas database that you may have installed together with $[officename] is restricted to a size of 100 MB, and a maximum of three users on a network. See the "License.txt" file in the Adabas directory for more details. The Adabas database must be installed in a separate directory from $[officename].				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154749				0	uz	The name of an Adabas file cannot exceed 8 characters. The path to the Adabas file, including the file name, cannot exceed 30 characters, and must be compliant with the 7-bit ASCII code. Both the path and the file name cannot contain spaces.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153254				0	uz	Under Windows, the Adabas setup application adds the DBROOT environment variable that contains the path information for the database. If the setup application finds this variable, it does not install the database.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30000000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154729				0	uz	Create New Adabas Database				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149378				0	uz	Use the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/30100000.xhp\" name=\"Create New Adabas Database\"\>\<emph\>Create New Adabas Database\</emph\>\</link\> dialog to create an Adabas database:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147045				0	uz	Choose \<emph\>File - New - Database\</emph\> to open the Database Wizard.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147394				0	uz	Click \<emph\>Connect to an existing database\</emph\>, and then select "Adabas" in the listbox (scroll up in the listbox).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155600				0	uz	Work through the steps in the remaining pages of the Database Wizard.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30000000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154270				0	uz	Deleting an Adabas Database				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3157869				0	uz	To delete the reference to an Adabas database, choose \<emph\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Base - Databases\</emph\>. Select the database, and then click \<emph\>Delete\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
