helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropgen.xhp	0	help	par_idN10590				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Enables $[officename] support for auto-incremented data fields in the current ODBC or JDBC data source. Select this option if the auto-increment feature in the SDBCX layer of the database is not supported. In general, the auto-increment is selected for the primary key field.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropgen.xhp	0	help	par_idN10593				0	uz	Auto-increment statement				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropgen.xhp	0	help	par_idN10597				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Enter the SQL command specifier that instructs the data source to auto-increment a specified Integer data field.\</ahelp\> For example, the following MySQL statement used the AUTO_INCREMENT statement to increase the "id" field each time the statement creates a data field:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropgen.xhp	0	help	par_idN105A0				0	uz	CREATE TABLE "table1" ("id" INTEGER AUTO_INCREMENT)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropgen.xhp	0	help	par_idN10634				0	uz	For this example, you must enter AUTO_INCREMENT into the \<emph\>Auto-increment statement\</emph\> box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
