helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\02\10030000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154049				0	uz	Distort				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\02\10030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149756				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Shear\"\>Lets you drag the handles of the selected object to change its shape.\</ahelp\> If the selected object is not a polygon or Bézier curve, you are prompted to change the object to a curve before you can distort it.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\02\10030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154693				0	uz	\<image id=\"img_id3154933\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_shear.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3154933\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\02\10030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154294				0	uz	Distort				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\02\10030000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154203				0	uz	Transparency				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\02\10030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154258				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:InteractiveTransparence\"\>Applies a transparency gradient to the selected object.\</ahelp\> The transparency line represents a a grayscale, with the black handle corresponding to 0% transparency and the white handle to 100% transparency.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\02\10030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147516				0	uz	Drag the white handle to change the direction of the transparency gradient. Drag the black handle to change the length of the gradient. You can also drag and drop colors onto the handles from the \<emph\>Color\</emph\> Bar to change their grayscale values.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\02\10030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154104				0	uz	To display the \<emph\>Color Bar\</emph\>, choose \<emph\>View - Toolbars - Color Bar\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\02\10030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154602				0	uz	\<image id=\"img_id3154790\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_interactivetransparence.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3154790\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\02\10030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150623				0	uz	Transparency				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\02\10030000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149932				0	uz	Gradient				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\02\10030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149594	47			0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:InteractiveGradient\"\>Modifies the gradient fill of the selected object. This command is only available if you applied a gradient to the selected object in \<emph\>Format - Area\</emph\>.\</ahelp\> Drag the handles of the gradient line to change the direction of the gradient or the length of the gradient. You can also drag and drop colors onto the handles from the \<emph\>Color\</emph\> Bar to change the color of the gradient endpoints. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\02\10030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151311				0	uz	To display the \<emph\>Color Bar\</emph\>, choose \<emph\>View - Toolbars - Color Bar\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\02\10030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150990				0	uz	\<image id=\"img_id3151102\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_interactivegradient.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3151102\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\02\10030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148400				0	uz	Gradient				2002-02-02 02:02:02
