helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_import.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146121				0	uz	\<variable id=\"html_import\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/html_import.xhp\" name=\"Importing HTML Pages Into Presentations \"\>Importing HTML Pages Into Presentations \</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_import.xhp	0	help	par_id3150750				0	uz	You can import any text file, including text in HTML documents, into a slide.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_import.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155443				0	uz	To insert text from a file into a slide:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_import.xhp	0	help	par_id3146313				0	uz	In the slide where you want to insert the text, choose \<emph\>Insert - File\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_import.xhp	0	help	par_id3150207				0	uz	Select "Text" or "HTML Document" as the \<emph\>File type\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_import.xhp	0	help	par_id3148610				0	uz	Locate the file containing the text that you want to add, and then click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_import.xhp	0	help	par_id3153915				0	uz	If the text file contains more text than can be inserted into a single slide, you can divide the text over several slides.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_import.xhp	0	help	par_id3149126				0	uz	Double-click in the inserted text to enter edit mode.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_import.xhp	0	help	par_id3143228				0	uz	Select all of the text that lies below the visible slide area and press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+X.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_import.xhp	0	help	par_id3153811				0	uz	Choose \<emph\>Insert – Slide\</emph\>, and then press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+V.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_import.xhp	0	help	par_id3147297				0	uz	Repeat steps 1 to 3 until all of the text is on slides.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
