helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\print_tofit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155067				0	uz	\<variable id=\"print_tofit\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/print_tofit.xhp\" name=\"Printing a Slide to Fit a Paper Size\"\>Printing a Slide to Fit a Paper Size\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\print_tofit.xhp	0	help	par_id3154704				0	uz	You can reduce the size of a slide when you print, so that the slide can fit on a printed page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\print_tofit.xhp	0	help	par_id3154658				0	uz	Open the document that you want to print.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\print_tofit.xhp	0	help	par_id3145384				0	uz	In \<emph\>Normal View\</emph\>, choose \<emph\>Format - Page\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Page\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\print_tofit.xhp	0	help	par_id3148871	6			0	uz	In \<emph\>Layout settings \</emph\>area, select the \<emph\>Fit object to paper format\</emph\> check box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\print_tofit.xhp	0	help	par_id3153811				0	uz	In the \<emph\>Paper format\</emph\> area, select a \<emph\>Format\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\print_tofit.xhp	0	help	par_id3150431				0	uz	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. The slide is resized to fit the printed page, while maintaining the relative positions of the objects on the slide.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Loading Line and Arrow Styles				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145253				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>line styles;loading\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>lines;about line ends\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>arrows;loading arrow styles\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>styles;arrow and line styles\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>loading;arrow and line styles\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145253				0	uz	\<variable id=\"line_arrow_styles\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/line_arrow_styles.xhp\" name=\"Loading Line and Arrow Styles\"\>Loading Line and Arrow Styles\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3154017				0	uz	You can use styles to organize similar line and arrow types. $[officename] provides a few standard style files that you can load and use in your document. If you want, you can add or delete elements from a style file, or even create a custom style file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154485				0	uz	To load a line styles file:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3156382				0	uz	Choose \<emph\>Format - Line\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Line Styles\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3154705				0	uz	Click the \<emph\>Load Line Styles\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3145588				0	uz	Locate the file containing the line styles that you want to load, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. The file has the format [filename].sod.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3151240				0	uz	To save a line styles file, click the \<emph\>Save Line Styles\</emph\> button, enter a filename, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154765				0	uz	To load an arrow styles file:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3153070				0	uz	Choose \<emph\>Format - Line\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Arrow Styles\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3149054				0	uz	Click the \<emph\>Load Arrow Styles\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150391				0	uz	Locate the file containing the line styles that you want to load, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. The file has the format [filename].sod.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3166465				0	uz	To save an arrow styles file, click the \<emph\>Save Arrow Styles\</emph\> button, enter a filename, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3145822				0	uz	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05200000.xhp\" name=\"Format - Line\"\>Format - Line\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Converting 2D Objects to Curves, Polygons, and 3D Objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150207				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>3D rotation objects; generating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>3D objects; generating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>converting; to curves, polygons, 3D\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>extrusion objects\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150207				0	uz	\<variable id=\"3d_create\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/3d_create.xhp\" name=\"Converting 2D Objects to Curves, Polygons, and 3D Objects\"\>Converting 2D Objects to Curves, Polygons, and 3D Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3153914				0	uz	You can convert two dimensional (2D) objects to create different shapes. $[officename] can convert 2D objects to the following object types:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3150210				0	uz	Curved object based on Bézier curves				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3154762				0	uz	Polygon object consisting of straight line segments				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3150051				0	uz	3D object with shading and a light source				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3149873				0	uz	3D rotation object with shading and a light source				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149048				0	uz	To convert an object to a curved shape:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3147295				0	uz	Select a 2D object on the slide or page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3150654				0	uz	Right-click the object and choose \<emph\>Convert - To Curve\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3145828				0	uz	To modify the shape of the object, click the \<emph\>Points\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id1027558\" src=\"svx/res/cd015.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id1027558\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> toolbar, and drag the handles of the object. You can also drag the control points of a handle to modify the shape of the curve.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153738				0	uz	To convert a 2D object to a polygon:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3145241				0	uz	Select a 2D object on the slide or page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3148774				0	uz	Right-click the object and choose \<emph\>Convert - To Polygon.\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3155368				0	uz	To modify the shape of the object, click the \<emph\>Points\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id7219458\" src=\"svx/res/cd015.png\" width=\"0.2201inch\" height=\"0.2201inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id7219458\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> toolbar, and drag the handles of the object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153919				0	uz	To convert a 2D object to a 3D object:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3147172				0	uz	Select a 2D object on the slide or page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN1088B				0	uz	Click the \<emph\>Extrusion On/Off\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id2490920\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_extrusiontoggle.png\" width=\"0.1665inch\" height=\"0.1665inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id2490920\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> bar, or right-click the object and choose \<emph\>Convert - To 3D\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3148828				0	uz	To edit the properties of the 3D object, use the \<emph\>Line and Filling\</emph\> toolbar and the \<emph\>3D Settings\</emph\> toolbar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN108C5				0	uz	To convert a text object to 3D, use the \<emph\>Fontwork\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3821222\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_fontworkgalleryfloater.png\" width=\"0.1665inch\" height=\"0.1665inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3821222\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> toolbar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145410				0	uz	To convert a 2D object to a 3D rotation object:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3154260				0	uz	A 3D rotation object is created by rotating the selected object around its vertical axis.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3147506				0	uz	Select a 2D object on the slide or page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3151318				0	uz	Right-click the object and choose \<emph\>Convert - To 3D Rotation Object\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3146125				0	uz	To edit the properties of the 3D object, use the Line and Filling toolbar and the 3D Settings toolbar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3149336				0	uz	You can rotate the 2D object before converting it to create a more complex shape.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\move_object.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Moving Objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\move_object.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146121				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>objects;moving in slides\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>moving;objects in slides\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\move_object.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146121				0	uz	\<variable id=\"move_object\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/move_object.xhp\" name=\"Moving Objects\"\>Moving Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\move_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3149667				0	uz	You can move selected objects in your slide by dragging them, using the arrow keys, or by copying the objects and pasting them in another location.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\move_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3145799				0	uz	The arrow keys let you move objects more precisely than with the mouse.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\vectorize.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Converting Bitmap Images into Vector Graphics				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\vectorize.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153415				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>vectorizing bitmaps\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>converting; bitmaps to polygons\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>bitmaps; converting to vector graphics\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>vector graphics;converting bitmaps\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\vectorize.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153415				0	uz	\<variable id=\"vectorize\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/vectorize.xhp\" name=\"Converting Bitmap Images into Vector Graphics\"\>Converting Bitmap Images into Vector Graphics\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\vectorize.xhp	0	help	par_id3155633				0	uz	A vector graphic can be resized without losing the quality of the graphic. In $[officename] Draw and Impress, you can convert a bitmap image into a vector graphic.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\vectorize.xhp	0	help	par_id3151241				0	uz	Select the bitmap image that you want to convert.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\vectorize.xhp	0	help	par_id3153812				0	uz	Do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\vectorize.xhp	0	help	par_id3145118				0	uz	In $[officename] Draw, choose \<emph\>Modify - Convert - To Polygon\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\vectorize.xhp	0	help	par_id3151387				0	uz	In $[officename] Impress, right-click the object, and then choose \<emph\>Convert - To Polygon\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\vectorize.xhp	0	help	par_id3149349				0	uz	Set the conversion options for the image, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. See \<link href=\"text/simpress/01/13050200.xhp\" name=\"Convert to Polygon\"\>\<emph\>Convert to Polygon\</emph\>\</link\> for a description of the conversion options.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\vectorize.xhp	0	help	par_id3147371				0	uz	\<link href=\"text/simpress/01/13050200.xhp\" name=\"Convert to Polygon\"\>Convert to Polygon\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
