helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\change_scale.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149018				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>zooming;keyboard\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>keyboard; zooming\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\change_scale.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149018				0	uz	\<variable id=\"change_scale\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/change_scale.xhp\" name=\"Zooming With the Keypad\"\>Zooming With the Keypad\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\change_scale.xhp	0	help	par_id3148487				0	uz	You can use the keypad to quickly enlarge or reduce the view on your slide.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\change_scale.xhp	0	help	par_id3149501				0	uz	To zoom in, press the Plus Sign.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\change_scale.xhp	0	help	par_id3148837				0	uz	To zoom out, press the Minus Sign.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\change_scale.xhp	0	help	par_id7954954				0	uz	If you are using a mouse with a scroll wheel, you can hold down Ctrl and turn the wheel to change the zoom factor in all main modules of %PRODUCTNAME.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\change_scale.xhp	0	help	par_id3145116				0	uz	\<link href=\"text/simpress/04/01020000.xhp\" name=\"Shortcut keys for presentations\"\>Shortcut keys for presentations\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Using Gluepoints				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	bm_id0919200803534995				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>glue points;using\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_idN1065F				0	uz	\<variable id=\"gluepoints\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/gluepoints.xhp\"\>Using Gluepoints\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id0919200803040964				0	uz	In Impress and Draw, you can connect each two shapes with a line called a \<link href=\"text/simpress/02/10100000.xhp\"\>connector\</link\>. When you draw a connector between shapes, the connector will be attached to a gluepoint on each shape. Each shape has some default gluepoints, and the positions of the default gluepoints depend on the specific shape. You can add your own custom gluepoints to a shape and then attach connectors to the custom gluepoints.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id0919200803041099				0	uz	To add and edit gluepoints				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id091920080304108				0	uz	Do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id0919200803041082				0	uz	Click the \<emph\>Glue Point\</emph\> icon on the Drawing toolbar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id0919200803041186				0	uz	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit - Glue Points\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id0919200803041160				0	uz	Click the \<emph\>Insert Glue Point\</emph\> icon on the Gluepoints toolbar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id0919200803041115				0	uz	Click inside the shape where you want to add the new gluepoint.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id0919200803041133				0	uz	If the shape is filled, you can click anywhere inside the shape. If the shape is unfilled, you can click the border to insert a glue point. Once inserted, you can drag the glue point to another position inside the shape.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id0919200803041250				0	uz	With the four icons next to the \<emph\>Insert Glue Point\</emph\> icon, you choose the directions which will be permitted for a connector at this gluepoint. You can choose one or more directions for a particular gluepoint.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id0919200803041298				0	uz	If the \<emph\>Glue Point Relative\</emph\> icon is active, the gluepoint moves when you resize the object to keep its position relative to the object borders.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id0919200803041223				0	uz	If the \<emph\>Glue Point Relative\</emph\> icon is not active, the icons next to it are no longer grayed out. With these icons you can decide where a gluepoint will be placed when the size of the object is changed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Showing a Slide Show				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	bm_id5592516				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>running slide shows\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>showing;slide shows\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>slide shows; starting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>presentations; starting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>starting; slide shows\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>automatic slide shows\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>slide transitions;automatic\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>automatic slide transition\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	hd_id4901272				0	uz	\<variable id=\"show\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/show.xhp\" name=\"Showing a Slide Show\"\>Showing a Slide Show\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id9636829				0	uz	Different ways exist to start a slide show. Once a slide show is running, you can take control pressing keys or clicking the mouse buttons.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id7076937				0	uz	By default, a slide show always starts with the first slide. You advance manually through slides up to the last slide. You can change these settings.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	hd_id9954527				0	uz	Running a Slide Show				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id6860255				0	uz	Choose \<emph\>Slide Show - Slide Show\</emph\> to run the show.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id3209936				0	uz	Click to advance to the next effect or to the next slide.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id8702658				0	uz	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Esc\</item\> to abort the show before the end.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id3741264				0	uz	Many more keys are available to \<link href=\"text/simpress/04/01020000.xhp\"\>control a slide show\</link\>. You can also right-click to open a context menu with useful commands.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	hd_id5694143				0	uz	Showing an automatic slide show (kiosk mode)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id5829645				0	uz	For an automatic change to the next slide, you must assign a slide transition to each slide. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id2361522				0	uz	On the Task Pane, click \<emph\>Slide Transition\</emph\> to open that tab page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id9168980				0	uz	In the \<emph\>Advance slide\</emph\> area, click \<emph\>Automatically after\</emph\>, and select a time duration.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id9766533				0	uz	Click \<emph\>Apply to All Slides\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id6081728				0	uz	You can assign a different time for every slide to advance to the next slide. The \<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/rehearse_timings.xhp\"\>rehearse timings\</link\> feature can assist you to get the timing right.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id9219641				0	uz	To advance to the first slide, after all slides have been shown, you must set the slide show to repeat automatically.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id3174230				0	uz	Choose \<emph\>Slide Show - Slide Show Settings\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id1336405				0	uz	In the Type area, click \<emph\>Auto\</emph\> and select a pause time between shows.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id4959257				0	uz	When you create a new slide show using the \<link href=\"text/shared/autopi/01050000.xhp\"\>Presentation Wizard\</link\>, you can select the duration of slides and of the pause, on the third wizard page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	hd_id1906491				0	uz	Running a slide show from a file				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id4799340				0	uz	You can start %PRODUCTNAME from a command prompt, followed by the parameter \<item type=\"literal\"\>-show\</item\> and an Impress filename. For example, to start the file \<item type=\"literal\"\>filename.odp\</item\> from the command prompt, enter the following command:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id1502121				0	uz	\<item type=\"literal\"\>soffice -show filename.odp\</item\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id8266853				0	uz	This assumes that soffice is in the program path of your system, and that \<item type=\"literal\"\>filename.odp\</item\> is located in the current directory.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_objects.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Animating Objects in Presentation Slides				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_objects.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150251				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>objects; moving along paths\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>connecting; paths and objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>paths; moving objects along\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>motion paths\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>deleting;animation effects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>effects;applying to/removing from objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>animation effects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>animations;editing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>custom animation\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_objects.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150251	31			0	uz	\<variable id=\"animated_objects\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/animated_objects.xhp\" name=\"Animating Objects in Slides\"\>Animating Objects in Presentation Slides\</link\> \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_objects.xhp	0	help	par_id3150214	32			0	uz	You can apply preset animation effects to objects on your slide. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_objects.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154762	70			0	uz	To apply an animation effect to an object: 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_objects.xhp	0	help	par_id3146964				0	uz	On a slide in \<emph\>Normal\</emph\> view, select the object you want to animate.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_objects.xhp	0	help	par_id3149875				0	uz	Choose \<emph\>Slide Show - Custom Animation\</emph\>, click \<emph\>Add\</emph\>, and then select an animation effect.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_objects.xhp	0	help	par_id3166462				0	uz	In the \<emph\>Custom Animation\</emph\> dialog, click a tab page to choose from a category of effects. Click an effect, then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_objects.xhp	0	help	par_id3156060				0	uz	To preview the animation, click the \<emph\>Play\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_objects.xhp	0	help	hd_id2476577				0	uz	To apply and edit a motion path effect:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_objects.xhp	0	help	par_id4217047				0	uz	An object can be animated to move along a motion path. You can use predefined or your own motion paths.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_objects.xhp	0	help	par_id2629474				0	uz	If you select "Curve", "Polygon", or "Freeform Line", the dialog closes and you can draw your own path. If the drawing is finished and not canceled, the created path is removed from the document and inserted as a motion path effect.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_objects.xhp	0	help	par_id8069704				0	uz	 \<emph\>Editing motion paths\</emph\> 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_objects.xhp	0	help	par_id4524674				0	uz	If the Custom Animation Panel is visible, the motion paths of all effects of the current slide are drawn as a transparent overlay on the slide. All paths are visible all the time, therefore animations with consecutive paths can be created easily. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_objects.xhp	0	help	par_id4396801				0	uz	A motion path can be selected by clicking on the path. A selected path will support handles, it can be moved and resized like a shape. A double click on a path starts the point edit mode. The point edit mode can also be started by \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit - Points\</item\> or by pressing \<item type=\"keycode\"\>F8\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_objects.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148387				0	uz	To remove an animation effect from an object:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_objects.xhp	0	help	par_id3148774				0	uz	On a slide in \<emph\>Normal\</emph\> view, select the object from which to remove the effect.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_objects.xhp	0	help	par_id3155372				0	uz	Choose \<emph\>Slide Show - Custom Animation\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_objects.xhp	0	help	par_id3153718				0	uz	Click \<emph\>Remove\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\masterpage.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Applying a Slide Design to a Slide Master 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\masterpage.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152596				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>slide designs\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>slide masters; designing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>backgrounds; slides\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>slides; backgrounds\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>master pages, see slide masters\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\masterpage.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152596				0	uz	\<variable id=\"masterpage\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/masterpage.xhp\" name=\"Applying a Slide Design to a Slide Master\"\>Applying a Slide Design to a Slide Master\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\masterpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3154017				0	uz	Every slide in a presentation has exactly one slide master, also known as master page. A slide master determines the text formatting style for the title and outline and the background design for all slides that use this slide master.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\masterpage.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149018				0	uz	To apply a new slide master				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\masterpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3154702				0	uz	Select \<emph\>Format - Slide Design\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\masterpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3148485				0	uz	Click \<emph\>Load\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\masterpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3145384				0	uz	Under \<emph\>Categories\</emph\>, select a slide design category.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\masterpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3153915	26			0	uz	Under \<emph\>Templates\</emph\>, select a template with the design that you want to apply. To preview the template, click \<emph\>More\</emph\>, and then select the \<emph\>Preview \</emph\>box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\masterpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3154652				0	uz	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\masterpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3145115				0	uz	Do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\masterpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3150436				0	uz	To apply the slide design to all of the slides in your presentation, select the \<emph\>Exchange background page\</emph\> check box, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\masterpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3151387				0	uz	To apply the slide design to the current slide only, clear the \<emph\>Exchange background page\</emph\> check box, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
