helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3148663				0	uz	You can create and edit drawing objects using the keyboard.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3125863				0	uz	To Create and Edit a Drawing Object				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3153188				0	uz	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>F6\</item\> to navigate to the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3146971				0	uz	Press the \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Right\</item\> arrow key until you reach the toolbar icon of a drawing tool.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_idN106CD				0	uz	If there is an arrow next to the icon, the drawing tool opens a sub toolbar. Press the \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Up\</item\> or \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Down\</item\> arrow key to open the sub toolbar, then press the \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Right\</item\> or \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Left\</item\> key to select an icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3147338				0	uz	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Enter\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154705				0	uz	The object is created at the center of the current document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155962				0	uz	To return to the document, press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+F6\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155062				0	uz	You can use the arrow keys to position the object where you want. To choose a command from the context menu for the object, press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Shift+F10\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
