helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	bm_id3125863				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>arranging; objects (guide)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>objects;aligning\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>distributing draw objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>aligning;draw objects\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	hd_id3125863				0	uz	Arranging Objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3153727				0	uz	Each object that you place in your document is successively stacked on the preceding object. To re-arrange the stacking order of a selected object, proceed as follows.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN107D5				0	uz	Click the object whose position you want to change.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3150327				0	uz	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Modify - Arrange\</item\> to bring up the context menu and choose one of the arrange options:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN107E6				0	uz	\<emph\>Bring to Front\</emph\> places the object on top of all other objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN107EC				0	uz	\<emph\>Bring Forward\</emph\> places the object one place forward in the stack of objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F2				0	uz	\<emph\>Send Backward\</emph\> places the object one place back in the stack of objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F8				0	uz	\<emph\>Send to Back\</emph\> places the object behind all other objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN107FE				0	uz	\<emph\>Behind Object\</emph\> places the object behind another object that you select				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155766				0	uz	Arranging an Object Behind Another Object				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN10811				0	uz	Click the object whose position you want to change.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3154253				0	uz	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Modify - Arrange\</item\> to open the context menu and choose \<emph\>Behind Object\</emph\>. The mouse pointer changes to a hand.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3149126				0	uz	Click the object behind which you want to place the selected object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145789				0	uz	Reversing The Stacking Order of Two Objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3154022				0	uz	Shift-click both objects to select them.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3155114				0	uz	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Modify - Arrange\</item\> to open the context menu and choose \<emph\>Reverse\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166425				0	uz	Aligning Objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3152994				0	uz	The \<emph\>Alignment\</emph\> function enables you to align objects relative to each other or relative to the page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN108A3				0	uz	Select an object to align it to the page or select multiple objects to align them relative to each other.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN108A7				0	uz	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Modify - Alignment\</item\> and select one of the alignment options.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN108AE				0	uz	Distributing Objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3151390				0	uz	If you select three or more objects in Draw, you can also use the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05360000.xhp\" name=\"Distribution\"\>\<emph\>Distribution\</emph\>\</link\> command to distribute the vertical and horizontal spacing evenly between the objects.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN108CE				0	uz	Select three or more objects to be distributed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN108D2				0	uz	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Modify - Distribution\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN108DA				0	uz	Select the horizontal and vertical distribution option and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3150535				0	uz	Selected objects are distributed evenly along the horizontal or vertical axis. The two outermost objects are used as reference points and do not move when the \<emph\>Distribution\</emph\> command is applied.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
