helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3150312				0	uz	Select a single column range in which to enter the frequency according to the class limits. You must select one field more than the class ceiling. In this example, select the range C1:C6. Call up the FREQUENCY function in the \<emph\>Function Wizard\</emph\>. Select the \<emph\>Data\</emph\> range in (A1:A11), and then the \<emph\>Classes\</emph\> range in which you entered the class limits (B1:B6). Select the \<emph\>Array\</emph\> check box and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. You will see the frequency count in the range C1:C6.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_idN11269				0	uz	\<embedvar href=\"text/scalc/00/00000004.xhp#moreontop\"/\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151030				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>MDETERM function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>determinants\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151030				0	uz	MDETERM				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3154073				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_MDET\"\>Returns the array determinant of an array.\</ahelp\> This function returns a value in the current cell; it is not necessary to define a range for the results.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156366				0	uz	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3156380				0	uz	MDETERM(Array)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3150290				0	uz	\<emph\>Array\</emph\> represents a square array in which the determinants are defined.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_idN11035				0	uz	You can find a general introduction to using Array functions on top of this page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_idN11333				0	uz	\<embedvar href=\"text/scalc/00/00000004.xhp#moreontop\"/\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151348				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>MINVERSE function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inverse arrays\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151348				0	uz	MINVERSE				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3145569				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_MINV\"\>Returns the inverse array.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156072				0	uz	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3156085				0	uz	MINVERSE(Array)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3157849				0	uz	\<emph\>Array\</emph\> represents a square array that is to be inverted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_idN113EE				0	uz	\<embedvar href=\"text/scalc/00/00000004.xhp#moreontop\"/\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157868				0	uz	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3149638				0	uz	Select a square range and select MINVERSE. Select the output array, select the \<emph\>Array\</emph\> field and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148546				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>MMULT function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148546				0	uz	MMULT				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3148518				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_MMULT\"\>Calculates the array product of two arrays.\</ahelp\> The number of columns for array 1 must match the number of rows for array 2. The square array has an equal number of rows and columns.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146767				0	uz	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3150798				0	uz	MMULT(Array; Array)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3150812				0	uz	\<emph\>Array\</emph\> at first place represents the first array used in the array product.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3152553				0	uz	\<emph\>Array\</emph\> at second place represents the second array with the same number of rows.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_idN114C3				0	uz	\<embedvar href=\"text/scalc/00/00000004.xhp#moreontop\"/\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152574				0	uz	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3146826				0	uz	Select a square range. Choose the MMULT function. Select the first \<emph\>Array\</emph\>, then select the second \<emph\>Array\</emph\>. Using \<emph\>Function Wizard\</emph\>, mark the \<emph\>Array\</emph\> check box. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. The output array will appear in the first selected range.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154970				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>TRANSPOSE function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154970				0	uz	TRANSPOSE				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3155276				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_MTRANS\"\>Transposes the rows and columns of an array.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
