helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12050200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147125				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCPAGE_SUBT_OPTIONS:BTN_FORMATS\"\>Considers formatting attributes when sorting.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12050200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155418				0	uz	Custom sort order				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12050200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149400				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:LISTBOX:RID_SCPAGE_SUBT_OPTIONS:LB_USERDEF\"\>Uses a custom sorting order that you defined under \<emph\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - Sort Lists\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12050200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149121				0	uz	Ascending				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12050200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155068				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCPAGE_SUBT_OPTIONS:BTN_ASCENDING\"\>Sorts beginning with the lowest value. You can define the sort rules on Data - Sort - Options. You define the default on Tools - Options - Language settings - Languages.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12050200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155443				0	uz	Descending				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12050200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153766				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCPAGE_SUBT_OPTIONS:BTN_DESCENDING\"\>Sorts beginning with the highest value. You can define the sort rules on Data - Sort - Options. You define the default on Tools - Options - Language settings - Languages.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_now.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	NOW				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_now.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150521				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>NOW function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_now.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150521				0	uz	\<variable id=\"now\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/func_now.xhp\"\>NOW\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_now.xhp	0	help	par_id3148829				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_JETZT\"\>Returns the computer system date and time.\</ahelp\> The value is updated when you recalculate the document or each time a cell value is modified.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_now.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146988				0	uz	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_now.xhp	0	help	par_id3154897				0	uz	NOW()				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_now.xhp	0	help	par_id4598529				0	uz	NOW is a function without arguments.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_now.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154205				0	uz	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_now.xhp	0	help	par_id3150774				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=NOW()-A1\</item\> returns the difference between the date in A1 and now. Format the result as a number.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Protecting Sheet				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153087				0	uz	Protecting Sheet				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148664				0	uz	\<variable id=\"tabelletext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Protect\"\>Protects the cells in the current sheet from being modified.\</ahelp\>\</variable\> Choose \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document - Sheet\</emph\> to open the \<emph\>Protect Sheet\</emph\> dialog in which you then specify sheet protection with or without a password.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149664				0	uz	To protect cells from further editing, the \<emph\>Protected\</emph\> check box must be checked on the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05020600.xhp\" name=\"Format - Cells - Cell Protection\"\>\<emph\>Format - Cells - Cell Protection\</emph\>\</link\> tab page or on the \<emph\>Format Cells\</emph\> context menu.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154490	8			0	uz	Unprotected cells or cell ranges can be set up on a protected sheet by using the \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document - Sheet\</emph\> and \<emph\>Format - Cells - Cell Protection\</emph\> menus: 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149123				0	uz	Select the cells that will be unprotected				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150329				0	uz	Select \<emph\>Format - Cells - Cell Protection\</emph\>. Unmark the \<emph\>Protected\</emph\> box and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3156384				0	uz	On the \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document - Sheet\</emph\> menu, activate protection for the sheet. Effective immediately, only the cell range you selected in step 1 can be edited.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149566	9			0	uz	To later change an unprotected area to a protected area, select the range. Next, on the \<emph\>Format - Cells - Cell Protection\</emph\> tab page, check the \<emph\>Protected\</emph\> box. Finally, choose the \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document - Sheet \</emph\>menu. The previously editable range is now protected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153964				0	uz	Sheet protection also affects the context menu of the sheet tabs at the bottom of the screen. The \<emph\>Delete\</emph\> and \<emph\>Move/Copy\</emph\> commands cannot be selected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150301				0	uz	If a sheet is protected, you will not be able to modify or delete any Cell Styles.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154656				0	uz	A protected sheet or cell range can no longer be modified until this protection is disabled. To disable the protection, choose the \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document - Sheet\</emph\> command. If no password was set, the sheet protection is immediately disabled. If the sheet was password protected, the \<emph\>Remove Protection\</emph\> dialog opens, where you must enter the password.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149815				0	uz	Once saved, protected sheets can only be saved again by using the \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\> command.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150206				0	uz	Password (optional)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3152990				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Protect\"\>Allows you to enter a password to protect the sheet from unauthorized changes.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148700				0	uz	Complete protection of your work can be achieved by combining both options on the \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document\</emph\> menu, including password protection. To prohibit opening the document altogether, in the \<emph\>Save\</emph\> dialog mark the \<emph\>Save with password\</emph\> box before you click the \<emph\>Save\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030200.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Remove Precedents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030200.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155628				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>cells; removing precedents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formula cells;removing precedents\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155628				0	uz	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06030200.xhp\" name=\"Remove Precedents\"\>Remove Precedents\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149456				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ClearArrowPrecedents\"\>Deletes one level of the trace arrows that were inserted with the \<emph\>Trace Precedents\</emph\> command.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12080100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Hide Details				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12080100.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155628				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>sheets; hiding details\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12080100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155628				0	uz	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12080100.xhp\" name=\"Hide Details\"\>Hide Details\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12080100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154515				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:HideDetail\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Hides the details of the grouped row or column that contains the cursor. To hide all of the grouped rows or columns, select the outlined table, and then choose this command.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12080100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153252	3			0	uz	To show all hidden groups, select the outlined table, and then choose \<emph\>Data -Outline –\</emph\> \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12080200.xhp\" name=\"Show Details\"\>\<emph\>Show Details\</emph\>\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090200.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Refresh				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151385				0	uz	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12090200.xhp\" name=\"Refresh\"\>Refresh\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_time.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	TIME 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_time.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154073				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>TIME function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_time.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154073				0	uz	\<variable id=\"time\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/func_time.xhp\"\>TIME\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_time.xhp	0	help	par_id3145762				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ZEIT\"\>TIME returns the current time value from values for hours, minutes and seconds.\</ahelp\> This function can be used to convert a time based on these three elements to a decimal time value.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_time.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155550				0	uz	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_time.xhp	0	help	par_id3154584				0	uz	TIME(Hour; Minute; Second)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_time.xhp	0	help	par_id3152904				0	uz	Use an integer to set the \<emph\>Hour\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_time.xhp	0	help	par_id3151346				0	uz	Use an integer to set the \<emph\>Minute\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_time.xhp	0	help	par_id3151366				0	uz	Use an integer to set the \<emph\>Second\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_time.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145577				0	uz	Examples				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_time.xhp	0	help	par_id3156076				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=TIME(0;0;0)\</item\> returns 00:00:00				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_time.xhp	0	help	par_id3156090				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=TIME(4;20;4)\</item\> returns 04:20:04				2002-02-02 02:02:02
