helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_second.xhp	0	help	bm_id3159390				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>SECOND function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_second.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159390				0	uz	\<variable id=\"second\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/func_second.xhp\"\>SECOND\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_second.xhp	0	help	par_id3148974				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_SEKUNDE\"\>Returns the second for the given time value.\</ahelp\> The second is given as an integer between 0 and 59.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_second.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154362				0	uz	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_second.xhp	0	help	par_id3148407				0	uz	SECOND(Number)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_second.xhp	0	help	par_id3155904				0	uz	\<emph\>Number\</emph\>, as a time value, is a decimal, for which the second is to be returned.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_second.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149992				0	uz	Examples				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_second.xhp	0	help	par_id3153350				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=SECOND(NOW())\</item\> returns the current second				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_second.xhp	0	help	par_id3150831				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=SECOND(C4)\</item\> returns 17 if contents of C4 = \<item type=\"input\"\>12:20:17\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12050000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Subtotals				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153822				0	uz	Subtotals				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145119				0	uz	\<variable id=\"teilergebnisse\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:DataSubTotals\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Calculates subtotals for the columns that you select.\</ahelp\>\</variable\> $[officename] uses the SUM function to automatically calculate the subtotal and grand total values in a labeled range. You can also use other functions to perform the calculation. $[officename] automatically recognizes a defined database area when you place the cursor in it.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153896				0	uz	For example, you can generate a sales summary for a certain postal code based on data from a client database.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
