helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3151017				0	uz	ACOSH(Number)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3149000	64			0	uz	 This function returns the inverse hyperbolic cosine of \<emph\>Number\</emph\>, that is the number whose hyperbolic cosine is Number. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id6393932				0	uz	 Number must be greater than or equal to 1.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150566				0	uz	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3145629				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=DELTA(1;2)\</item\> returns 0.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id951567				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ACOSH(COSH(4))\</item\> returns 4.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149027				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>ACOT function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
