helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id159611				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ISEVEN_ADD(5)\</item\> returns 0.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id6097598				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ISEVEN_ADD(5)\</item\> returns 0.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147356				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>GCD function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>greatest common divisor\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147356				0	uz	GCD				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152465				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_GGT\"\>Returns the greatest common divisor of two or more integers.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id2769249				0	uz	The greatest common divisor is the positive largest integer which will divide, without remainder, each of the given integers.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150643				0	uz	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3154524				0	uz	GCD(Integer1; Integer2; ...; Integer30)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3149340				0	uz	\<emph\>Integer1 To 30\</emph\> are up to 30 integers whose greatest common divisor is to be calculated.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147317				0	uz	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3151285				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=GCD(16;32;24) \</item\>gives the result 8, because 8 is the largest number that can divide 16, 24 and 32 without a remainder.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id1604663				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=GCD(B1:B3)\</item\> where cells B1, B2, B3 contain \<item type=\"input\"\>9\</item\>, \<item type=\"input\"\>12\</item\>, \<item type=\"input\"\>9\</item\> gives 3.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151221				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>GCD_ADD function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
