helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156193				0	uz	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3150223				0	uz	COMBIN(Count1; Count2)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3150313				0	uz	\<emph\>Count1\</emph\> is the number of items in the set.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3153830				0	uz	\<emph\>Count2\</emph\> is the number of items to choose from the set.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id6807458				0	uz	COMBIN returns the number of ordered ways to choose these items. For example if there are 3 items A, B and C in a set, you can choose 2 items in 3 different ways, namely AB, AC and BC.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id7414471				0	uz	COMBIN implements the formula: Count1!/(Count2!*(Count1-Count2)!)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153171				0	uz	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3153517				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=DELTA(1;2)\</item\> returns 0.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150284				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>COMBINA function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>number of combinations with repetitions\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150284				0	uz	COMBINA				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157894				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_KOMBINATIONEN2\"\>Returns the number of combinations of a subset of items including repetitions.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145752				0	uz	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3145765				0	uz	COMBINA(Count1; Count2)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3153372				0	uz	\<emph\>Count1\</emph\> is the number of items in the set.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155544				0	uz	\<emph\>Count2\</emph\> is the number of items to choose from the set.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id1997131				0	uz	COMBINA returns the number of unique ways to choose these items, where the order of choosing is irrelevant, and repetition of items is allowed. For example if there are 3 items A, B and C in a set, you can choose 2 items in 6 different ways, namely AB, BA, AC, CA, BC and CB.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id2052064				0	uz	COMBINA implements the formula: (Count1+Count2-1)! / (Count2!(Count1-1)!)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154584				0	uz	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152904				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=DELTA(1;2)\</item\> returns 0.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156086				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>TRUNC function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>decimal places;cutting off\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156086				0	uz	TRUNC				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157866				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_KUERZEN\"\>Truncates a number by removing decimal places.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148499				0	uz	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3148511				0	uz	TRUNC(Number; Count)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3150796				0	uz	Returns \<emph\>Number\</emph\> with at most \<emph\>Count\</emph\> decimal places. Excess decimal places are simply removed, irrespective of sign.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3150816				0	uz	\<item type=\"literal\"\>TRUNC(Number; 0)\</item\> behaves as \<item type=\"literal\"\>INT(Number)\</item\> for positive numbers, but effectively rounds towards zero for negative numbers.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152555				0	uz	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152569				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=TRUNC(1.239;2)\</item\> returns 1.23. The 9 is lost.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id7050080				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=TRUNC(-1.234999;3)\</item\> returns -1.234. All the 9s are lost.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153601				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>LN function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>natural logarithm\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153601				0	uz	LN				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3154974				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_LN\"\>Returns the natural logarithm based on the constant e of a number.\</ahelp\> The constant e has a value of approximately 2.71828182845904.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154993				0	uz	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155284				0	uz	LN(Number)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155297				0	uz	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the value whose natural logarithm is to be calculated.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153852				0	uz	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3153866				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=LN(3)\</item\> returns the natural logarithm of 3 (approximately 1.0986).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id5747245				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=VALUE("4321")\</item\> returns 4321.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3109813				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>LOG function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>logarithms\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3109813				0	uz	LOG				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3109841				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_LOG\"\>Returns the logarithm of a number to the specified base.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144719				0	uz	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144732				0	uz	LOG(Number; Base)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144746				0	uz	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the value whose logarithm is to be calculated.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152860				0	uz	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3154429				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=LOG(10;3)\</item\> returns the logarithm to base 3 of 10 (approximately 2.0959).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id5577562				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=LEN(12345.67)\</item\> returns 8.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154187				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>LOG10 function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>base-10 logarithm\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154187				0	uz	LOG10				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155476				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_LOG10\"\>Returns the base-10 logarithm of a number.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155494				0	uz	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3159294				0	uz	LOG10(Number)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3159308				0	uz	Returns the logarithm to base 10 of \<emph\>Number\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159328				0	uz	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157916				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=LOG10(5)\</item\> returns the base-10 logarithm of 5 (approximately 0.69897).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152518				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>CEILING function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rounding;up to multiples of significance\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152518				0	uz	CEILING				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3153422				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_OBERGRENZE\"\>Rounds a number up to the nearest multiple of Significance.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153440				0	uz	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3153454				0	uz	CEILING(Number; Significance; Mode)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3153467				0	uz	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the number that is to be rounded up.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155000				0	uz	\<emph\>Significance\</emph\> is the number to whose multiple the value is to be rounded up.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155020				0	uz	\<emph\>Mode\</emph\> is an optional value. If the Mode value is given and not equal to zero, and if Number and Significance are negative, then rounding is done based on the absolute value of Number. This parameter is ignored when exporting to MS Excel as Excel does not know any third parameter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163792				0	uz	If both parameters Number and Significance are negative and the Mode value is equal to zero or is not given, the results in $[officename] and Excel will differ after the import has been completed. If you export the spreadsheet to Excel, use Mode=1 to see the same results in Excel as in Calc.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145697				0	uz	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3145710				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=CEILING(-11;-2)\</item\> returns -10				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3145725				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=CEILING(-11;-2;0)\</item\> returns -10				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3145740				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=CEILING(-11;-2;1)\</item\> returns -12				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3157762				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>PI function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157762				0	uz	PI				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157790				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_PI\"\>Returns 3.14159265358979, the value of the mathematical constant PI to 14 decimal places.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157809				0	uz	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157822				0	uz	PI()				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157836				0	uz	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152370				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=PI()\</item\> returns 3.14159265358979.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152418				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>MULTINOMIAL function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152418				0	uz	MULTINOMIAL				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152454				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_MULTINOMIAL\"\> Returns the factorial of the sum of the arguments divided by the product of the factorials of the arguments.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155646				0	uz	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155660				0	uz	MULTINOMIAL(Number(s))				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155673				0	uz	\<emph\>Number(s)\</emph\> is a list of up to 30 numbers.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155687				0	uz	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155701				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=MULTINOMIAL(F11:H11)\</item\> returns 1260, if F11 to H11 contain the values \<item type=\"input\"\>2\</item\>, \<item type=\"input\"\>3\</item\> and \<item type=\"input\"\>4\</item\>. This corresponds to the formula =(2+3+4)! / (2!*3!*4!)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155717				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>POWER function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155717				0	uz	POWER				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3159495				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_POTENZ\"\>Returns a number raised to a power.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159513				0	uz	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3159540				0	uz	Returns \<emph\>Base\</emph\> raised to the power of \<emph\>Power\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id5081637				0	uz	The same result may be achieved by using the exponentiation operator ^:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id9759514				0	uz	\<item type=\"literal\"\>Base^Power\</item\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159580				0	uz	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3159594				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=POWER(4;3)\</item\> returns 64, which is 4 to the power of 3.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id1614429				0	uz	=4^3 also returns 4 to the power of 3.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152651				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>SERIESSUM function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152651				0	uz	SERIESSUM				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152688				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Sums the first terms of a power series.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152708				0	uz	SERIESSUM(x;n;m;coefficients) = coefficient_1*x^n + coefficient_2*x^(n+m) + coefficient_3*x^(n+2m) +...+ coefficient_i*x^(n+(i-1)m)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152724				0	uz	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_idN11BD9				0	uz	SERIESSUM(X; N; M; Coefficients)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152737				0	uz	\<emph\>X\</emph\> is the input value for the power series.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144344				0	uz	\<emph\>N\</emph\> is the initial power				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144357				0	uz	\<emph\>M\</emph\> is the increment to increase N				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144370				0	uz	\<emph\>Coefficients\</emph\> is a series of coefficients. For each coefficient the series sum is extended by one section.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3144386				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>PRODUCT function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>numbers;multiplying\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>multiplying;numbers\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144386				0	uz	PRODUCT				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144414				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_PRODUKT\"\>Multiplies all the numbers given as arguments and returns the product.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144433				0	uz	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144446				0	uz	PRODUCT(Number1; Number2; ...; Number30)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144460				0	uz	\<emph\>Number1 to 30\</emph\> are up to 30 arguments whose product is to be calculated.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id1589098				0	uz	PRODUCT returns number1 * number2 * number3 * ...				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144480				0	uz	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144494				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=PRODUCT(2;3;4)\</item\> returns 24.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3160340				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>SUMSQ function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>square number additions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sums;of square numbers\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3160340				0	uz	SUMSQ				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3160368				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_QUADRATESUMME\"\>If you want to calculate the sum of the squares of numbers (totaling up of the squares of the arguments), enter these into the text fields.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3160388				0	uz	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3160402				0	uz	SUMSQ(Number1; Number2; ...; Number30)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3160415				0	uz	\<emph\>Number1 to 30\</emph\> are up to 30 arguments the sum of whose squares is to be calculated.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3160436				0	uz	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3160449				0	uz	If you enter the numbers \<item type=\"input\"\>2\</item\>; \<item type=\"input\"\>3\</item\> and \<item type=\"input\"\>4\</item\> in the Number 1; 2 and 3 text boxes, 29 is returned as the result.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3158247				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>MOD function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>remainders of divisions\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158247				0	uz	MOD				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158276				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_REST\"\>Returns the remainder when one integer is divided by another.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158294				0	uz	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158308				0	uz	MOD(Dividend; Divisor)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158321				0	uz	 For integer arguments this function returns Dividend modulo Divisor, that is the remainder when \<emph\>Dividend\</emph\> is divided by \<emph\>Divisor\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158341				0	uz	This function is implemented as \<item type=\"literal\"\>Dividend - Divisor * INT(Dividend/Divisor)\</item\> , and this formula gives the result if the arguments are not integer.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158361				0	uz	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158374				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=MOD(22;3)\</item\> returns 1, the remainder when 22 is divided by 3.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id1278420				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=MOD(11.25;2.5)\</item\> returns 1.25.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3144592				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>QUOTIENT function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>divisions\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144592				0	uz	QUOTIENT				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144627				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_QUOTIENT\"\>Returns the integer part of a division operation.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144646				0	uz	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144659				0	uz	QUOTIENT(Numerator; Denominator)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id9038972				0	uz	Returns the integer part of \<emph\>Numerator\</emph\> divided by \<emph\>Denominator\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id7985168				0	uz	QUOTIENT is equivalent to \<item type=\"literal\"\>INT(numerator/denominator)\</item\>, except that it may report errors with different error codes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144674				0	uz	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144687				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=QUOTIENT(11;3)\</item\> returns 3. The remainder of 2 is lost.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3144702				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>RADIANS function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>converting;degrees, into radians\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144702				0	uz	RADIANS				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158025				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_RAD\"\>Converts degrees to radians.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158042				0	uz	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158055				0	uz	RADIANS(Number)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158069				0	uz	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the angle in degrees to be converted to radians.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id876186				0	uz	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3939634				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=RADIANS(90)\</item\> returns 1.5707963267949, which is PI/2 to Calc's accuracy.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3158121				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>ROUND function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158121				0	uz	ROUND				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158150				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_RUNDEN\"\>Rounds a number to a certain number of decimal places.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158169				0	uz	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158182				0	uz	ROUND(Number; Count)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158196				0	uz	Returns \<emph\>Number\</emph\> rounded to \<emph\>Count\</emph\> decimal places. If Count is omitted or zero, the function rounds to the nearest integer. If Ccunt is negative, the function rounds to the nearest 10, 100, 1000, etc.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id599688				0	uz	This function rounds to the nearest number. See ROUNDDOWN and ROUNDUP for alternatives.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145863				0	uz	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3145876				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ROUND(2.348;2)\</item\> returns 2.35				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3145899				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ROUND(-32.4834;3)\</item\> returns -32.483. Change the cell format to see all decimals.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id1371501				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ROUND(2.348;0)\</item\> returns 2.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id4661702				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ROUND(2.5)\</item\> returns 3. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id7868892				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ROUND(987.65;-2)\</item\> returns 1000.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145991				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>ROUNDDOWN function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145991				0	uz	ROUNDDOWN				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3146020				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ABRUNDEN\"\>Rounds a number down, toward zero, to a certain precision.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146037				0	uz	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3146051				0	uz	ROUNDDOWN(Number; Count)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3146064				0	uz	Returns \<emph\>Number\</emph\> rounded down (towards zero) to \<emph\>Count\</emph\> decimal places. If Count is omitted or zero, the function rounds down to an integer. If Count is negative, the function rounds down to the next 10, 100, 1000, etc.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id2188787				0	uz	This function rounds towards zero. See ROUNDUP and ROUND for alternatives.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163164				0	uz	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163178				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ROUNDDOWN(1.234;2)\</item\> returns 1.23.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id5833307				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ROUNDDOWN(45.67;0)\</item\> returns 45.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id7726676				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ROUNDDOWN(-45.67)\</item\> returns -45.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3729361				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ROUNDDOWN(987.65;-2)\</item\> returns 900.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3163268				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>ROUNDUP function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163268				0	uz	ROUNDUP				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163297				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_AUFRUNDEN\"\>Rounds a number up, away from zero, to a certain precision.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163315				0	uz	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163328				0	uz	ROUNDUP(Number; Count)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163342				0	uz	Returns \<emph\>Number\</emph\> rounded up (away from zero) to \<emph\>Count\</emph\> decimal places. If Count is omitted or zero, the function rounds up to an integer. If Count is negative, the function rounds up to the next 10, 100, 1000, etc.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id9573961				0	uz	This function rounds away from zero. See ROUNDDOWN and ROUND for alternatives.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163381				0	uz	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144786				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ROUNDUP(1.1111;2)\</item\> returns 1.12.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id7700430				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ROUNDUP(1.2345;1)\</item\> returns 1.3.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id1180455				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ROUNDUP(45.67;0)\</item\> returns 46.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3405560				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ROUNDUP(-45.67)\</item\> returns -46.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3409527				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ROUNDUP(987.65;-2)\</item\> returns 1000.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3144877				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>SIN function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144877				0	uz	SIN				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144906				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_SIN\"\>Returns the sine of the given angle (in radians).\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144923				0	uz	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144937				0	uz	SIN(Number)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144950				0	uz	Returns the (trigonometric) sine of \<emph\>Number\</emph\>, the angle in radians.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id8079470				0	uz	To return the sine of an angle in degrees, use the RADIANS function.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144969				0	uz	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144983				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=SIN(PI()/2)\</item\> returns 1, the sine of PI/2 radians.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3916440				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=SIN(RADIANS(30))\</item\> returns 0.5, the sine of 30 degrees.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3163397				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>SINH function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163397				0	uz	SINH				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163426				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_SINHYP\"\>Returns the hyperbolic sine of a number.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163444				0	uz	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163457				0	uz	SINH(Number)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163471				0	uz	Returns the hyperbolic sine of \<emph\>Number\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163491				0	uz	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163504				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=SINH(0)\</item\> returns 0, the hyperbolic sine of 0.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3163596				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>SUM function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>adding;numbers in cell ranges\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163596				0	uz	SUM				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163625				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_SUMME\"\>Adds all the numbers in a range of cells.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163643				0	uz	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163656				0	uz	SUM(Number1; Number2; ...; Number30)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163671				0	uz	\<emph\>Number 1 to Number 30\</emph\> are up to 30 arguments whose sum is to be calculated.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163690				0	uz	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163704				0	uz	If you enter the numbers \<item type=\"input\"\>2\</item\>; \<item type=\"input\"\>3 \</item\>and \<item type=\"input\"\>4\</item\> in the Number 1; 2 and 3 text boxes, 9 will be returned as the result.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3151740				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=SUM(A1;A3;B5)\</item\> calculates the sum of the three cells. \<item type=\"input\"\>=SUM (A1:E10)\</item\> calculates the sum of all cells in the A1 to E10 cell range.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3151756				0	uz	Conditions linked by AND can be used with the function SUM() in the following manner:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3151774				0	uz	Example assumption: You have entered invoices into a table. Column A contains the date value of the invoice, column B the amounts. You want to find a formula that you can use to return the total of all amounts only for a specific month, e.g. only the amount for the period >=2008-01-01 to <2008-02-01. The range with the date values covers A1:A40, the range containing the amounts to be totaled is B1:B40. C1 contains the start date, 2008\<item type=\"input\"\>-01-01\</item\>, of the invoices to be included and C2 the date, 2008\<item type=\"input\"\>-02-01\</item\>, that is no longer included.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3151799				0	uz	Enter the following formula as an array formula:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3151813				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=SUM((A1:A40>=C1)*(A1:A40<C2)*B1:B40)\</item\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3151828				0	uz	In order to enter this as an array formula, you must press the Shift\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>+Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>+ Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+ Enter keys instead of simply pressing the Enter key to close the formula. The formula will then be shown in the \<emph\>Formula\</emph\> bar enclosed in braces.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3151869				0	uz	{=SUM((A1:A40>=C1)*(A1:A40<C2)*B1:B40)}				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3151884				0	uz	The formula is based on the fact that the result of a comparison is 1 if the criterion is met and 0 if it is not met. The individual comparison results will be treated as an array and used in matrix multiplication, and at the end the individual values will be totaled to give the result matrix.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151957				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>SUMIF function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>adding;specified numbers\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151957				0	uz	SUMIF				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3151986				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_SUMMEWENN\"\>Adds the cells specified by a given criteria.\</ahelp\> This function is used to browse a range when you search for a certain value.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152015				0	uz	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152028				0	uz	SUMIF(Range; Criteria; SumRange)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152043				0	uz	\<emph\>Range\</emph\> is the range to which the criteria are to be applied.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152062				0	uz	\<emph\>Criteria\</emph\> is the cell in which the search criterion is shown, or the search criterion itself. If the criteria is written into the formula, it has to be surrounded by double quotes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152083				0	uz	\<emph\>SumRange\</emph\> is the range from which values are summed. If this parameter has not been indicated, the values found in the Range are summed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id8347422				0	uz	SUMIF supports the reference concatenation operator (~) only in the Criteria parameter, and only if the optional SumRange parameter is not given.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152110				0	uz	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152148				0	uz	To sum up only negative numbers: \<item type=\"input\"\>=SUMIF(A1:A10;"<0")\</item\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id6670125				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=SUMIF(A1:A10;">0";B1:10)\</item\> - sums values from the range B1:B10 only if the corresponding values in the range A1:A10 are >0.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id6062196				0	uz	See COUNTIF() for some more syntax examples that can be used with SUMIF().				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152195				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>TAN function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152195				0	uz	TAN				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152224				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_TAN\"\>Returns the tangent of the given angle (in radians).\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152242				0	uz	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152255				0	uz	TAN(Number)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152269				0	uz	Returns the (trigonometric) tangent of \<emph\>Number\</emph\>, the angle in radians.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id5752128				0	uz	To return the tangent of an angle in degrees, use the RADIANS function.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152287				0	uz	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152301				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=TAN(PI()/4) \</item\>returns 1, the tangent of PI/4 radians.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id1804864				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=TAN(RADIANS(45))\</item\> returns 1, the tangent of 45 degrees.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3165434				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>TANH function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3165434				0	uz	TANH				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3165462				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_TANHYP\"\>Returns the hyperbolic tangent of a number.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3165480				0	uz	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3165494				0	uz	TANH(Number)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3165508				0	uz	Returns the hyperbolic tangent of \<emph\>Number\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3165527				0	uz	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3165541				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=TANH(0)\</item\> returns 0, the hyperbolic tangent of 0.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3165633				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>AutoFilter function; subtotals\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sums;of filtered data\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>filtered data; sums\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>SUBTOTAL function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3165633				0	uz	SUBTOTAL				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3165682				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_TEILERGEBNIS\"\>Calculates subtotals.\</ahelp\> If a range already contains subtotals, these are not used for further calculations. Use this function with the AutoFilters to take only the filtered records into account.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3165704				0	uz	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3165717				0	uz	SUBTOTAL(Function; Range)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3165731				0	uz	\<emph\>Function\</emph\> is a number that stands for one of the following functions:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3165782				0	uz	Function index				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3165806				0	uz	Function				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3165833				0	uz	1				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3165856				0	uz	AVERAGE				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3165883				0	uz	2				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3165906				0	uz	COUNT				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3165933				0	uz	3				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3165956				0	uz	COUNTA				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3165983				0	uz	4				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3166006				0	uz	MAX				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3166033				0	uz	5				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3166056				0	uz	MIN				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143316				0	uz	6				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143339				0	uz	PRODUCT				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143366				0	uz	7				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143389				0	uz	STDEV				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143416				0	uz	8				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143439				0	uz	STDEVP				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143466				0	uz	9				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143489				0	uz	SUM				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143516				0	uz	10				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143539				0	uz	VAR				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143566				0	uz	11				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143589				0	uz	VARP				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143606				0	uz	\<emph\>Range\</emph\> is the range whose cells are included.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143625				0	uz	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143638				0	uz	You have a table in the cell range A1:B5 containing cities in column A and accompanying figures in column B. You have used an AutoFilter so that you only see rows containing the city Hamburg. You want to see the sum of the figures that are displayed; that is, just the subtotal for the filtered rows. In this case the correct formula would be:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143658				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=SUBTOTAL(9;B2:B5)\</item\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3143672				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>Euro; converting in\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>CONVERT function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143708				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_UMRECHNEN\"\>Converts old European national currency to and from Euros.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143731				0	uz	\<emph\>Syntax\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143763				0	uz	\<emph\>Value\</emph\> is the amount of the currency to be converted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143782				0	uz	\<emph\>Currency1\</emph\> and \<emph\>Currency2\</emph\> are the currency units to convert from and to respectively. These must be text, the official abbreviation for the currency (for example, "EUR"). The rates (shown per Euro) were set by the European Commission.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143819				0	uz	\<emph\>Examples\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143837				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=CONVERT(100;"ATS";"EUR")\</item\> converts 100 Austrian Schillings into Euros.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143853				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=CONVERT(100;"EUR";"DEM")\</item\> converts 100 Euros into German Marks.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id0908200902090676				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>COVAR function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id0908200902074836				0	uz	CONVERT				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id0908200902131071				0	uz	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id0908200902131152				0	uz	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3157177				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>ODD function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rounding;up/down to nearest odd integer\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157177				0	uz	ODD				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157205				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_UNGERADE\"\>Rounds a positive number up to the nearest odd integer and a negative number down to the nearest odd integer.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157223				0	uz	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157237				0	uz	ODD(Number)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157250				0	uz	 Returns \<emph\>Number\</emph\> rounded to the next odd integer up, away from zero.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157270				0	uz	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157283				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=DELTA(1;2)\</item\> returns 0.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id8746910				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ISODD_ADD(5)\</item\> returns 1.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id9636524				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ISODD_ADD(5)\</item\> returns 1.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id5675527				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ISODD_ADD(5)\</item\> returns 1.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3157404				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>FLOOR function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rounding;down to nearest multiple of significance\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157404				0	uz	FLOOR				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157432				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_UNTERGRENZE\"\>Rounds a number down to the nearest multiple of Significance.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157451				0	uz	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157464				0	uz	FLOOR(Number; Significance; Mode)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157478				0	uz	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the number that is to be rounded down.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157497				0	uz	\<emph\>Significance\</emph\> is the value to whose multiple the number is to be rounded down.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157517				0	uz	\<emph\>Mode\</emph\> is an optional value. If the Mode value is given and not equal to zero, and if Number and Significance are negative, then rounding is done based on the absolute value of the number. This parameter is ignored when exporting to MS Excel as Excel does not know any third parameter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163894				0	uz	If both parameters Number and Significance are negative, and if the Mode value is equal to zero or is not specified, then the results in $[officename] Calc and Excel will differ after exporting. If you export the spreadsheet to Excel, use Mode=1 to see the same results in Excel as in Calc.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163932				0	uz	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163945				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=FLOOR( -11;-2)\</item\> returns -12				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163966				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=FLOOR( -11;-2;0)\</item\> returns -12				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163988				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=FLOOR( -11;-2;1)\</item\> returns -10				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3164086				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>SIGN function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>algebraic signs\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164086				0	uz	SIGN				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164115				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_VORZEICHEN\"\>Returns the sign of a number. Returns 1 if the number is positive, -1 if negative and 0 if zero.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164136				0	uz	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164150				0	uz	SIGN(Number)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164164				0	uz	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the number whose sign is to be determined.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164183				0	uz	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164197				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=GESTEP(5;1)\</item\> returns 1.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164212				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=N(TRUE)\</item\> returns 1				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3164252				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>MROUND function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>nearest multiple\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164252				0	uz	MROUND				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164288				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_MROUND\"\>Returns a number rounded to the nearest multiple of another number.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164306				0	uz	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164320				0	uz	MROUND(Number; Multiple)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3486434				0	uz	Returns \<emph\>Number\</emph\> rounded to the nearest multiple of \<emph\>Multiple\</emph\>. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3068636				0	uz	An alternative implementation would be \<item type=\"literal\"\>Multiple * ROUND(Number/Multiple)\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164333				0	uz	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164347				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=MROUND(15.5;3)\</item\> returns 15, as 15.5 is closer to 15 (= 3*5) than to 18 (= 3*6).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_idN14DD6				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=MROUND(1.4;0.5)\</item\> returns 1.5 (= 0.5*3).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3164375				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>SQRT function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>square roots;positive numbers\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164375				0	uz	SQRT				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164404				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_WURZEL\"\>Returns the positive square root of a number.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164424				0	uz	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164437				0	uz	SQRT(Number)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164451				0	uz	Returns the positive square root of \<emph\>Number\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id6870021				0	uz	 Number must be positive.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164471				0	uz	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164484				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=DELTA(1;2)\</item\> returns 0.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3591723				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=SQRT(-16)\</item\> returns an \<item type=\"literal\"\>invalid argument\</item\> error.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3164560				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>SQRTPI function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>square roots;products of Pi\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164560				0	uz	SQRTPI				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164596				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_SQRTPI\"\>Returns the square root of (PI times a number).\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164614				0	uz	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164627				0	uz	SQRTPI(Number)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id1501510				0	uz	Returns the positive square root of (PI multiplied by \<emph\>Number\</emph\>).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id9929197				0	uz	This is equivalent to \<item type=\"literal\"\>SQRT(PI()*Number)\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164641				0	uz	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164654				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=SQRTPI(2)\</item\> returns the squareroot of (2PI), approximately 2.506628.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3164669				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>random numbers; between limits\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>RANDBETWEEN function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164669				0	uz	RANDBETWEEN				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164711				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_RANDBETWEEN\"\>Returns an integer random number in a specified range.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164745				0	uz	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164758				0	uz	RANDBETWEEN(Bottom; Top)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id7112338				0	uz	Returns an integer random number between integers \<emph\>Bottom\</emph\> and \<emph\>Top\</emph\> (both inclusive).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id2855616				0	uz	This function produces a new random number each time Calc recalculates. To force Calc to recalculate manually press Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+F9.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id2091433				0	uz	To generate random numbers which never recalculate, copy cells containing this function, and use \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit - Paste Special\</item\> (with \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Paste All\</item\> and \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Formulas\</item\> not marked and \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Numbers\</item\> marked).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164772				0	uz	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164785				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=RANDBETWEEN(20;30)\</item\> returns an integer of between 20 and 30.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3164800				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>RAND function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>random numbers;between 0 and 1\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164800				0	uz	RAND				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164829				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ZUFALLSZAHL\"\>Returns a random number between 0 and 1.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164870				0	uz	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164884				0	uz	RAND()				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id5092318				0	uz	This function produces a new random number each time Calc recalculates. To force Calc to recalculate manually press Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+F9.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id9312417				0	uz	To generate random numbers which never recalculate, copy cells each containing =RAND(), and use \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit - Paste Special\</item\> (with \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Paste All\</item\> and \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Formulas\</item\> not marked and \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Numbers\</item\> marked).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id9089022				0	uz	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id9569078				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=RAND()\</item\> returns a random number between 0 and 1.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3164897				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>COUNTIF function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>counting;specified cells\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164897				0	uz	COUNTIF				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164926				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ZAEHLENWENN\"\>Returns the number of cells that meet with certain criteria within a cell range.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164953				0	uz	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164967				0	uz	COUNTIF(Range; Criteria)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164980				0	uz	\<emph\>Range\</emph\> is the range to which the criteria are to be applied.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3165000				0	uz	\<emph\>Criteria\</emph\> indicates the criteria in the form of a number, an expression or a character string. These criteria determine which cells are counted. You may also enter a search text in the form of a regular expression, e.g. b.* for all words that begin with b. You may also indicate a cell range that contains the search criterion. If you search for literal text, enclose the text in double quotes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3165037				0	uz	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3166505				0	uz	A1:A10 is a cell range containing the numbers \<item type=\"input\"\>2000\</item\> to \<item type=\"input\"\>2009\</item\>. Cell B1 contains the number \<item type=\"input\"\>2006\</item\>. In cell B2, you enter a formula:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3581652				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=COUNTIF(A1:A10;2006)\</item\> - this returns 1				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id708639				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=COUNTIF(A1:A10;B1)\</item\> - this returns 1				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id5169225				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=COUNTIF(A1:A10;">=2006") \</item\>- this returns 3				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id2118594				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=COUNTIF(A1:A10;"<"&B1)\</item\> - when B1 contains \<item type=\"input\"\>2006\</item\>, this returns 6				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id166020				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=COUNTIF(A1:A10;C2)\</item\> where cell C2 contains the text \<item type=\"input\"\>>2006\</item\> counts the number of cells in the range A1:A10 which are >2006 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id6386913				0	uz	To count only negative numbers: \<item type=\"input\"\>=COUNTIF(A1:A10;"<0")\</item\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_today.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	TODAY				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_today.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145659				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>TODAY function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_today.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145659				0	uz	\<variable id=\"today\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/func_today.xhp\"\>TODAY\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_today.xhp	0	help	par_id3153759				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_HEUTE\"\>Returns the current computer system date.\</ahelp\> The value is updated when you reopen the document or modify the values of the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_today.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154051				0	uz	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_today.xhp	0	help	par_id3153154				0	uz	TODAY()				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_today.xhp	0	help	par_id3154741				0	uz	 TODAY is a function without arguments.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_today.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153627				0	uz	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_today.xhp	0	help	par_id3156106				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>TODAY()\</item\> returns the current computer system date.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days360.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	DAYS360 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days360.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148555				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>DAYS360 function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days360.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148555				0	uz	\<variable id=\"days360\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/func_days360.xhp\"\>DAYS360\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days360.xhp	0	help	par_id3156032				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_TAGE360\"\>Returns the difference between two dates based on the 360 day year used in interest calculations.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days360.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155347				0	uz	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days360.xhp	0	help	par_id3155313				0	uz	DAYS360("Date1"; "Date2"; Type)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days360.xhp	0	help	par_id3145263				0	uz	If \<emph\>Date2\</emph\> is earlier than \<emph\>Date1\</emph\>, the function will return a negative number.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days360.xhp	0	help	par_id3151064				0	uz	The optional argument \<emph\>Type\</emph\> determines the type of difference calculation. If Type = 0 or if the argument is missing, the US method (NASD, National Association of Securities Dealers) is used. If Type <> 0, the European method is used.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days360.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148641				0	uz	Examples				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days360.xhp	0	help	par_id3156348				0	uz	=DAYS360("2000-01-01";NOW()) returns the number of interest days from January 1, 2000 until today.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_datevalue.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	DATEVALUE 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_datevalue.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145621				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>DATEVALUE function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_datevalue.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145621				0	uz	\<variable id=\"datevalue\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/func_datevalue.xhp\"\>DATEVALUE\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_datevalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3145087				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_DATWERT\"\>Returns the internal date number for text in quotes.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_datevalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3149281				0	uz	The internal date number is returned as a number. The number is determined by the date system that is used by $[officename] to calculate dates.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_datevalue.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156294				0	uz	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_datevalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3149268				0	uz	DATEVALUE("Text")				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_datevalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3154819	23			0	uz	\<emph\>Text\</emph\> is a valid date expression and must be entered with quotation marks.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_datevalue.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156309				0	uz	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_datevalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3155841	25			0	uz	\<emph\>=DATEVALUE("1954-07-20")\</emph\> yields 19925.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Database Functions				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148946				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>Function Wizard; databases\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>functions; database functions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>databases; functions in $[officename] Calc\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148946				0	uz	Database Functions				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3145173	2			0	uz	\<variable id=\"datenbanktext\"\>This section deals with functions used with data organized as one row of data for one record. \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154016				0	uz	The Database category may be confused with a database integrated in $[officename]. However, there is no connection between a database in $[officename] and the Database category in $[officename] Calc.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
