helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12080200.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153561				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>tables; showing details\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12080200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153561				0	uz	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12080200.xhp\" name=\"Show Details\"\>Show Details\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12080200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153822				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ShowDetail\"\>Shows the details of the grouped row or column that contains the cursor. To show the details of all of the grouped rows or columns, select the outlined table, and then choose this command.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12080200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155922	3			0	uz	To hide a selected group, choose \<emph\>Data -Outline –\</emph\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12080100.xhp\" name=\"Hide Details\"\>\<emph\>Hide Details\</emph\>\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Trace Precedents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030100.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155628				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>cells; tracing precedents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formula cells;tracing precedents\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155628				0	uz	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06030100.xhp\" name=\"Trace Precedents\"\>Trace Precedents\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153542				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ShowPrecedents\"\>This function shows the relationship between the current cell containing a formula and the cells used in the formula.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147265				0	uz	Traces are displayed in the sheet with marking arrows. At the same time, the range of all the cells contained in the formula of the current cell is highlighted with a blue frame.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154321				0	uz	This function is based on a principle of layers. For example, if the precedent cell to a formula is already indicated with a tracer arrow, when you repeat this command, the tracer arrows are drawn to the precedent cells of this cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060200.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Protecting document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150541				0	uz	Protecting document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145172				0	uz	\<variable id=\"dokumenttext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ToolProtectionDocument\"\>Protects the sheet structure of your document from modifications. It is impossible to insert, delete, rename, move or copy sheets.\</ahelp\>\</variable\> Open the \<emph\>Protect document\</emph\> dialog with \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document - Document\</emph\>. Optionally enter a password and click OK.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153188				0	uz	The structure of protected spreadsheet documents can be changed only if the \<emph\>Protect\</emph\> option is disabled. On the context menus for the spreadsheet tabs at the lower graphic border, only the menu item \<emph\>Select All Sheets\</emph\> can be activated. All other menu items are deactivated. To remove the protection, call up the command \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document - Document\</emph\> again. If no password is assigned, protection is immediately removed. If you were assigned a password, the \<emph\>Remove Spreadsheet Protection\</emph\> dialog appears, in which you must enter the password. Only then can you remove the check mark specifying that protection is active.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145750	7			0	uz	A protected document, once saved, can only be saved again with the \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\> menu command. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152596				0	uz	Password (optional)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155412				0	uz	You can create a password to protect your document against unauthorized or accidental modifications.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150717	9			0	uz	You can completely protect your work by combining both options from \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document\</emph\>, including password entry. If you want to prevent the document from being opened by other users, select \<emph\>Save With Password \</emph\>and click the \<emph\>Save\</emph\> button. The \<emph\>Enter Password\</emph\> dialog appears. Consider carefully when choosing a password; if you forget it after you close a document you will be unable to access the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Statistical Functions Part One				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146320				0	uz	\<variable id=\"ae\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060181.xhp\"\>Statistical Functions Part One\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145632				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>INTERCEPT function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>points of intersection\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>intersections\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145632				0	uz	INTERCEPT				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3146887				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ACHSENABSCHNITT\"\>Calculates the point at which a line will intersect the y-values by using known x-values and y-values.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150374				0	uz	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3149718				0	uz	INTERCEPT(DataY; DataX)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3149947	6			0	uz	\<emph\>DataY\</emph\> is the dependent set of observations or data.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3147412	7			0	uz	\<emph\>DataX\</emph\> is the independent set of observations or data.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3152983				0	uz	Names, arrays or references containing numbers must be used here. Numbers can also be entered directly.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157906				0	uz	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3148728				0	uz	To calculate the intercept, use cells D3:D9 as the y value and C3:C9 as the x value from the example spreadsheet. Input will be as follows:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3149013	11			0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=INTERCEPT(D3:D9;C3:C9)\</item\> = 2.15.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148437				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>COUNT function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>numbers;counting\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148437				0	uz	COUNT				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3150700				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ANZAHL\"\>Counts how many numbers are in the list of arguments.\</ahelp\> Text entries are ignored.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153930				0	uz	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3148585				0	uz	COUNT(Value1; Value2; ... Value30)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3155827	17			0	uz	\<emph\>Value1; Value2, ...\</emph\> are 1 to 30 values or ranges representing the values to be counted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149254				0	uz	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3149953				0	uz	The entries 2, 4, 6 and eight in the Value 1-4 fields are to be counted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3154558	20			0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=COUNT(2;4;6;"eight")\</item\> = 3. The count of numbers is therefore 3.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149729				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>COUNTA function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>number of entries\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149729				0	uz	COUNTA				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3150142				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ANZAHL2\"\>Counts how many values are in the list of arguments.\</ahelp\> Text entries are also counted, even when they contain an empty string of length 0. If an argument is an array or reference, empty cells within the array or reference are ignored.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148573				0	uz	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3153111				0	uz	COUNTA(Value1; Value2; ... Value30)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3150001	26			0	uz	\<emph\>Value1; Value2, ...\</emph\> are 1 to 30 arguments representing the values to be counted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150334				0	uz	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3154508				0	uz	The entries 2, 4, 6 and eight in the Value 1-4 fields are to be counted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3158000	29			0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=COUNTA(2;4;6;"eight")\</item\> = 4. The count of values is therefore 4.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150267				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>B function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>probabilities of samples with binomial distribution\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150267				0	uz	B				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3156061				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_B\"\>Returns the probability of a sample with binomial distribution.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150659				0	uz	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3148392				0	uz	B(Trials; SP; T1; T2)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3149002	35			0	uz	\<emph\>Trials\</emph\> is the number of independent trials.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3148875	36			0	uz	\<emph\>SP\</emph\> is the probability of success on each trial.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3145352	37			0	uz	\<emph\>T1\</emph\> defines the lower limit for the number of trials.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3149538	38			0	uz	\<emph\>T2\</emph\> (optional) defines the upper limit for the number of trials.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148768				0	uz	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3154633				0	uz	What is the probability with ten throws of the dice, that a six will come up exactly twice? The probability of a six (or any other number) is 1/6. The following formula combines these factors:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3149393	41			0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=B(10;1/6;2)\</item\> returns a probability of 29%.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	bm_id3158416				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>RSQ function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>determination coefficients\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>regression analysis\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158416				0	uz	RSQ				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3154949				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_BESTIMMTHEITSMASS\"\>Returns the square of the Pearson correlation coefficient based on the given values.\</ahelp\> RSQ (also called determination coefficient) is a measure for the accuracy of an adjustment and can be used to produce a regression analysis.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152820				0	uz	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3155822				0	uz	RSQ(DataY; DataX)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3150470	47			0	uz	\<emph\>DataY\</emph\> is an array or range of data points.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3153181	48			0	uz	\<emph\>DataX\</emph\> is an array or range of data points.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156258				0	uz	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3155991	50			0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=RSQ(A1:A20;B1:B20)\</item\> calculates the correlation coefficient for both data sets in columns A and B.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145620				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>BETAINV function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cumulative probability density function;inverse of\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145620				0	uz	BETAINV				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3149825				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_BETAINV\"\>Returns the inverse of the cumulative beta probability density function.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152479				0	uz	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3156300				0	uz	BETAINV(Number; Alpha; Beta; Start; End)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3149266	56			0	uz	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the value between \<emph\>Start\</emph\> and \<emph\>End\</emph\> at which to evaluate the function.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3149710	57			0	uz	\<emph\>Alpha\</emph\> is a parameter to the distribution.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3156306	58			0	uz	\<emph\>Beta\</emph\> is a parameter to the distribution.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3150960	59			0	uz	\<emph\>Start\</emph\> (optional) is the lower bound for \<emph\>Number\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3151268	60			0	uz	\<emph\>End\</emph\> (optional) is the upper bound for \<emph\>Number\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147077				0	uz	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3146859	62			0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=BETAINV(0.5;5;10)\</item\> returns the value 0.33.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156096				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>BETADIST function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cumulative probability density function;calculating\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156096				0	uz	BETADIST				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150762				0	uz	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3147571				0	uz	BETADIST(Number; Alpha; Beta; Start; End)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3156317	68			0	uz	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the value between \<emph\>Start\</emph\> and \<emph\>End\</emph\> at which to evaluate the function.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3156107	69			0	uz	\<emph\>Alpha\</emph\> is a parameter to the distribution.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3153619	70			0	uz	\<emph\>Beta\</emph\> is a parameter to the distribution.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3150254	71			0	uz	\<emph\>Start\</emph\> (optional) is the lower bound for \<emph\>Number\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3149138	72			0	uz	\<emph\>End\</emph\> (optional) is the upper bound for \<emph\>Number\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145649				0	uz	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3156118	74			0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=BETADIST(0.75;3;4)\</item\> returns the value 0.96				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	bm_id3143228				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>BINOMDIST function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143228				0	uz	BINOMDIST				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3146897				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_BINOMVERT\"\>Returns the individual term binomial distribution probability.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149289				0	uz	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3156009				0	uz	BINOMDIST(X; Trials; SP; C)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3154304	80			0	uz	\<emph\>X\</emph\> is the number of successes in a set of trials.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3147492	81			0	uz	\<emph\>Trials\</emph\> is the number of independent trials.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3146085	82			0	uz	\<emph\>SP\</emph\> is the probability of success on each trial.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3149760	83			0	uz	\<emph\>C\</emph\> = 0 calculates the probability of a single event and \<emph\>C\</emph\> = 1 calculates the cumulative probability.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151171				0	uz	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3145666	85			0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=BINOMDIST(A1;12;0.5;0)\</item\> shows (if the values \<item type=\"input\"\>0\</item\> to \<item type=\"input\"\>12\</item\> are entered in A1) the probabilities for 12 flips of a coin that \<emph\>Heads\</emph\> will come up exactly the number of times entered in A1.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3150120	86			0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=BINOMDIST(A1;12;0.5;1)\</item\> shows the cumulative probabilities for the same series. For example, if A1 = \<item type=\"input\"\>4\</item\>, the cumulative probability of the series is 0, 1, 2, 3 or 4 times \<emph\>Heads\</emph\> (non-exclusive OR).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	bm_id0119200902432928				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>CHIINV function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id0119200902421451				0	uz	CHIINV				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id0119200902475241				0	uz	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id0119200902475286				0	uz	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the probability value for which the inverse Gamma distribution is to be calculated.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id0119200902475282				0	uz	\<emph\>DegreesFreedom\</emph\> is the degrees of freedom of the experiment.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148835				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>CHIINV function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148835				0	uz	CHIINV				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3149906				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_CHIINV\"\>Returns the inverse of the one-tailed probability of the chi-squared distribution.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159157				0	uz	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3150504				0	uz	CHIINV(Number; DegreesFreedom)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3154898	92			0	uz	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the value of the error probability.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3154294	93			0	uz	\<emph\>DegreesFreedom\</emph\> is the degrees of freedom of the experiment.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154208				0	uz	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3150777				0	uz	A die is thrown 1020 times. The numbers on the die 1 through 6 come up 195, 151, 148, 189, 183 and 154 times (observation values). The hypothesis that the die is not fixed is to be tested.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3153062				0	uz	The Chi square distribution of the random sample is determined by the formula given above. Since the expected value for a given number on the die for n throws is n times 1/6, thus 1020/6 = 170, the formula returns a Chi square value of 13.27.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3148806				0	uz	If the (observed) Chi square is greater than or equal to the (theoretical) Chi square CHIINV, the hypothesis will be discarded, since the deviation between theory and experiment is too great. If the observed Chi square is less that CHIINV, the hypothesis is confirmed with the indicated probability of error.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3149763	95			0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=CHIINV(0.05;5)\</item\> returns 11.07.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3159142	133			0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=CHIINV(0.02;5)\</item\> returns 13.39.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3158401				0	uz	If the probability of error is 5%, the die is not true. If the probability of error is 2%, there is no reason to believe it is fixed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154260				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>CHITEST function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154260				0	uz	CHITEST				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3151052				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_CHITEST\"\>Returns the probability of a deviance from a random distribution of two test series based on the chi-squared test for independence.\</ahelp\> CHITEST returns the chi-squared distribution of the data.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3148925				0	uz	The probability determined by CHITEST can also be determined with CHIDIST, in which case the Chi square of the random sample must then be passed as a parameter instead of the data row.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154280				0	uz	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3149162				0	uz	CHITEST(DataB; DataE)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3158421	101			0	uz	\<emph\>DataB\</emph\> is the array of the observations.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3166453	102			0	uz	\<emph\>DataE\</emph\> is the range of the expected values.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146946				0	uz	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3154096				0	uz	Data_B (observed)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3152948				0	uz	Data_E (expected)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3152876				0	uz	1				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3149922				0	uz	2				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3149417				0	uz	3				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3148467				0	uz	4				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3149927				0	uz	5				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3143275				0	uz	6				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3149481	104			0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=CHITEST(A1:A6;B1:B6)\</item\> equals 0.02. This is the probability which suffices the observed data of the theoretical Chi-square distribution.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148690				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>CHIDIST function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148690				0	uz	CHIDIST				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3156338				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_CHIVERT\"\>Returns the probability value from the indicated Chi square that a hypothesis is confirmed.\</ahelp\> CHIDIST compares the Chi square value to be given for a random sample that is calculated from the sum of (observed value-expected value)^2/expected value for all values with the theoretical Chi square distribution and determines from this the probability of error for the hypothesis to be tested.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3151316				0	uz	The probability determined by CHIDIST can also be determined by CHITEST.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155123				0	uz	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3158439				0	uz	CHIDIST(Number; DegreesFreedom)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3148675	110			0	uz	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the chi-square value of the random sample used to determine the error probability.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3155615	111			0	uz	\<emph\>DegreesFreedom\</emph\> are the degrees of freedom of the experiment.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146787				0	uz	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3145774	113			0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=CHIDIST(13.27; 5)\</item\> equals 0.02.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3156141				0	uz	If the Chi square value of the random sample is 13.27 and if the experiment has 5 degrees of freedom, then the hypothesis is assured with a probability of error of 2%.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	bm_id0119200902231887				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>LOGNORMDIST function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cumulative lognormal distribution\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id0119200901583452				0	uz	CHIDIST				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id0119200902395520				0	uz	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id011920090239564				0	uz	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the value for which the F distribution is to be calculated.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id0119200902395660				0	uz	\<emph\>DegreesFreedom\</emph\> is the degrees of freedom of the experiment.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150603				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>EXPONDIST function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>exponential distributions\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150603				0	uz	EXPONDIST				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3149563				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_EXPONVERT\"\>Returns the exponential distribution.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153789				0	uz	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3150987				0	uz	EXPONDIST(Number; Lambda; C)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3154663	119			0	uz	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the value of the function.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3154569	120			0	uz	\<emph\>Lambda\</emph\> is the parameter value.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3147332	121			0	uz	\<emph\>C\</emph\> is a logical value that determines the form of the function. \<emph\>C = 0\</emph\> calculates the density function, and \<emph\>C = 1\</emph\> calculates the distribution.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146133				0	uz	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3150357	123			0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=EXPONDIST(3;0.5;1)\</item\> returns 0.78.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12050100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	1st, 2nd, 3rd Group				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12050100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149784				0	uz	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12050100.xhp\" name=\"1st, 2nd, 3rd Group\"\>1st, 2nd, 3rd Group\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12050100.xhp	0	help	par_id3145068				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SCPAGE_SUBT_GROUP1\"\>Specify the settings for up to three subtotal groups. Each tab has the same layout.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12050100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148797				0	uz	To insert subtotal values into a table:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12050100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154908				0	uz	Ensure that the columns of the table have labels.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12050100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153968	4			0	uz	Select the table or the area in the table that you want to calculate subtotals for, and then choose \<emph\>Data – Subtotals\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12050100.xhp	0	help	par_id3161831				0	uz	In the \<emph\>Group By\</emph\> box, select the column that you want to add the subtotals to.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12050100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153188				0	uz	In the \<emph\>Calculate subtotals for\</emph\> box, select the check boxes for the columns containing the values that you want to subtotal.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12050100.xhp	0	help	par_id3152460				0	uz	In the \<emph\>Use function\</emph\> box, select the function that you want to use to calculate the subtotals.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12050100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154321				0	uz	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12050100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156441				0	uz	Group by				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12050100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154013				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SC_SUBT_GROUP\"\>Select the column that you want to control the subtotal calculation process. If the contents of the selected column change, the subtotals are automatically recalculated.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12050100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154943				0	uz	Calculate subtotals for				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12050100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147125				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SC_SUBT_COLS\"\>Select the column(s) containing the values that you want to subtotal.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12050100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156283				0	uz	Use function				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12050100.xhp	0	help	par_id3145647				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SC_SUBT_FUNC\"\>Select the mathematical function that you want to use to calculate the subtotals.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12010100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Options				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12010100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154760				0	uz	Options				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12010100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153379				0	uz	Contains column labels				2002-02-02 02:02:02
