helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	DAYS 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151328				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>DAYS function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151328				0	uz	\<variable id=\"days\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/func_days.xhp\"\>DAYS\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days.xhp	0	help	par_id3155139				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_TAGE\"\>Calculates the difference between two date values.\</ahelp\> The result returns the number of days between the two days.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155184				0	uz	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days.xhp	0	help	par_id3149578				0	uz	DAYS(Date2; Date1)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days.xhp	0	help	par_id3151376				0	uz	\<emph\>Date1\</emph\> is the start date, \<emph\>Date2\</emph\> is the end date. If \<emph\>Date2\</emph\> is an earlier date than \<emph\>Date1\</emph\> the result is a negative number.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151001				0	uz	Examples				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days.xhp	0	help	par_id3159101				0	uz	=DAYS("2010-01-01"; NOW()) returns the number of days from today until January 1, 2010.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days.xhp	0	help	par_id3163720				0	uz	=DAYS("1990-10-10";"1980-10-10") returns 3652 days.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080300.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Edit Print Ranges				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153088				0	uz	Edit Print Ranges				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080300.xhp	0	help	par_id3159488				0	uz	\<variable id=\"druckbereichetext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:EditPrintArea\"\>Opens a dialog where you can specify the print range.\</ahelp\>\</variable\> You can also set the rows or columns which are to be repeated in every page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080300.xhp	0	help	par_idN105AE				0	uz	\<embedvar href=\"text/scalc/guide/printranges.xhp#printranges\"/\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156281				0	uz	Print range				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080300.xhp	0	help	par_id3147228				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:EDIT:RID_SCDLG_AREAS:ED_PRINTAREA\"\>Allows you to modify a defined print range.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080300.xhp	0	help	par_id3145174				0	uz	Select \<emph\>-none-\</emph\> to remove a print range definition for the current spreadsheet. Select \<emph\>-entire sheet-\</emph\> to set the current sheet as a print range. Select \<emph\>-selection-\</emph\> to define the selected area of a spreadsheet as the print range. By selecting \<emph\>-user-defined-\</emph\>, you can define a print range that you have already defined using the \<emph\>Format - Print Ranges - Define\</emph\> command. If you have given a name to a range using the \<emph\>Insert - Names - Define\</emph\> command, this name will be displayed and can be selected from the list box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080300.xhp	0	help	par_id3145272				0	uz	In the right-hand text box, you can enter a print range by reference or by name. If the cursor is in the \<emph\>Print range\</emph\> text box, you can also select the print range in the spreadsheet with your mouse.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149260				0	uz	Rows to repeat				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080300.xhp	0	help	par_id3147426				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:EDIT:RID_SCDLG_AREAS:ED_REPEATROW\"\>Choose one or more rows to print on every page. In the right text box enter the row reference, for example, "1" or $1" or "$2:$3".\</ahelp\> The list box displays \<emph\>-user defined-\</emph\>. You can also select \<emph\>-none-\</emph\> to remove a defined repeating row.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080300.xhp	0	help	par_id3155418				0	uz	You can also define repeating rows by dragging the mouse in the spreadsheet, if the cursor is in the \<emph\>Rows to repeat\</emph\> text field in the dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149581				0	uz	Columns to repeat				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080300.xhp	0	help	par_id3155602				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:EDIT:RID_SCDLG_AREAS:ED_REPEATCOL\"\>Choose one or more columns to print on every page. In the right text box enter the column reference, for example, "A" or "AB" or "$C:$E".\</ahelp\> The list box then displays \<emph\>-user defined-\</emph\>. You can also select \<emph\>-none-\</emph\> to remove a defined repeating column.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05080300.xhp	0	help	par_id3150749				0	uz	You can also define repeating columns by dragging the mouse in the spreadsheet, if the cursor is in the \<emph\>Columns to repeat\</emph\> text field in the dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\03100000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Page Break Preview				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\03100000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151384				0	uz	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/03100000.xhp\" name=\"Page Break Preview\"\>Page Break Preview\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\03100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150792				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:PagebreakMode\"\>Display the page breaks and print ranges in the sheet. Choose \<emph\>View - Normal\</emph\> to switch this mode off.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\03100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153877				0	uz	The context menu of the page break preview contains functions for editing page breaks, including the following options:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\03100000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154731				0	uz	Delete All Manual Breaks				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\03100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149400				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:DeleteAllBreaks\"\>Deletes all manual breaks in the current sheet.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\03100000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155067				0	uz	Add Print Range				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\03100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155764				0	uz	Adds the selected cells to print ranges.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
