helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145787				0	uz	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05050300.xhp\" name=\"Show\"\>Show\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150542				0	uz	If a sheet has been hidden, the Show Sheet dialog opens, which allows you to select a sheet to be shown again.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05050000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10656				0	uz	Right-To-Left				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05050000.xhp	0	help	par_idN1065A				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:SheetRightToLeft\"\>Changes the orientation of the current sheet to Right-To-Left if \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01150300.xhp\"\>CTL\</link\> support is enabled.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	WORKDAY				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149012				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>WORKDAY function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149012				0	uz	\<variable id=\"workday\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/func_workday.xhp\"\>WORKDAY\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	par_id3149893				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_WORKDAY\"\> The result is a date number that can be formatted as a date. You then see the date of a day that is a certain number of \<emph\>workdays\</emph\> away from the \<emph\>start date\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146944				0	uz	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	par_id3154844				0	uz	WORKDAY(StartDate; Days; Holidays)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	par_id3147469				0	uz	\<emph\>StartDate\</emph\> is the date from when the calculation is carried out. If the start date is a workday, the day is included in the calculation.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	par_id3153038				0	uz	\<emph\>Days\</emph\> is the number of workdays. Positive value for a result after the start date, negative value for a result before the start date.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	par_id3150693				0	uz	\<emph\>Holidays\</emph\> is a list of optional holidays. These are non-working days. Enter a cell range in which the holidays are listed individually.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150141				0	uz	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	par_id3152782				0	uz	What date came 17 workdays after 1 December 2001? Enter the start date "2001-12-01" in C3 and the number of workdays in D3. Cells F3 to J3 contain the following Christmas and New Year holidays: "2001-12-24", "2001-12-25", "2001-12-26", "2001-12-31", "2002-01-01".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	par_id3146142				0	uz	=WORKDAY(C3;D3;F3:J3) returns 2001-12-28. Format the serial date number as a date, for example in the format YYYY-MM-DD.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_year.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	YEAR				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_year.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153982				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>YEAR function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_year.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153982				0	uz	\<variable id=\"year\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/func_year.xhp\"\>YEAR\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_year.xhp	0	help	par_id3147496				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_JAHR\"\>Returns the year as a number according to the internal calculation rules.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_year.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146090				0	uz	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_year.xhp	0	help	par_id3154304				0	uz	YEAR(Number)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_year.xhp	0	help	par_id3156013				0	uz	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> shows the internal date value for which the year is to be returned.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_year.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152797				0	uz	Examples				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_year.xhp	0	help	par_id3145668				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=YEAR(1)\</item\> returns 1899				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_year.xhp	0	help	par_id3151168				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=YEAR(2)\</item\> returns 1900				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_year.xhp	0	help	par_id3150115				0	uz	\<item type=\"input\"\>=YEAR(33333.33)\</item\> returns 1991				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02180000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Move or Copy a Sheet				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02180000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153360				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; moving\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; copying\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>moving; spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copying; spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02180000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153360				0	uz	Move or Copy a Sheet				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02180000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154686				0	uz	\<variable id=\"tabelleverschiebenkopierentext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Move\"\>Moves or copies a sheet to a new location in the document or to a different document.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02180000.xhp	0	help	par_id2282479				0	uz	When you copy and paste cells containing \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060102.xhp\"\>date values\</link\> between different spreadsheets, both spreadsheet documents must be set to the same date base. If date bases differ, the displayed date values will change!				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02180000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163710				0	uz	To Document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02180000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148645				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:LISTBOX:RID_SCDLG_MOVETAB:LB_DEST\"\>Indicates where the current sheet is to be moved or copied to.\</ahelp\> Select \<emph\>new document\</emph\> if you want to create a new location for the sheet to be moved or copied.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02180000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154012				0	uz	Insert Before				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02180000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145366				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:LISTBOX:RID_SCDLG_MOVETAB:LB_INSERT\"\>The current sheet is moved or copied in front of the selected sheet.\</ahelp\> The \<emph\>move to end position\</emph\> option places the current sheet at the end.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02180000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153726				0	uz	Nusxa olish				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02180000.xhp	0	help	par_id3144764				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCDLG_MOVETAB:BTN_COPY\"\>Specifies that the sheet is to be copied. If the option is unmarked, the sheet is moved.\</ahelp\> Moving sheets is the default.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
