helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\specialfilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153566				0	uz	Specify that only rows which either have the value \<item type=\"literal\"\>January\</item\> in the \<emph\>Month\</emph\> cells OR a value of under 160000 in the \<emph\>Standard\</emph\> cells will be displayed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\specialfilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147372				0	uz	Choose \<emph\>Data - Filter - Advanced Filter\</emph\>, and then select the range A20:E22. After you click OK, only the filtered rows will be displayed. The other rows will be hidden from view.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Cells in Currency Format				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156329				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>currency formats; spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; currency formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>international currency formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formats; currency formats in cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>currencies; default currencies\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defaults;currency formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing;currency formats\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156329				0	uz	\<variable id=\"currency_format\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/currency_format.xhp\" name=\"Cells in Currency Format\"\>Cells in Currency Format\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3150010				0	uz	Exchanging of \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc documents can lead to misunderstandings, if your \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc document is loaded by a user who uses a different default currency format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3156442				0	uz	In \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc you can define that a number that you have formatted as "1,234.50 €", still remains in euros in another country and does not become dollars.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3150749				0	uz	For example, if the language is set to "Default" and you are using a german locale setting, the currency format will be "1.234,00 €". A point is used before the thousand digits and a comma before the decimal places. If you now select the subordinate currency format "$ English (US)" from the \<emph\>Format\</emph\> list box , you will get the following format: "$ 1.234,00". As you can see, the separators have remained the same. Only the currency symbol has been changed and converted, but the underlying format of the notation remains the same as in the locale setting.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3145640				0	uz	If, under \<emph\>Language\</emph\>, you convert the cells to "English (US)", the English-language locale setting is also transferred and the default currency format is now "$ 1,234.00".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3154255				0	uz	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020300.xhp\" name=\"Format - Cell - Numbers\"\>Format - Cell - Numbers\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	User-defined Number Formats				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	bm_id3143268				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>numbers; user-defined formatting in tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting; user-defined numbers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>number formats; millions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>format codes; user-defined number formats\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143268				0	uz	\<variable id=\"format_value_userdef\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/format_value_userdef.xhp\" name=\"User-defined Number Formats\"\>User-defined Number Formats\</link\> \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3150400				0	uz	You can define your own number formats to display numbers in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3150767				0	uz	As an example, to display the number 10,200,000 as 10.2 Million:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3150868				0	uz	Select the cells to which you want to apply a new, user-defined format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3149664				0	uz	Choose \<emph\>Format - Cells - Numbers\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3149260				0	uz	In the \<emph\>Categories\</emph\> list box select "User-defined".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3148646				0	uz	In the \<emph\>Format code\</emph\> text box enter the following code:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
