helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Renaming Sheets				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150398				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>renaming sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheet tabs;renaming\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables;renaming\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>names; sheets\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150398				0	uz	\<variable id=\"rename_table\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/rename_table.xhp\" name=\"Renaming Sheets\"\>Renaming Sheets\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3155131				0	uz	Click the name of the sheet that you want to change.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3149260				0	uz	Enter a new name for the sheet and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3149667				0	uz	Alternatively, hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option key\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt key\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> and click on any sheet name and enter the new name directly.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id0909200810502833				0	uz	Sheet names can contain almost any character. Some naming restrictions apply when you want to save the spreadsheet to Microsoft Excel format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id090920081050283				0	uz	When saving to Microsoft Excel format, the following characters are not allowed in sheet names:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id090920081050281				0	uz	colon :				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id0909200810502897				0	uz	back slash \\				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id090920081050299				0	uz	forward slash /				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id0909200810502913				0	uz	question mark ?				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id090920081050298				0	uz	asterisk *				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id0909200810502969				0	uz	left square bracket [				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id0909200810502910				0	uz	right square bracket ]				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id0909200810502971				0	uz	single quote ' as the first or last character of the name				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id090920081050307				0	uz	In cell references, a sheet name has to be enclosed in single quotes ' if the name contains other characters than alphanumeric or underscore. A single quote contained within a name has to be escaped by doubling it (two single quotes). For example, you want to reference the cell A1 on a sheet with the following name:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id0909200810503071				0	uz	This year's sheet				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id0909200810503054				0	uz	The reference must be enclosed in single quotes, and the one single quote inside the name must be doubled:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id0909200810503069				0	uz	'This year''s sheet'.A1				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3155444				0	uz	The name of a sheet is independent of the name of the spreadsheet. You enter the spreadsheet name when you save it for the first time as a file. The document can contain up to 256 individual sheets, which can have different names.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Entering Values				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150868				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>values; inserting in multiple cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;values\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cell ranges;selecting for data entries\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>areas, see also cell ranges\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3405255				0	uz	\<variable id=\"cell_enter\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cell_enter.xhp\"\>Entering Values\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id7147129				0	uz	Calc can simplify entering data and values into multiple cells. You can change some settings to conform to your preferences.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id5621509				0	uz	To enter values into a range of cells manually				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id8200018				0	uz	There are two features that assist you when you enter a block of data manually.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id1867427				0	uz	Area detection for new rows				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id7908871				0	uz	In the row below a heading row, you can advance from one cell to the next with the \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Tab\</item\> key. After you enter the value into the last cell in the current row, press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Enter\</item\>. Calc positions the cursor below the first cell of the current block.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id6196783				0	uz	\<image id=\"img_id6473586\" src=\"res/helpimg/area1.png\" width=\"6.4437inch\" height=\"2.1252inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id6473586\"\>area detection\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3583788				0	uz	Area selection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id2011780				0	uz	Use drag-and-drop to select the area where you want to input values. But start dragging from the last cell of the area and release the mouse button when you have selected the first cell. Now you can start to input values. Always press the \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Tab\</item\> key to advance to the next cell. You will not leave the selected area.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id7044282				0	uz	\<image id=\"img_id2811365\" src=\"res/helpimg/area2.png\" width=\"6.4437inch\" height=\"2.1252inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id2811365\"\>area selection\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3232520				0	uz	Select the area from E7 to B3. Now B3 is waiting for your input. Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Tab\</item\> to advance to the next cell within the selected area.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id8950163				0	uz	To enter values to a range of cells automatically				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id633869				0	uz	See \<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/calc_series.xhp\"\>Automatically Filling in Data Based on Adjacent Cells\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_rotate.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Rotating Tables (Transposing)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_rotate.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154346				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>tables; transposing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>transposing tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inverting tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>swapping tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>columns; swap with rows\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rows; swapping with columns\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; rotating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rotating; tables\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_rotate.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154346				0	uz	\<variable id=\"table_rotate\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/table_rotate.xhp\" name=\"Rotating Tables (Transposing)\"\>Rotating Tables (Transposing)\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3154013				0	uz	In $[officename] Calc, there is a way to "rotate" a spreadsheet so that rows become columns and columns become rows.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3153142				0	uz	Select the cell range that you want to transpose.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3153191				0	uz	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Cut\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3148575				0	uz	Click the cell that is to be the top left cell in the result.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3156286				0	uz	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Paste Special\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3144764				0	uz	In the dialog, mark \<emph\>Paste all\</emph\> and \<emph\>Transpose\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3155600				0	uz	If you now click OK the columns and rows are transposed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3146969				0	uz	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/02070000.xhp\" name=\"Paste Special\"\>Paste Special\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Importing and Exporting dBASE Files 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	bm_id1226844				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>exporting;spreadsheets to dBASE\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>importing;dBASE files\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>dBASE import/export\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; importing from/exporting to dBASE files\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables in databases;importing dBASE files\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10738				0	uz	\<variable id=\"dbase_files\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/dbase_files.xhp\"\>Importing and Exporting dBASE Files\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10756				0	uz	You can open and save data in the dBASE file format (*.dbf file extension) in $[officename] Base or a spreadsheet. In %PRODUCTNAME Base, a dBASE database is a folder that contains files with the .dbf file extension. Each file corresponds to a table in the database. Formulas and formatting are lost when you open and save a dBASE file from %PRODUCTNAME.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10759				0	uz	To Import a dBASE File Into a Spreadsheet				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10760				0	uz	Choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1071F				0	uz	Locate the *.dbf file that you want to import. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10768				0	uz	Click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10730				0	uz	The \<emph\>Import dBASE files\</emph\> dialog opens.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10774				0	uz	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10777				0	uz	The dBASE file opens as a new Calc spreadsheet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1074E				0	uz	If you want to save the spreadsheet as a dBASE file, do not alter or delete the first row in the imported file. This row contains information that is required by a dBASE database.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1077A				0	uz	To Import a dBASE File Into a Database Table				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1076C				0	uz	A %PRODUCTNAME Base database table is actually a link to an existing database.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10796				0	uz	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - New - Database\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10786				0	uz	In the \<emph\>File name\</emph\> box of the \<emph\>Save As\</emph\> dialog, enter a name for the database.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10792				0	uz	Click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1079A				0	uz	In the \<emph\>Database type \</emph\>box of the \<emph\>Database Properties\</emph\> dialog, select "dBASE".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107A6				0	uz	Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107AE				0	uz	Click \<emph\>Browse\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107B6				0	uz	Locate the directory that contains the dBASE file, and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107BE				0	uz	Click \<emph\>Create\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F1				0	uz	To Export a Spreadsheet to a dBASE File				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F8				0	uz	Choose \<emph\>File - Save as\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10800				0	uz	In the \<emph\>File format\</emph\> box, select "dBASE file".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F9				0	uz	In the \<emph\>File name\</emph\> box, type a name for the dBASE file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10801				0	uz	Click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10808				0	uz	Only the data on the current sheet is exported.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Merging and Splitting Cells				2002-02-02 02:02:02
