helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Filtering Cell Ranges 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153541				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>cell ranges;applying/removing filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>filtering;cell ranges/database ranges\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>database ranges;applying/removing filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>removing;cell range filters\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153541				0	uz	\<variable id=\"database_filter\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/database_filter.xhp\" name=\"Filtering Cell Ranges\"\>Filtering Cell Ranges\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_id3145069				0	uz	You can use several filters to filter cell ranges in spreadsheets. A standard filter uses the options that you specify to filter the data. An AutoFilter filters data according to a specific value or string. An advanced filter uses filter criteria from specified cells.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10682				0	uz	To Apply a Standard Filter to a Cell Range				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150398				0	uz	Click in a cell range.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10693				0	uz	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data - Filter - Standard Filter\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_id3156422				0	uz	In the \<emph\>Standard Filter\</emph\> dialog, specify the filter options that you want.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A5				0	uz	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153143				0	uz	The records that match the filter options that you specified are shown.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153728				0	uz	To Apply an AutoFilter to a Cell Range				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_id3144764				0	uz	Click in a cell range or a database range.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_id9303872				0	uz	If you want to apply multiple AutoFilters to the same sheet, you must first define database ranges, then apply the AutoFilters to the database ranges.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_id3154944				0	uz	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data - Filter - AutoFilter\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_idN106DB				0	uz	An arrow button is added to the head of each column in the database range.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153878				0	uz	Click the arrow button in the column that contains the value or string that you want to set as the filter criteria.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10749				0	uz	Select the value or string that you want to use as the filter criteria.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_idN1074C				0	uz	The records that match the filter criteria that you selected are shown.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E8				0	uz	To Remove a Filter From a Cell Range				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_idN1075C				0	uz	Click in a filtered cell range.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_idN106EC				0	uz	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data - Filter - Remove Filter\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
