helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150769				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>series; calculating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>calculating; series\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>linear series\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>growth series\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>date series\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>powers of 2 calculations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; filling automatically\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>auto filling cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>AutoFill function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>filling;cells, automatically\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150769				0	uz	\<variable id=\"calc_series\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/calc_series.xhp\" name=\"Automatically Calculating Series\"\>Automatically Filling in Data Based on Adjacent Cells\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A8				0	uz	You can automatically fill cells with data with the AutoFill command or the Series command.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D3				0	uz	Using AutoFill				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D7				0	uz	AutoFill automatically generates a data series based on a defined pattern.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_id3154319				0	uz	On a sheet, click in cell, and type a number.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_idN106CB				0	uz	Click in another cell and then click back in the cell where you typed the number.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_id3145272				0	uz	Drag the fill handle in the bottom right corner of the cell across the cells that you want to fill, and release the mouse button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_id3145801				0	uz	The cells are filled with ascending numbers.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_idN106EE				0	uz	To quickly create a list of consecutive days, enter "Monday" in a cell, and drag the fill handle.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_id9720145				0	uz	Hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>if you do not want to fill the cells with different values.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_idN10737				0	uz	You can double-click the fill handle to automatically fill all empty columns of the current data block. For example, first enter Jan into A1 and drag the fill handle down to A12 to get the twelve months in the first column. Now enter some values into B1 and C1. Select those two cells, and double-click the fill handle. This fills automatically the data block B1:C12.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_idN10713				0	uz	Using a Defined Series				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_id3150749				0	uz	Select the cell range in the sheet that you want to fill.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_id3154754				0	uz	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit - Fill - Series\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_idN10716				0	uz	Select the parameters for the series. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_idN10731				0	uz	If you select a \<emph\>linear\</emph\> series, the increment that you enter is \<emph\>added\</emph\> to each consecutive number in the series to create the next value.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_idN1073C				0	uz	If you select a \<emph\>growth\</emph\> series, the increment that you enter is \<emph\>multiplied\</emph\> by each consecutive number to create the next value.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_idN10747				0	uz	If you select a \<emph\>date\</emph\> series, the increment that you enter is added to the time unit that you specify.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_id3159173				0	uz	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01060400.xhp\" name=\"Sort lists\"\>Sort lists\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	 Importing and Exporting CSV Files 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	bm_id892361				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>number series import\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data series import\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>exporting; tables as text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>importing; tables as text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>delimited values and files\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>comma separated files and values\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text file import and export\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>csv files;importing and exporting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; importing/exporting as text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text documents; importing to spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10862				0	uz	\<variable id=\"csv_files\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/csv_files.xhp\"\>Opening and Saving Text CSV Files\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10880				0	uz	Comma Separated Values (CSV) is text file format that you can use to exchange data from a database or a spreadsheet between applications. Each line in a Text CSV file represents a record in the database, or a row in a spreadsheet. Each field in a database record or cell in a spreadsheet row is usually separated by a comma. However, you can use other characters to delimit a field, such as a tabulator character.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10886				0	uz	If the content of a field or cell contains a comma, the contents of the field or cell \<emph\>must\</emph\> be enclosed by single quotes (') or double quotes (").				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10890				0	uz	To Open a Text CSV File in Calc				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10897				0	uz	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data - Sort\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1089F				0	uz	Locate the CSV file that you want to open.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN108A2				0	uz	If the file has a *.csv extension, select the file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN108A5				0	uz	If the CSV file has another extension, select the file, and then select "Text CSV" in the \<emph\>File type\</emph\> box				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1082D				0	uz	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data - Sort\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN108B1				0	uz	Specify the options to divide the text in the file into columns.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN108BB				0	uz	You can preview the layout of the imported data at the bottom of the \<emph\>Text Import\</emph\> dialog. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_id8444166				0	uz	Right-click a column in the preview to set the format or to hide the column.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN108C5				0	uz	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data - Sort\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN108FA				0	uz	To Save a Sheet as a Text CSV File				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN106FC				0	uz	When you export a spreadsheet to CSV format, only the data on the current sheet is saved. All other information, including formulas and formatting, is lost.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10901				0	uz	Open the Calc sheet that you want to save as a Text CSV file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
