helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2760093				0	uz	When you drag-and-drop a selection of cells on a Calc sheet, the cells normally overwrite the existing cells in the area where you drop. This is the normal \<emph\>overwrite mode\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id9527268				0	uz	When you hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key while releasing the mouse button, you enter the \<emph\>insert mode\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id79653				0	uz	In insert mode, the existing cells where you drop will be shifted to the right or to the bottom, and the dropped cells are inserted into the now empty positions without overwriting. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id8676717				0	uz	The surrounding box of the moved cells looks different in insert mode. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3968932				0	uz	In overwrite mode you see all four borders around the selected area. In insert mode you see only the left border when target cells will be shifted to the right. You see only the upper border when target cells will be shifted down. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id7399517				0	uz	Whether the target area will be shifted to the right or to the bottom depends on the distance between source and target cells, if you move within the same sheet. It depends on the number of horizontal or vertical cells in the moved area, if you move to a different sheet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id8040406				0	uz	If you move cells in insert mode within the same row (only horizontally), then after insertion of the cells, all cells will be shifted to the left to fill the source area.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2586748				0	uz	In both modes, you can hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>key, or \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift keys while you release the mouse button to insert a copy or a link, respectively.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id5814081				0	uz	Keys pressed while releasing the mouse button				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id6581316				0	uz	Result				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id9906613				0	uz	No key				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2815637				0	uz	Cells are moved and overwrite the cells in the target area. Source cells are emptied.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id6161687				0	uz	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>key				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id4278389				0	uz	Cells are copied and overwrite the cells in the target area. Source cells stay as they are.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2805566				0	uz	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift keys				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id5369121				0	uz	Links to the source cells are inserted and overwrite the cells in the target area. Source cells stay as they are.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id9518723				0	uz	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2926419				0	uz	Cells are moved and shift the cells in the target area to the right or to the bottom. Source cells are emptied, except if you move within the same rows on the same sheet. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id4021423				0	uz	If you move within the same rows on the same sheet, the cells in the target area shift to the right, and then the whole row shifts to fill the source area.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2783898				0	uz	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option+Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt+Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>keys				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2785119				0	uz	Cells are copied and shift the cells in the target area to the right or to the bottom. Source cells stay as they are.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id584124				0	uz	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option+Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt+Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift keys				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id5590990				0	uz	Links to the source cells are inserted and shift the cells in the target area to the right or to the bottom. Source cells stay as they are.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_view.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Changing Table Views				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_view.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147304				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>row headers; hiding\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>column headers; hiding\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; views\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>views; tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>grids;hiding lines in sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hiding;headers/grid lines\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing;table views\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
