helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_id3147262				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_FORMAT_CAT\"\>You can choose among various options for formatting a $[officename] Math formula. The format options are displayed in the lower half of the Selection window.\</ahelp\> These options are also listed in the \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000001.xhp#kontextmenue\" name=\"context menu\"\>context menu\</link\> of the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_id3153536				0	uz	The letter "a" refers to the placeholder in your formula which you would like to assign to the respective formatting. You can substitute this character for any other you like.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
