helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_id3149319				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_ALIGNCX\"\>Assigns horizontal central alignment to "a" and inserts a placeholder.\</ahelp\> You can also type \<emph\>alignc<?>\</emph\> directly in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_idN10352				0	uz	\<image id=\"img_id3155583\" src=\"starmath/res/co21911.png\" width=\"0.3335inch\" height=\"0.3335inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3155583\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_id3149768				0	uz	Align right				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_id3149780				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_ALIGNRX\"\>Inserts the command for right alignment and a placeholder.\</ahelp\> You can also type \<emph\>alignr<?>\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_idN1038D				0	uz	\<image id=\"img_id3155085\" src=\"starmath/res/co21907.png\" width=\"0.3335inch\" height=\"0.3335inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3155085\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_id3154338				0	uz	Matrix stack				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_id3146941				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_MATRIX\"\>This icon inserts a matrix with four placeholders.\</ahelp\> You can also type \<emph\>matrix{<?>#<?>##<?>#<?>}\</emph\> directly in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window. The position of an element inside this diagram is indicated by two coordinates; the first specifies the line number and the second the column number. You can expand this matrix in any direction in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window by adding characters.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_idN103C9				0	uz	\<image id=\"img_id3150027\" src=\"starmath/res/co21903.png\" width=\"0.3335inch\" height=\"0.3335inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3150027\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_id3149358				0	uz	Gap				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_id3149370				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_BLANK\"\>This icon inserts a gap or space between placeholders.\</ahelp\> You can also type \<emph\>~\</emph\> directly in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window. The command must appear to the left or right of a symbol, variable, number or complete command.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_id3155394	48			0	uz	For alignment, the \<emph\>alignl, alignc\</emph\> and \<emph\>alignr\</emph\> commands are especially effective, if you are 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_id3151009				0	uz	aligning numbers and denominators, for example \<emph\>{alignl a}over{b+c}\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_id3148812				0	uz	constructing binomials or stacks, for example \<emph\>binom{2*n}{alignr k}\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_id3154360				0	uz	aligning the elements in a matrix, for example \<emph\>matrix{alignr a#b+2##c+1/3#alignl d}\</emph\> and				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_id3155946				0	uz	beginning a new line, for example \<emph\>a+b-c newline alignr x/y\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_id3154621				0	uz	When using the align instructions, note that				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_id3147382				0	uz	they can only placed at the beginning of expressions and can only occur once. Therefore you can type \<emph\>a+b alignr c\</emph\>, but not \<emph\>a+alignr b\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_id3154004				0	uz	they affect each other, which means that typing \<emph\>{alignl{alignr a}}over{b+c}\</emph\> aligns \<emph\>a\</emph\> on the right.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	hd_id8036133				0	uz	To align using the "matrix" command				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_idN10F70				0	uz	Aligning to the left				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_id3149645				0	uz	If a line or an expression begins with text, it is aligned on the left by default. You can change this with any of the \<emph\>align\</emph\> commands. An example is \<emph\>stack{a+b-c*d#alignr "text"}\</emph\>, where "text" appears aligned to the right. Note that text must always be surrounded by quotation marks.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_id3149966				0	uz	The standard centralized formulas can be aligned to the left without using the \<emph\>Format - Alignment\</emph\> menu. To do this, place an empty character string, that is, the inverted commas which surround any text "", before the section of formula that you want to align. For example, typing \<emph\>"" a+b newline "" c+d\</emph\> results in both equations being left-aligned instead of centered.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_id3145654				0	uz	When typing information in the Commands window, note that some formats require spaces for the correct structure. This is especially true when entering values (for example, a lsup{3}) instead of placeholders.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_id3148708				0	uz	Click \<link href=\"text/smath/01/03091100.xhp\" name=\"Brackets and Grouping\"\>Brackets and Grouping\</link\> for more information about formatting in \<emph\>$[officename] Math\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_id3155340				0	uz	Useful information about \<link href=\"text/smath/01/03091200.xhp\" name=\"Indexes and Exponents\"\>Indexes and Exponents\</link\> and \<link href=\"text/smath/01/03091400.xhp\" name=\"Scaling\"\>Scaling\</link\>, helps you organize your document in the best possible way.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090906.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Matrix in Bold Font				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090906.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154704				0	uz	\<link href=\"text/smath/01/03090906.xhp\" name=\"Matrix in Bold Font\"\>Matrix in Bold Font\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090906.xhp	0	help	par_id3150342				0	uz	Here is an example of how to create a bold font matrix in \<emph\>$[officename] Math\</emph\>. You can copy this example to the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window using the clipboard and use it in your own formula.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090906.xhp	0	help	par_id3148866				0	uz	\<image id=\"img_id3150210\" src=\"res/helpimg/smzb6.png\" width=\"9.511cm\" height=\"7.99cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3150210\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090906.xhp	0	help	par_id3154763				0	uz	bold { f(x", "y) = left [ stack { x + y over z + left lbrace matrix { 2 # 3 # 4 ## 4 # 5 # 6 ## 6 # 7 # 8} right rbrace # {y + sin (x)} over %alpha # z + y over g } right ]}				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090901.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Symbols with Indices				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090901.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156382				0	uz	\<link href=\"text/smath/01/03090901.xhp\" name=\"Symbols with Indices\"\>Symbols with Indices\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090901.xhp	0	help	par_id3150301				0	uz	The following example explains how to create symbols with indexes in \<emph\>$[officename] Math\</emph\>. You can copy this example to the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window by using the clipboard and use it in your own formula.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
