helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3156102	39			0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_XCIRCY\"\>Inserts a \<emph\>concatenation sign\</emph\> with two placeholders. \</ahelp\> You can also type \<emph\>circ\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150906				0	uz	By typing \<emph\><?>oplus<?>\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window, you insert a \<emph\>circled plus operator\</emph\> in your document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3151197				0	uz	Type \<emph\><?>ominus<?>\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window to insert a \<emph\>circled minus operator\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155082				0	uz	Type \<emph\><?>odot<?>\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window to insert a \<emph\>circled dot operator\</emph\> in the formula.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154331				0	uz	Type \<emph\><?>odivide<?>\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window to insert a \<emph\>circled division operator\</emph\> in the formula.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150089				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_XWIDESLASHY\"\>Type \<emph\>a wideslash b\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window to produce two characters with a slash (from lower left to upper right) between them.\</ahelp\> The characters are set such that everything to the left of the slash is up, and everything to the right is down. This command is also available in the context menu of the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150024				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_XWIDEBSLASHY\"\>Type \<emph\>a widebslash b\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window to produce two characters with a slash (from upper left to lower right) between them.\</ahelp\> The characters are set such that everything to the left of the slash is down, and everything to the right is up. This command is also available in the context menu of the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149376				0	uz	Type \<emph\>sub\</emph\> or \<emph\>sup\</emph\> in the Commands window to add indexes and powers to the characters in your formula; for example, a sub 2.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147398				0	uz	When entering information manually in the Commands window, please note that a number of operators require spaces between the elements for the correct structure. This is especially true if you are using values instead of placeholders in your operators, for example, to construct a division 4 div 3 or a div b.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\02100000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Next Error				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\02100000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150299				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>error search; next error\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>finding ;errors in %PRODUCTNAME Math\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
