helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020202.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154908				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>Input statement\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154908				0	uz	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03020202.xhp\" name=\"Input# Statement [Runtime]\"\>Input# Statement [Runtime]\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020202.xhp	0	help	par_id3156424				0	uz	Reads data from an open sequential file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3125863				0	uz	Syntax:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020202.xhp	0	help	par_id3150440				0	uz	Input #FileNumber As Integer; var1[, var2[, var3[,...]]]				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146121				0	uz	Parameters:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020202.xhp	0	help	par_id3145749				0	uz	\<emph\>FileNumber:\</emph\> Number of the file that contains the data that you want to read. The file must be opened with the Open statement using the key word INPUT.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020202.xhp	0	help	par_id3150011				0	uz	\<emph\>var:\</emph\> A numeric or string variable that you assign the values read from the opened file to.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020202.xhp	0	help	par_id3159153				0	uz	The \<emph\>Input#\</emph\> statement reads numeric values or strings from an open file and assigns the data to one or more variables. A numeric variable is read up to the first carriage return (Asc=13), line feed (Asc=10), space, or comma. String variables are read to up to the first carriage return (Asc=13), line feed (Asc=10), or comma.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020202.xhp	0	help	par_id3146984				0	uz	Data and data types in the opened file must appear in the same order as the variables that are passed in the "var" parameter. If you assign non-numeric values to a numeric variable, "var" is assigned a value of "0".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020202.xhp	0	help	par_id3156442				0	uz	Records that are separated by commas cannot be assigned to a string variable. Quotation marks (") in the file are disregarded as well. If you want to read these characters from the file, use the \<emph\>Line Input#\</emph\> statement to read pure text files (files containing only printable characters) line by line.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020202.xhp	0	help	par_id3147349				0	uz	If the end of the file is reached while reading a data element, an error occurs and the process is aborted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152578				0	uz	Example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
