helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150616				0	uz	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03080201.xhp\" name=\"Exp Function [Runtime]\"\>Exp Function [Runtime]\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080201.xhp	0	help	par_id3155555				0	uz	Returns the base of the natural logarithm (e = 2.718282) raised to a power.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150984				0	uz	Syntax:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080201.xhp	0	help	par_id3145315				0	uz	Exp (Number)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154347				0	uz	Return value:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080201.xhp	0	help	par_id3149670				0	uz	Double				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154760				0	uz	Parameters:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080201.xhp	0	help	par_id3150793				0	uz	\<emph\>Number:\</emph\> Any numeric expression that specifies the power that you want to raise "e" to (the base of natural logarithms). The power must be for both single-precision numbers less than or equal to 88.02969 and double-precision numbers less than or equal to 709.782712893, since $[officename] Basic returns an Overflow error for numbers exceeding these values.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156280				0	uz	Example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
