helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146120				0	uz	This section describes how to assign Basic programs to program events.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149263				0	uz	You can automatically execute a macro when a specified software event occurs by assigning the desired macro to the event. The following table provides an overview of program events and at what point an assigned macro is executed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148455				0	uz	Event				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145799				0	uz	An assigned macro is executed...				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149379				0	uz	Program Start				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150715				0	uz	... after a $[officename] application is started.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146914				0	uz	Program End				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153765				0	uz	...before a $[officename] application is terminated.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145150				0	uz	Create Document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3163808				0	uz	...after a new document is created with \<emph\>File - New\</emph\> or with the \<emph\>New\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145790				0	uz	Open Document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154572				0	uz	...after a document is opened with \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\> or with the \<emph\>Open\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153266				0	uz	Save Document As				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150208				0	uz	...before a document is saved under a specified name (with \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\>, or with \<emph\>File - Save\</emph\> or the \<emph\>Save\</emph\> icon, if a document name has not yet been specified).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3158215				0	uz	Document has been saved as				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150980				0	uz	... after a document was saved under a specified name (with \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\>, or with \<emph\>File - Save\</emph\> or with the \<emph\>Save\</emph\> icon, if a document name has not yet been specified).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150519				0	uz	Save Document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155529				0	uz	...before a document is saved with \<emph\>File - Save\</emph\> or the \<emph\>Save\</emph\> icon, provided that a document name has already been specified.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149404				0	uz	Document has been saved				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151332				0	uz	...after a document is saved with \<emph\>File - Save\</emph\> or the \<emph\>Save\</emph\> icon, provided that a document name has already been specified.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146868				0	uz	...before a document is closed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148606				0	uz	...after a document was closed. Note that the "Save Document" event may also occur when the document is saved before closing.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3144772				0	uz	Activate Document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149442				0	uz	...after a document is brought to the foreground.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150888				0	uz	Deactivate Document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154060				0	uz	...after another document is brought to the foreground.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152384				0	uz	Print Document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152873				0	uz	...after the \<emph\>Print\</emph\> dialog is closed, but before the actual print process begins.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3159227				0	uz	JavaScript run-time error				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145362				0	uz	...when a JavaScript run-time error occurs.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154767				0	uz	Print Mail Merge				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153555				0	uz	...after the \<emph\>Print\</emph\> dialog is closed, but before the actual print process begins. This event occurs for each copy printed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156366				0	uz	Change of the page count				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154627				0	uz	...when the page count changes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154737				0	uz	Message received				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150952				0	uz	...if a message was received.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01040000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153299				0	uz	Assigning a Macro to an Event				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147244				0	uz	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Customize\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Events\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146098				0	uz	Select whether you want the assignment to be globally valid or just valid in the current document in the \<emph\>Save In\</emph\> listbox.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150431				0	uz	Select the event from the \<emph\>Event\</emph\> list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148742				0	uz	Click \<emph\>Macro\</emph\> and select the macro to be assigned to the selected event.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146321				0	uz	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to assign the macro.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147414				0	uz	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to close the dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01040000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154581				0	uz	Removing the Assignment of a Macro to an Event				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146883				0	uz	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Customize\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Events\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155909				0	uz	Select whether you want to remove a global assignment or an assignment that is just valid in the current document by selecting the option in the \<emph\>Save In\</emph\> listbox.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3159129				0	uz	Select the event that contains the assignment to be removed from the \<emph\>Event\</emph\> list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149143				0	uz	Click \<emph\>Remove\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149351				0	uz	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to close the dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020305.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Seek Statement [Runtime]				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020305.xhp	0	help	bm_id3159413				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>Seek statement\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020305.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159413				0	uz	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03020305.xhp\" name=\"Seek Statement [Runtime]\"\>Seek Statement [Runtime]\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020305.xhp	0	help	par_id3153381				0	uz	Sets the position for the next writing or reading in a file that was opened with the Open statement.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020305.xhp	0	help	par_id2100589				0	uz	For random access files, the Seek statement sets the number of the next record to be accessed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020305.xhp	0	help	par_id5444807				0	uz	For all other files, the Seek statement sets the byte position at which the next operation is to occur.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020305.xhp	0	help	par_id3156280				0	uz	See also: \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03020103.xhp\" name=\"Open\"\>Open\</link\>, \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03020304.xhp\" name=\"Seek\"\>Seek\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020305.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145785				0	uz	Syntax:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020305.xhp	0	help	par_id3145273				0	uz	Seek[#FileNumber], Position (As Long)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020305.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154321				0	uz	Parameters:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020305.xhp	0	help	par_id3153952	9			0	uz	\<emph\>FileNumber: \</emph\>The data channel number used in the Open statement.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020305.xhp	0	help	par_id3145366	10			0	uz	\<emph\>Position: \</emph\>Position for the next writing or reading. Position can be a number between 1 and 2,147,483,647. According to the file type, the position indicates the number of the record (files in the Random mode) or the byte position (files in the Binary, Output, Append or Input mode). The first byte in a file is position 1, the second byte is position 2, and so on.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\05060700.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Macro				2002-02-02 02:02:02
