helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150791				0	uz	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03020103.xhp\" name=\"Open Statement[Runtime]\"\>Open Statement[Runtime]\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020103.xhp	0	help	par_id3150769				0	uz	Opens a data channel.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147230				0	uz	Syntax:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020103.xhp	0	help	par_id3154124				0	uz	Open FileName As String [For Mode] [Access IOMode] [Protected] As [#]FileNumber As Integer [Len = DatasetLength]				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156280				0	uz	Parameters:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020103.xhp	0	help	par_id3155132	6			0	uz	\<emph\>FileName: \</emph\>Name and path of the file that you wan to open. If you try to read a file that does not exist (Access = Read), an error message appears. If you try to write to a file that does not exist (Access = Write), a new file is created.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020103.xhp	0	help	par_id3149262				0	uz	\<emph\>Mode:\</emph\> Keyword that specifies the file mode. Valid values: Append (append to sequential file), Binary (data can be accessed by bytes using Get and Put), Input (opens data channel for reading), Output (opens data channel for writing), and Random (edits relative files).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020103.xhp	0	help	par_id3154014				0	uz	\<emph\>IOMode:\</emph\> Keyword that defines the access type. Valid values: Read (read-only), Write (write-only), Read Write (both).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020103.xhp	0	help	par_id3150011				0	uz	\<emph\>Protected:\</emph\> Keyword that defines the security status of a file after opening. Valid values: Shared (file may be opened by other applications), Lock Read (file is protected against reading), Lock Write (file is protected against writing), Lock Read Write (denies file access).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020103.xhp	0	help	par_id3153190				0	uz	\<emph\>FileNumber:\</emph\> Any integer expression from 0 to 511 to indicate the number of a free data channel. You can then pass commands through the data channel to access the file. The file number must be determined by the FreeFile function immediately before the Open statement.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020103.xhp	0	help	par_id3151115				0	uz	\<emph\>DatasetLength:\</emph\> For random access files, set the length of the records.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020103.xhp	0	help	par_id3153418				0	uz	You can only modify the contents of a file that was opened with the Open statement. If you try to open a file that is already open, an error message appears.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149123				0	uz	Example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
