helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020405.xhp	0	help	par_id3151074				0	uz	\<emph\>FileNumber:\</emph\> The number of the file that was opened with the Open statement.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020405.xhp	0	help	par_id3144766				0	uz	\<emph\>Attribute:\</emph\> Integer expression that indicates the type of file information that you want to return. The following values are possible:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020405.xhp	0	help	par_id3147396				0	uz	1: The FileAttr-Function indicates the access mode of the file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020405.xhp	0	help	par_id3149959				0	uz	2: The FileAttr-Function returns the file access number of the operating system.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020405.xhp	0	help	par_id3154018				0	uz	If you specify a parameter attribute with a value of 1, the following return values apply:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020405.xhp	0	help	par_id3149124				0	uz	1 - INPUT (file open for input)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020405.xhp	0	help	par_id3156275				0	uz	2 - OUTPUT (file open for output)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020405.xhp	0	help	par_id3155066				0	uz	4 - RANDOM (file open for random access)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020405.xhp	0	help	par_id3148406				0	uz	8 - APPEND (file open for appending)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020405.xhp	0	help	par_id3154757				0	uz	32 - BINARY (file open in binary mode).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
