helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010102.xhp	0	help	par_id3147317	9			0	uz	\<emph\>DialogTitle\</emph\>: String expression displayed in the title bar of the dialog. If omitted, the name of the respective application is displayed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010102.xhp	0	help	par_id3153954	10			0	uz	\<emph\>Type\</emph\>: Any integer expression that specifies the dialog type and defines the number and type of buttons or icons displayed. \<emph\>Type\</emph\> represents a combination of bit patterns (dialog elements defined by adding the respective values):				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010102.xhp	0	help	par_id3154319	11			0	uz	\<emph\>Values\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010102.xhp	0	help	par_id3147397				0	uz	0 : Display OK button only.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010102.xhp	0	help	par_id3145646				0	uz	1 : Display OK and Cancel buttons.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010102.xhp	0	help	par_id3149410				0	uz	2 : Display Abort, Retry, and Ignore buttons.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010102.xhp	0	help	par_id3151075				0	uz	3 : Display Yes, No, and Cancel buttons.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010102.xhp	0	help	par_id3153878				0	uz	4 : Display Yes and No buttons.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010102.xhp	0	help	par_id3155601				0	uz	5 : Display Retry and Cancel buttons.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
