helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	par_id3154760				0	uz	Log (Number)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149457				0	uz	Return value:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	par_id3150791				0	uz	Double				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151211				0	uz	Parameters:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	par_id3151041				0	uz	\<emph\>Number:\</emph\> Any numeric expression that you want to calculate the natural logarithm for.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	par_id3150869				0	uz	The natural logarithm is the logarithm to the base e. Base e is a constant with an approximate value of 2.718282...				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	par_id3153968				0	uz	You can calculate logarithms to any base (n) for any number (x) by dividing the natural logarithm of x by the natural logarithm of n, as follows:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	par_id3145420				0	uz	Log n(x) = Log(x) / Log(n)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155131				0	uz	Example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	par_id3152463				0	uz	Sub ExampleLogExp				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	par_id3145750				0	uz	Dim a as Double				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	par_id3151116				0	uz	Dim const b1=12.345e12				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	par_id3146985				0	uz	Dim const b2=1.345e34				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	par_id3148616				0	uz	a=Exp( Log(b1)+Log(b2) )				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	par_id3149262				0	uz	MsgBox "" & a & chr(13) & (b1*b2) ,0,"Multiplication by logarithm function"				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	par_id3155411				0	uz	end sub				2002-02-02 02:02:02
