helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3156215				0	uz	Boolean expressions combined with AND only return the value \<emph\>True\</emph\> if both expressions evaluate to \<emph\>True\</emph\>:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150870				0	uz	\<emph\>True\</emph\> AND \<emph\>True\</emph\> returns \<emph\>True\</emph\>; for all other combinations the result is \<emph\>False\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153768				0	uz	The AND operator also performs a bitwise comparison of identically positioned bits in two numeric expressions.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
