helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153360				0	uz	Use File I/O functions to create and manage user-defined (data) files.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150398				0	uz	You can use these functions to support the creation of "relative" files, so that you can save and reload certain records by specifying their record number. File I/O functions can also help you manage your files by providing you with information such as file size, current path settings, or the creation date of a file or a directory.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
