helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080104.xhp	0	help	par_id3148663				0	uz	Determines the tangent of an angle. The angle is specified in radians.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080104.xhp	0	help	par_id3153379				0	uz	Using the angle Alpha, the Tan Function calculates the ratio of the length of the side opposite the angle to the length of the side adjacent to the angle in a right-angled triangle.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080104.xhp	0	help	par_id3154366				0	uz	Tan(Alpha) = side opposite the angle/side adjacent to angle				2002-02-02 02:02:02
