helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080103.xhp	0	help	par_id3149456				0	uz	Returns the sine of an angle. The angle is specified in radians. The result lies between -1 and 1.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080103.xhp	0	help	par_id3153379				0	uz	Using the angle Alpha, the Sin Function returns the ratio of the length of the opposite side of an angle to the length of the hypotenuse in a right-angled triangle.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080103.xhp	0	help	par_id3148798				0	uz	Sin(Alpha) = side opposite the angle/hypotenuse				2002-02-02 02:02:02
