helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080103.xhp	0	help	par_id3145786				0	uz	\<emph\>Number:\</emph\> Numeric expression that defines the angle in radians that you want to calculate the sine for.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080103.xhp	0	help	par_id3155413				0	uz	To convert degrees to radians, multiply degrees by Pi/180, and to convert radians to degrees, multiply radians by 180/Pi.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
