helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060300.xhp	0	help	par_id3150440				0	uz	If you use the Imp operator in Boolean expressions, False is only returned if the first expression evaluates to True and the second expression to False.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060300.xhp	0	help	par_id3163710				0	uz	If you use the Imp operator in bit expressions, a bit is deleted from the result if the corresponding bit is set in the first expression and the corresponding bit is deleted in the second expression.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
