helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03131800.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150040				0	uz	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03131800.xhp\" name=\"CreateUnoDialog Function [Runtime]\"\>CreateUnoDialog Function [Runtime]\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03131800.xhp	0	help	par_id3154186				0	uz	Creates a Basic Uno object that represents a Uno dialog control during Basic runtime.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03131800.xhp	0	help	par_id3153750				0	uz	Dialogs are defined in the dialog libraries. To display a dialog, a "live" dialog must be created from the library.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03131800.xhp	0	help	par_id3153681				0	uz	See \<link href=\"text/sbasic/guide/sample_code.xhp\" name=\"Examples\"\>Examples\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03131800.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154286				0	uz	Syntax:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03131800.xhp	0	help	par_id3159176				0	uz	CreateUnoDialog( oDlgDesc )				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03131800.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143270				0	uz	Example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03131800.xhp	0	help	par_id3159157				0	uz	' Get dialog description from the dialog library				2002-02-02 02:02:02
