helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154374				0	uz	Page (step)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154109				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Specify the number of the dialog page to which the current control is assigned or the page number of the dialog you want to edit.\</ahelp\> If a dialog has only one page set its \<emph\>Page (Step)\</emph\> value to \<emph\>0\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148580				0	uz	Select \<emph\>Page (Step)\</emph\> = 0 to make a control visible on every dialog page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3146144				0	uz	To switch between dialog pages at run time, you need to create a macro that changes the value of \<emph\>Page (Step)\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
