helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	hd_id6124149				0	uz	\<variable id=\"wiz_data_series\"\>\<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_data_series.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard - Data Series\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id9651478				0	uz	On this page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\> you can change the source range of all data series separately, including their labels. You can also change the range of the categories. You can first select the data range on the Data Range page and then remove unnecessary data series or add data series from other cells here.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id6326487				0	uz	If there seem to be too many options on this page, just define the data range on the Chart Wizard - Data Range page and skip this page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id686361				0	uz	This dialog is only available for charts based on a Calc or Writer table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	hd_id9241615				0	uz	Organizing data series				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id7159337				0	uz	In the Data Series list box you see a list of all data series in the current chart.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id4921720				0	uz	To organize the data series, select an entry in the list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id6627094				0	uz	Click Add to add another data series below the selected entry. The new data series has the same type as the selected entry.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id2926419				0	uz	Click Remove to remove the selected entry from the Data Series list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id4443800				0	uz	Use the Up and Down arrow buttons to move the selected entry in the list up or down. This does not change the order in the data source table, but changes only the arrangement in the chart.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	hd_id9777520				0	uz	Editing data series				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id1474654				0	uz	Click an entry in the list to view and edit the properties for that entry.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id4855189				0	uz	In the Data Ranges list box you see the role names and cell ranges of the data series components. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id9475081				0	uz	Click an entry, then edit the contents in the text box below. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id4695272				0	uz	The label next to the text box states the currently selected role. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id3931699				0	uz	Enter the range or click \<emph\>Select data range\</emph\> to minimize the dialog and select the range with the mouse.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id8626667				0	uz	If you want a data range of multiple cell areas that are not next to each other, enter the first range, then manually add a semicolon at the end of the text box, then enter the other ranges. Use a semicolon as delimiter between ranges.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id5971556				0	uz	The range for a data role, like Y-Values, must not include a label cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	hd_id7622608				0	uz	Editing categories or data labels				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id9222693				0	uz	Enter or select a cell range that will be used as text for categories or data labels. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id9500106				0	uz	Depending on the chart type, the texts are shown on the X axis or as data labels. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id5201879				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Shows a list of all data series in the chart. Click an entry to view and edit that data series. Click \<emph\>Add\</emph\> to insert a new series into the list after the selected entry.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id2571794				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Shows all the data ranges used by the data series that is selected in the Data Series list box. Each data range shows the role name and the source range address.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id2254402				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Shows the source range address from the second column of the Data Range list box. You can change the range in the text box or by dragging in the document. To minimize this dialog while you select the data range in Calc, click the \<emph\>Select data range\</emph\> button.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id2419507				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Shows the source range address of the categories (the texts you can see on the x-axis of a category chart). For an XY-chart, the text box contains the source range of the data labels which are displayed for the data points. To minimize this dialog while you select the data range in Calc, click the \<emph\>Select data range\</emph\> button.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id1091647				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Adds a new entry below the current entry in the Data Series list. If an entry is selected, the new data series gets the same chart type.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id8831446				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Removes the selected entry from the Data Series list.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id7022309				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Moves up the selected entry in the Data Series list.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_series.xhp	0	help	par_id2844019				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Moves down the selected entry in the Data Series list.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Title				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020100.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150769				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>editing; titles\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150769				0	uz	Title				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149666				0	uz	\<variable id=\"titel\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ZTitle\"\>Modifies the properties of the selected title.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149378				0	uz	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020100.xhp\" name=\"Character\"\>Character\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_pie.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Chart Type Pie 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_pie.xhp	0	help	bm_id7621997				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>donut charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pie charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>chart types;pie/donut\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_pie.xhp	0	help	hd_id3365276				0	uz	\<variable id=\"type_pie\"\>\<link href=\"text/schart/01/type_pie.xhp\"\>Chart Type Pie\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_pie.xhp	0	help	par_id245979				0	uz	On the first page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\> you can choose a chart type. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_pie.xhp	0	help	hd_id5799432				0	uz	Pie				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_pie.xhp	0	help	par_id6549272				0	uz	A pie chart shows values as circular sectors of the total circle. The length of the arc, or the area of each sector, is proportional to its value.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_pie.xhp	0	help	par_id6529740				0	uz	Pie - this subtype shows sectors as colored areas of the total pie, for one data column only. In the created chart, you can click and drag any sector to separate that sector from the remaining pie or to join it back.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_pie.xhp	0	help	par_id9121982				0	uz	Exploded pie - this subtype shows the sectors already separated from each other. In the created chart, you can click and drag any sector to move it along a radial from the pie's center.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_pie.xhp	0	help	par_id3808404				0	uz	Donut - this subtype can show multiple data columns. Each data column is shown as one donut shape with a hole inside, where the next data column can be shown. In the created chart, you can click and drag an outer sector to move it along a radial from the donut's center.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_pie.xhp	0	help	par_id2394482				0	uz	Exploded donut - this subtype shows the outer sectors already separated from the remaining donut. In the created chart, you can click and drag an outer sector to move it along a radial from the donut's center.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_net.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Chart Type Net				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_net.xhp	0	help	bm_id2193975				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>net charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>chart types;net\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>radar charts, see net charts\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_net.xhp	0	help	hd_id1990722				0	uz	\<variable id=\"type_net\"\>\<link href=\"text/schart/01/type_net.xhp\"\>Chart Type Net\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_net.xhp	0	help	par_id40589				0	uz	On the first page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\> you can choose a chart type. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_net.xhp	0	help	hd_id1391338				0	uz	Net				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_net.xhp	0	help	par_id7812433				0	uz	A Net chart displays data values as points connected by some lines, in a grid net that resembles a spider net or a radar tube display.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_net.xhp	0	help	par_id3512375				0	uz	For each row of chart data, a radial is shown on which the data is plotted. All data values are shown with the same scale, so all data values should have about the same magnitude.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040202.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Positioning				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040202.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150869				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>positioning; axes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>charts;positioning axes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>X axes;positioning\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Y axes;positioning\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>axes;interval marks\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150868				0	uz	\<link href=\"text/schart/01/05040202.xhp\" name=\"positioning\"\>Positioning\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040202.xhp	0	help	par_id3154013				0	uz	Controls the positioning of the axis.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040202.xhp	0	help	hd_id1006200801024782				0	uz	Axis line				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040202.xhp	0	help	par_id1006200801024970				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Select where to cross the other axis: at start, at end, at a specified value, or at a category.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040202.xhp	0	help	par_id1006200801024957				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the value where the axis line should cross the other axis.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040202.xhp	0	help	par_id100620080102503				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select the category where the axis line should cross the other axis.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040202.xhp	0	help	hd_id100620080102509				0	uz	Labels				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040202.xhp	0	help	hd_id1006200801523879				0	uz	Place labels				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040202.xhp	0	help	par_id1006200801523889				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Select where to place the labels: near axis, near axis (other side), outside start, or outside end.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040202.xhp	0	help	hd_id1006200801025030				0	uz	Interval marks				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149048				0	uz	Major:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040202.xhp	0	help	par_id3150397				0	uz	Specifies whether the marks are to be on the inner or outer side of the axis. It is possible to combine both: you will then see marks on both sides.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151387				0	uz	Inner				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040202.xhp	0	help	par_id3156399				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:CHECKBOX:TP_SCALE_Y:CBX_TICKS_INNER\"\>Specifies that marks are placed on the inner side of the axis.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166469				0	uz	Outer				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040202.xhp	0	help	par_id3153120				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:CHECKBOX:TP_SCALE_Y:CBX_TICKS_OUTER\"\>Specifies that marks are placed on the outer side of the axis.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159128				0	uz	Minor:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040202.xhp	0	help	par_id3146885				0	uz	This area is used to define the marking dashes between the axis marks. It is possible to activate both fields. This will result in a marking line running from the outside to the inside.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150654				0	uz	Inner				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040202.xhp	0	help	par_id3146880				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:CHECKBOX:TP_SCALE_Y:CBX_HELPTICKS_INNER\"\>Specifies that minor interval marks are placed on the inner side of the axis.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154677				0	uz	Outer				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040202.xhp	0	help	par_id3150745				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:CHECKBOX:TP_SCALE_Y:CBX_HELPTICKS_OUTER\"\>Specifies that minor interval marks are placed on the outer side of the axis.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040202.xhp	0	help	hd_id1006200801025271				0	uz	Place marks				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040202.xhp	0	help	par_id1006200801025278				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Select where to place the marks: at labels, at axis, or at axis and labels.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Options				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149400				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>aligning; 2D charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>charts; aligning\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pie charts;options\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149400				0	uz	\<link href=\"text/schart/01/04060000.xhp\" name=\"Options\"\>Options\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155067				0	uz	Use this dialog to define some options that are available for specific chart types. The contents of the Options dialog vary with the chart type.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150043				0	uz	Align data series to:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145228				0	uz	In this area you can choose between two Y axis scaling modes. The axes can only be scaled and given properties separately.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147346				0	uz	Primary Y axis				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147005				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:RADIOBUTTON:TP_OPTIONS:RBT_OPT_AXIS_1\"\>This option is active as default. All data series are aligned to the primary Y axis.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143221				0	uz	Secondary Y axis				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154656				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:RADIOBUTTON:TP_OPTIONS:RBT_OPT_AXIS_2\"\>Changes the scaling of the Y axis. This axis is only visible when at least one data series is assigned to it and the axis view is active.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166423				0	uz	Settings				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150365				0	uz	Define the settings for a bar chart in this area. Any changes apply to all data series of the chart, not to the selected data only.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145584				0	uz	Spacing				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155376				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:METRICFIELD:TP_OPTIONS:MT_GAP\"\>Defines the spacing between the columns in percent.\</ahelp\> The maximal spacing is 600%.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145384				0	uz	Overlap				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156447				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:METRICFIELD:TP_OPTIONS:MT_OVERLAP\"\>Defines the necessary settings for overlapping data series.\</ahelp\> You can choose between -100 and +100%.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153305				0	uz	Connection Lines				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148868				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:CHECKBOX:TP_OPTIONS:CB_CONNECTOR\"\>For "stacked" and "percent" column (vertical bar) charts, mark this check box to connect the column layers that belong together with lines.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id9842219				0	uz	Show bars side by side				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id9800103				0	uz	If two axes are shown in a bar chart, and some data series are attached to the first axis, while some other data series are attached to the second axis, then both sets of data series are shown independently, overlapping each other.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id2144535				0	uz	As a result, bars attached to the first y-axis are partly or completely hidden by bars attached to the second y-axis. To avoid this, enable the option to display bars side by side. \<ahelp hid=\".\"\>The bars from different data series are shown as if they were attached only to one axis.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id24414				0	uz	Clockwise direction				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id2527237				0	uz	Available for pie and donut charts. \<ahelp hid=\".\"\>The default direction in which the pieces of a pie chart are ordered is counterclockwise. Enable the \<emph\>Clockwise direction\</emph\> checkbox to draw the pieces in opposite direction.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id401013				0	uz	Starting angle				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id761131				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Drag the small dot along the circle or click any position on the circle to set the starting angle of a pie or donut chart. The starting angle is the mathematical angle position where the first piece is drawn. The value of 90 degrees draws the first piece at the 12 o'clock position. A value of 0 degrees starts at the 3 o'clock position.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id553910				0	uz	In 3D pie and donut charts that were created with older versions of the software, the starting angle is 0 degrees instead of 90 degrees. For old and new 2D charts the default starting angle is 90 degrees.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id1414838				0	uz	When you change the starting angle or the direction, only current versions of the software show the changed values. Older versions of the software display the same document using the default values: Always counterclockwise direction and a starting value of 90 degrees (2D pie charts) or 0 degrees (3D pie charts).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3179723				0	uz	Degrees				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id2164067				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Enter the starting angle between 0 and 359 degrees. You can also click the arrows to change the displayed value.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Chart Type Column and Line 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	bm_id5976744				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>column and line charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>chart types;column and line\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>combination charts\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id8596453				0	uz	\<variable id=\"type_column_line\"\>\<link href=\"text/schart/01/type_column_line.xhp\"\>Chart Type Column and Line\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id4818567				0	uz	On the first page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\> you can choose a chart type. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id2451551				0	uz	Column and Line				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3101901				0	uz	A Column and Line chart is a combination of a \<link href=\"text/schart/01/type_column_bar.xhp\"\>Column chart\</link\> with a \<link href=\"text/schart/01/type_line.xhp\"\>Line chart\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id7910397				0	uz	Select one of the variants				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id5244300				0	uz	Columns and Lines. The rectangles of the column data series are drawn side by side so that you can easily compare their values.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id7163609				0	uz	Stacked Columns and Lines. The rectangles of the column data series are drawn stacked above each other, so that the height of a column visualizes the sum of the data values.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id1842097				0	uz	You can insert a second y-axis with \<link href=\"text/schart/01/04040000.xhp\"\>Insert - Axes\</link\> after you finish the wizard.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id8297677				0	uz	To specify a data range				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id8871120				0	uz	The leftmost columns (or the top rows) of the selected data range provide the data that are shown as Columns objects. The other columns or rows of the data range provide the data for the Lines objects. You can change this assignment in the \<emph\>Data Series\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id2952055				0	uz	Select the data range.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id594500				0	uz	Click one of the options for data series in rows or in columns.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id1944944				0	uz	Check whether the data range has labels in the first row or in the first column or both.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id6667683				0	uz	Organizing data series				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id7616809				0	uz	In the Data Series list box you see a list of all data series in the current chart.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id9770195				0	uz	The column data series are positioned at the top of the list, the line data series at the bottom of the list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id1446272				0	uz	To organize the data series, select an entry in the list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3779717				0	uz	Click Add to add another data series below the selected entry. The new data series has the same type as the selected entry.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id5056611				0	uz	Click Remove to remove the selected entry from the Data Series list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id7786492				0	uz	Use the Up and Down arrow buttons to move the selected entry in the list up or down. This way you can convert a Column data series to a List data series and back. This does not change the order in the data source table, but changes only the arrangement in the chart.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id265816				0	uz	Editing data series				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id6768700				0	uz	Click an entry in the list to view and edit the properties for that entry.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id1924497				0	uz	In the Data Ranges list box you see the role names and cell ranges of the data series components. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id5081942				0	uz	Click an entry, then edit the contents in the text box below. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id2958464				0	uz	The label next to the text box states the currently selected role. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id883816				0	uz	Enter the range or click \<emph\>Select data range\</emph\> to minimize the dialog and select the range with the mouse.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id5091708				0	uz	The range for a data role, like Y-Values, must not include a label cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id974456				0	uz	Editing categories or data labels				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id2767113				0	uz	Enter or select a cell range that will be used as text for categories or data labels. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id301828				0	uz	The values in the Categories range will be shown as labels on the x axis.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id8996246				0	uz	Inserting chart elements				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id5729544				0	uz	Use the Chart Elements page of the Chart Wizard to insert any of the following elements:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id2932828				0	uz	Chart titles				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id9449446				0	uz	Legend				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id8122196				0	uz	Visible grid lines				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id9909665				0	uz	For additional elements use the Insert menu of the chart in edit mode. There you can define the following elements:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id9141819				0	uz	Secondary axes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id6354869				0	uz	Minor grids				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id2685323				0	uz	Data labels				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id6042664				0	uz	Statistics, for example mean values, y error bars and trend lines				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id7889950				0	uz	To set different data labels for each data series, use the properties dialog of the data series.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
