helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	par_id3147436	75			0	uz	\<variable id=\"sytextbeschr\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ToggleAxisDescr\"\>The\<emph\> AxesTitle On/Off \</emph\>icon on the \<emph\>Formatting\</emph\> bar switches the labeling of all axes on or off.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150717				0	uz	Rotate text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	par_id3154510				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ToggleAxisDescr\"\>Defines the text direction of cell contents.\</ahelp\> Click one of the ABCD buttons to assign the required direction.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150327				0	uz	ABCD wheel				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	par_id3149018				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SCH_ALIGNMENT_CTR_DIAL\"\>Clicking anywhere on the wheel defines the variable text orientation.\</ahelp\> The letters "ABCD" on the button correspond to the new setting.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154254				0	uz	ABCD button				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	par_id3154702				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SCH_ALIGNMENT_STACKED\"\>Assigns vertical text orientation for cell contents.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	par_id3150342				0	uz	If you define a vertical x-axis label, the text may be cut off by the line of the x-axis.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166432				0	uz	Degrees				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	par_id3150199				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SCH_ALIGNMENT_DEGREES\"\>Allows you to manually enter the orientation angle.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152985				0	uz	Text flow				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	par_id3155089				0	uz	Determines the text flow of the data label.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148837				0	uz	Overlap				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	par_id3151240				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:CHECKBOX:TP_AXIS_LABEL:CB_AXIS_LABEL_TEXTOVERLAP\"\>Specifies that the text in cells may overlap other cells.\</ahelp\> This can be especially useful if there is a lack of space. This option is not available with different title directions.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157982				0	uz	Break				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	par_id3155268				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:CHECKBOX:TP_AXIS_LABEL:CB_AXIS_LABEL_TEXTBREAK\"\>Allows a text break.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159205				0	uz	The following options are not available for all chart types:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152872				0	uz	Tartib				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	par_id3159230				0	uz	The options on this tab are only available for a 2D chart, under \<emph\>Format - Axis - Y Axis\</emph\> or \<emph\>X Axis\</emph\>. In this area, you can define the alignment of the number labels on the X or Y axis.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146963				0	uz	Tile				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	par_id3155758				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:RADIOBUTTON:TP_AXIS_LABEL:RB_AXIS_LABEL_SIDEBYSIDE\"\>Arranges numbers on the axis side by side.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151195				0	uz	Stagger odd				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	par_id3145114				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:RADIOBUTTON:TP_AXIS_LABEL:RB_AXIS_LABEL_UPDOWN\"\>Staggers numbers on the axis, even numbers lower than odd numbers.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147250				0	uz	Stagger even				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153958				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:RADIOBUTTON:TP_AXIS_LABEL:RB_AXIS_LABEL_DOWNUP\"\>Stagger numbers on the axes, odd numbers lower than even numbers.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147301				0	uz	Automatic				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	par_id3147404				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:RADIOBUTTON:TP_AXIS_LABEL:RB_AXIS_LABEL_AUTOORDER\"\>Automatically arranges numbers on the axis.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	par_id3149353				0	uz	Problems may arise in displaying labels if the size of your chart is too small. You can avoid this by either enlarging the view or decreasing the font size.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	hd_id1106200812235146				0	uz	Text Direction				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	par_id1106200812235271				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Specify the text direction for a paragraph that uses complex text layout (CTL). This feature is only available if complex text layout support is enabled.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Chart Type XY				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	bm_id84231				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>scatter charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>XY charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>chart types;XY (scatter)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>error indicators in charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>error bars in charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>averages in charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>statistics in charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>variances in charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>standard deviation in charts\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	hd_id9346598				0	uz	\<variable id=\"type_xy\"\>\<link href=\"text/schart/01/type_xy.xhp\"\>Chart Type XY (Scatter)\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id2003845				0	uz	On the first page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\> you can choose a chart type. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	hd_id7757194				0	uz	XY (Scatter)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id5977965				0	uz	An XY chart in its basic form is based on one data series consisting of a name, a list of x‑values, and a list of y‑values. Each value pair (x|y) is shown as a point in a coordinate system. The name of the data series is associated with the y‑values and shown in the legend.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id4381847				0	uz	Choose an XY chart for the following example tasks:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id1336710				0	uz	scale the x‑axis				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id1221655				0	uz	generate a parameter curve, for example a spiral				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id3397320				0	uz	draw the graph of a function				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id7657399				0	uz	explore the statistical association of quantitative variables				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id8925138				0	uz	Your XY chart may have more than one data series.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	hd_id5461897				0	uz	XY Chart Variants				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id8919339				0	uz	You can choose an XY chart variant on the first page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\>, or by choosing \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Chart Type \</item\>for a chart in edit mode.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id4634235				0	uz	The chart is created with default settings. After the chart is finished, you can edit its properties to change the appearance. Line styles and icons can be changed on the \<emph\>Line\</emph\>tab page of the data series properties dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id5482039				0	uz	Double-click any data point to open the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data Series\</item\> dialog. In this dialog, you can change many properties of the data series.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id0805200810492449				0	uz	For 2D charts, you can choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Y Error Bars\</item\> to enable the display of error bars.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id6221198				0	uz	You can enable the display of mean value lines and trend lines using commands on the Insert menu.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	hd_id1393475				0	uz	Points only				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	hd_id5376140				0	uz	Lines Only				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id4408093				0	uz	This variant draws straight lines from one data point to the next. The data points are not shown by icons. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id7261268				0	uz	The drawing order is the same as the order in the data series. Mark \<emph\>Sort by X Values\</emph\> to draw the lines in the order of the x values. This sorting applies only to the chart, not to the data in the table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	hd_id6949369				0	uz	Points and Lines				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id9611499				0	uz	This variant shows points and lines at the same time.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	hd_id6765953				0	uz	3D Lines				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id7422711				0	uz	The lines are shown like tapes. The data points are not shown by icons. In the finished chart choose \<link href=\"text/schart/01/three_d_view.xhp\"\>3D View\</link\> to set properties like illumination and angle of view.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	hd_id239265				0	uz	Smooth Lines				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id7957396				0	uz	Mark \<emph\>Smooth Lines\</emph\> to draw curves instead of straight line segments.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id1202124				0	uz	Click \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> to set details for the curves.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id5989562				0	uz	\<emph\>Cubic Spline\</emph\> interpolates your data points with polynomials of degree 3. The transitions between the polynomial pieces are smooth, having the same slope and curvature. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id6128421				0	uz	The \<emph\>Resolution\</emph\> determines how many line segments are calculated to draw a piece of polynomial between two data points. You can see the intermediate points if you click any data point.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id9280373				0	uz	\<emph\>B-Spline\</emph\> uses the data points as control points to form a B-spline curve. Those curves are built piecewise from polynomials. The \<emph\>Data points order\</emph\> sets the degree k of these polynomials. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Axes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040100.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153768				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>axes;formatting\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153768				0	uz	Axes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154319				0	uz	\<variable id=\"achsen\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:DiagramAxisAll\"\>Opens a dialog, where you can edit the properties of the selected axis.\</ahelp\>\</variable\> The name of the dialog depends on the selected axis.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149667				0	uz	The \<link href=\"text/schart/01/05040200.xhp\" name=\"Y axis\"\>Y axis\</link\> has an enhanced dialog. For X-Y charts, the X axis chart is also enhanced by the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/05040201.xhp\" name=\"Scaling\"\>\<emph\>Scaling\</emph\>\</link\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040100.xhp	0	help	par_id3159266				0	uz	Scaling the X axis is only possible in the X-Y chart type.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145230				0	uz	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020100.xhp\" name=\"Character\"\>Character\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05010200.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Data Series				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05010200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150449				0	uz	\<link href=\"text/schart/01/05010200.xhp\" name=\"Data Series\"\>Data Series\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05010200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145750				0	uz	Use this to change the properties of a selected data series. This dialog appears when one data series is selected when you choose \<emph\>Format - Object Properties\</emph\>. Some of the menu entries are only available for 2D or 3D charts.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05010200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154015				0	uz	Any changes made here affect the entire data series. For example, if you change the color, all elements belonging to this data series will change color.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05010200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146916				0	uz	\<link href=\"text/schart/01/04050000.xhp\" name=\"Y Error Bars\"\>Y Error Bars\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Chart Wizard - Data Range				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	bm_id2429578				0	uz	\<bookmark_value\>data ranges in charts\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	hd_id8313852				0	uz	\<variable id=\"wiz_data_range\"\>\<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_data_range.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard - Data Range\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id8829309				0	uz	On this page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\> you can select one single source of data range. This range may consist of more than one rectangular range of cells.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id6401867				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Opens the Data Ranges dialog where you can edit Data Range and Data Series.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id2025818				0	uz	Use the Chart Wizard - Data Series page if you need more control over the data ranges.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id8466139				0	uz	This dialog is only available for charts based on a Calc or Writer table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	hd_id1877193				0	uz	To specify a data range				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id5924863				0	uz	Select the data range. Do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id4357432				0	uz	Enter the data range in the text box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id5626392				0	uz	In Calc, an example data range would be "$Sheet1.$B$3:$B$14". Note that a data range may consist of more than one region in a spreadsheet, e.g. "$Sheet1.A1:A5;$Sheet1.D1:D5" is also a valid data range. In Writer, an example data range would be "Table1.A1:E4".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id6823938				0	uz	If you want a data range of multiple cell areas that are not next to each other, enter the first range, then manually add a semicolon at the end of the text box, then enter the other ranges. Use a semicolon as delimiter between ranges.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id1434369				0	uz	Click one of the options for data series in rows or in columns.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id7524033				0	uz	Check whether the data range has labels in the first row or in the first column or both.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id5256508				0	uz	In the preview you can see how the final chart will look.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id379650				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the data range that you want to include in your chart. To minimize this dialog while you select the data range in Calc, click the \<emph\>Select data range\</emph\> button.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id953703				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Data series get their data from consecutive rows in the selected range. For scatter charts, the first data series will contain x-values for all series. All other data series are used as y-values, one for each series.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id4496597				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Data series get their data from consecutive columns in the selected range. For scatter charts, the first data column will contain x-values for all series. All other data columns are used as y-values, one for each series.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id2898953				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>For data series in columns: The first row in the range is used as names for data series. For data series in rows: The first row in the range is used as categories. The remaining rows comprise the data series. If this check box is not selected, all rows are data series.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id7546311				0	uz	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>For data series in columns: The first column in the range is used as names for data series. For data series in rows: The first column in the range is used as categories. The remaining columns comprise the data columns. If this check box is not selected, all columns are data columns.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	uz	Axis				2002-02-02 02:02:02
